{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen","id":1478313,"title":"Warning: Grumpy Post. The Fenrir have Fallen.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-04-08T18:24:40-07:00","id":1478313,"title":"Warning: Grumpy Post. The Fenrir have Fallen.","content":"Confirmed by one of the spokespeople for the Werewolf: Retaliation boardgame that they are following the W5 setting bible and that the Fenrir are now a Fallen Tribe.<br /> <br /> *Begins punching random objects in the shed*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-08T19:05:02-07:00","id":1478315,"title":"","content":"Are you sure? <br /> <br /> If so, that sucks, but it just strengthens my already significant misgivings about W5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-08T20:26:33-07:00","id":1478319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478315#post1478315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you sure?<br /> <br /> If so, that sucks, but it just strengthens my already significant misgivings about W5.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, its not word from Achilli. But it is from a production partner following his directives......so...semi-sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-08T20:39:23-07:00","id":1478320,"title":"","content":"We've known of of the Tribes was going to &quot;fall&quot; for awhile now. None of them would have made me happy exactly, but the Fenrir is probably the least interesting option, and the option that has the least potential positive impact on the game. It's basically the &quot;safe&quot; pick that will definitely piss some people off, and I can't see it actually making anyone happy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-08T20:41:00-07:00","id":1478321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478319#post1478319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, its not word from Achilli. But it is from a production partner following his directives......so...semi-sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if that\u2019s the way it is, I\u2019ll likely stay away from W5 as a matter of principle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-08T23:28:47-07:00","id":1478327,"title":"","content":"Having it be one of the tribes that can best reflect the growth of ultra-right politics in Europe makes it a good commentary on the times in which it's being published. I don't mind.<br /> <br /> It does make for a funny commentary on the game's setting, though, that when the word first broke that one of the tribes was going to fall, enough of the tribes are sketchy that players were able to honestly wonder for a while which one it was going to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-08T23:44:05-07:00","id":1478330,"title":"","content":"How does the Tribe with actual form on rooting out and utterly destroying the ultra-right element in their tribe decades ago reflect the growth? Surely the eugenics of certain Silver Fang houses or the prevalent anti-Crinos-Born rhetoric of the Fianna would be more fitting than those who actually stood up and punched the fuck out of the Nazi even if he was their cousin, uncle or brother.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T00:05:55-07:00","id":1478333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478330#post1478330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does the Tribe with actual form on rooting out and utterly destroying the ultra-right element in their tribe decades ago reflect the growth? Surely the eugenics of certain Silver Fang houses or the prevalent anti-Crinos-Born rhetoric of the Fianna would be more fitting than those who actually stood up and punched the fuck out of the Nazi even if he was their cousin, uncle or brother.</div> </div> </div> </div>i have mixed feelings because on one hand you\u2019re right, they did try and make that a plot point to try and salvage the Tribe for Revised edition. On the other hand, when the Tribe had been written since 1e with that as their thematic heart (to the point of intentionally using a swastika as their Tribal Glyph) I can appreciate the \u201ctoo little too late, these guys aren\u2019t salvageable\u201d.<br /> <br /> Of course this kind of heighlights my sentiment that fixing WtA can\u2019t be done via metaplot on the existing foundation. You need a full reboot<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T00:29:49-07:00","id":1478335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478327#post1478327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having it be one of the tribes that can best reflect the growth of ultra-right politics in Europe makes it a good commentary on the times in which it's being published.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beyond the point made that this commentary means undoing the work in previous editions to purge the Fenrir of their ultra-right faction(s), it's also too on the nose for my tastes.<br /> <br /> If you really want to make this commentary in WtA? The Children of Gaia should fall. The Fenrir falling is just saying, &quot;the Tribe with the strongest thematic ties to European far right-wing populist politics turns out to have lots of bad elements in them, so we're making them worse.&quot; The Coggies falling is an actual metaphor for the failures of liberal humanism to adapt to the post-Cold War world, and how that's left the opening for seemingly defeated social ills to roar back into politics. &quot;Hey ultra-right nutjobs exist!&quot; is only scary in the fact that it's true, and it's always been true. What's scary is the idea that we can't trust all the institutions that we built up to ensure society marches towards progress despite that truth because they're failing us. And that's exactly what the fall of the Coggies would be: the voices of moderation, unity, and equality within a society falling into corruption and their own brand of evil.<br /> <br /> While perhaps a risk of being to edgy, the Coggies falling is an actual shake up to the Garou Nation. It's a blow they're not ready for, and has years of both book and play implications to explore, that touches directly on the pulse of lots of very real global issues as the institutions of the post-WWII and post-Cold War international order continue to show the cracks in their effectiveness and value. What happens if the Garou equivalent of the UN falls apart is a much more important commentary (if you make a good commentary out of it of course) than the commentary of the equivalent of Orban retaking PM in Hungary and leading the country in a regressive direction after people thought they got rid of him in '02..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It does make for a funny commentary on the game's setting, though, that when the word first broke that one of the tribes was going to fall, enough of the tribes are sketchy that players were able to honestly wonder for a while which one it was going to be. </div> </div> </div>The game's been trying to add this sort of complexity into the Tribes since 2e. There's a reason why Rev. included an idea of what the fall of each of the Tribes would look like; none of them are supposed to be immune from this potential fate.<br /> <br /> When we have a book that's detailed that, the idea that fans had lots of theories about which Tribe it might be was likely more of a reflection of which Tribes that fans wanted to see go, and what the fans think Paradox's creative team is up to.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T01:07:11-07:00","id":1478337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478315#post1478315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If so, that sucks, but it just strengthens my already significant misgivings about W5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's how I feel...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T01:52:22-07:00","id":1478338,"title":"","content":"Getting rid of any of the tribes is an error in my opinion. Getting rid of the get because dumb skinhead trash wants to play one, assuming that's the reason is genuinely baffling. <br /> <br /> Im surprised I have to comment on this but the 'solution'is to not let a Nazi into your games not burn down the game to spite them. I'm not going to want one in my game even if hypothetical skinhead plays a loverly friendly hippy child of gaia or were playing thirsty sword lesbians....because its a bloody nazi.<br /> <br /> I mean on a practical level gets one of the tribes were the fact you're genrally a middle class white dude writting other people's folklore isn't an issue so anything get should be one of ones they're keen to keep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 04-09-2022, 04:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T01:56:53-07:00","id":1478340,"title":"","content":"Dang. For my group, that is probably the worst choice. Our one hard-core Werewolf fan is also a massive Get of Fenris fan. In fact, I don't think I can recall him ever playing a non-Get character. So, no chance of my group playing this now. Any other tribe would have worked better. Oh well.<br /> <br /> Personally, I was really going it hoping it would be the Glasswalkers falling to the Weaver, since that would make a more interesting dynamic than having another tribe shack up with the Wyrn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T02:13:18-07:00","id":1478343,"title":"","content":"Also confirmed that the Stargazers are out as well. But as the departure of a large section of the Tribe was a plotpoint in Revised its probably not as much of a surprise.<br /> <br /> Achilli did state only 11 playable tribes in W5......so I guess they can't use the ' just like 1st Ed' excuse they used for V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T04:05:02-07:00","id":1478344,"title":"","content":"Ultimately, the 13 Tribes are a really bad setup. There's a drastic divide between ones highly tied to specific cultures, and ones with more wide-spread if not global appeal by attaching to concepts that crop up in all human (or canine in one case) communities. The Tribes as they stand are anti-Golidlocks: they're in the middle when there should be either less of them mechanically (but expand the role of Camps/etc. to create local variations) or more of them so you can get a better spread of cultural ties and not try to have most of them be any sort of global.<br /> <br /> Except (and this is a bit except) for continuing the lore as already established, you'd lose nothing from the game if the White Howlers, Fianna, and Fenrir were just different groups within one larger northern European Tribe. The tragedy of the fall of the Howlers would remain the same, its impact of the Fianna would probably be more justified as Tribemates instead of being territorial rivals, and so on.<br /> <br /> But, this is a continuation, not a reboot. It's not the time to try to fix these elements. The fans losing access to playing two Tribes needs some serious payoff that I at least can't imagine what it would be. Even as someone that thinks WtA has the wrong number of Tribes, I don't see what losing two is supposed to do for the game; there's a reason why a lot of people felt sidelining the Stargazers (who were brought back anyway) wasn't a good choice. The Stargazers getting re-axed is also not a good look when Paradox is indicating they have no intention of revisiting the KotE in V5. Getting rid of the south-east Asian vampire variants, and the only south-east Asian specific Tribe of Garou, at best, is a huge red flag that they can't attract creators that know the cultures well enough to actually do a decent job instead of rehashing the issues the oWW had. <br /> <br /> &quot;We have to trim down the Tribes, but only via metaplot,&quot; feels like such a corporate executive directive and not an organic creative decision, it can't help but taint preconceptions about what's going to happen with W5.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T05:03:40-07:00","id":1478345,"title":"","content":"Why the fuck did they go with the decision if this is true? Do these writers seriously take the &quot;All Get are Nazis&quot; at face value muttered by some fans who have no clue about their lore when in revised, most of the tribe literally slaughtered the Nazi elements?<br /> <br /> I may not be European nor of Norse descent, but if they simply made the Get fall to make a &quot;commentary against the far right in Europe&quot; this is the worst decision they could ever make.<br /> <br /> Instead of making them stray away from Nazi shit, they somehow made it worse despite an easy solution to this.<br /> <br /> I genuinely fear what they will do to the Stargazers and the Beast Courts to some extent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25313-raziel","name":"Raziel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T05:51:09-07:00","id":1478347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raziel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478345#post1478345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why the fuck did they go with the decision if this is true? Do these writers seriously take the &quot;All Get are Nazis&quot; at face value muttered by some fans who have no clue about their lore when in revised, most of the tribe literally slaughtered the Nazi elements?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is, perhaps a bit overstated. The Swords of Heimdall were purged, but that doesn't actually make the Get free of the taint of fascist ideologies in their ranks. The Swords were extremists, who took their methods to the point where the rest of the Fenrir couldn't tolerate them any more. The problem with extremists and zealots is that they tend to reflect a certain amount of insidious belief within a larger community. The real Nazis didn't just spring up out of nowhere, and didn't just sway the German people into following them with a spectacle of new ideas. Nazism is an extremist concentration of a number of beliefs that are already present in European societies taken to its violent conclusions. The Swords were part of the Fenrir for so long because a lot of their beliefs overlap with mainstream Fenrir philosophy even if most Fenrir would never take it that far. Similarly, a Red Talon that kills human children as frequently as possible is an extremist, but to an extent they're doing something lots of Red Talons kind of wish they were free to do, but refuse such extremism. <br /> <br /> The Swords could only grow in fertile soil, and that soil hasn't changed just because the Swords have been rooted out from it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I may not be European nor of Norse descent, but if they simply made the Get fall to make a &quot;commentary against the far right in Europe&quot; this is the worst decision they could ever make. </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, this is actually rather untrue. If you were told you had to cut a Tribe from WtA, the choices are fraught with potential backlash (esp. with the position the nWW put Paradox in with some of the early V5 books). Everything bad about cutting the Fenrir would only be compounded with justified outrage over representational issues if you picked the Black Furies, Silent Striders, either of the North American Tribes, the Bone Gnawers, etc. One of the reasons I had the Red Talons as my top guess for the &quot;fallen&quot; Tribe was because they have the least issue with people feeling like the characters that represent them are being taken out of the game.<br /> <br /> Cutting any Tribe is going to have fan backlash. A Scandinavian company cutting the Scandinavian Tribe caries a smaller risk of that negative backlash spreading beyond fans attached to their favorite Tribes.<br /> <br /> Once the already bad decision of axing two Tribes was made, the Fenrir easily jumped into the top 3 of the least bad options with the Red Talons and Shadow Lords as far as the &quot;fallen&quot; one of the two goes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I genuinely fear what they will do to the Stargazers and the Beast Courts to some extent. </div> </div> </div>My current bar on this is set to, &quot;hopefully just never talk about them every again.&quot; But that's a lot easier for them to do with the KotE than it is for the SGs and Beast Courts.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T06:08:58-07:00","id":1478350,"title":"","content":"Not surprising, since W5 seems to take every possible step to maximize pointless and depressing grimderp. I keep wondering what the point is in playing such a glumly metaplot, since the Garou may as well all just kill themselves and it wouldn't change anything.<br /> <br /> The narrative and representational problems of the game aren't going to be solved by designating the Get as &quot;Nazi Tribe&quot; and making them into pure villains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25545-jollycooperative","name":"jollycooperative","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T07:21:07-07:00","id":1478356,"title":"","content":"I think the problem was, that the Get got the connection to the real life Nazi Germany in 1st Edition. For the Get of Fenris ideology is a form of Elitism that is also found in other tribes and that as a game element is something that can and should be part of the game world.<br /> <br /> And sure, there might be some reasons to rationalize changing this and that in the Setting, but there will always be different views if it was really necessary or a good choice. For now, I can't see that the cutting of the tribes will highten the appeal for players who played the game a long time...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T08:19:05-07:00","id":1478362,"title":"","content":"Well, obviously the Get of Fenris were designed to represent certain far right ideas, or at least caricatures of what the original authors though were far right ideas. The Tribe symbol is like a Swastika. Now, to say that they are fascists is an oversimplification of both the Get and fascism, but the connection is there.<br /> <br /> But, and get ready for it, so what? All of the Tribes have stereotypes as a part of their theme and just about all of them believe in extreme and potentially harmful ideas. The Black Furies have a history of murdering their own male infants and many still hate men. The Red Talons mostly want to exterminate humanity. The Wendigo hate whitey. The Fianna are drunken Irish hooligans. I could go on. <br /> <br /> All of the Tribes have these crazy quirks and character flaws and, while they could be improved, that is part of the fun. In fact, from the inception of White Wolf, it was intended to be mature games with moral complexity and shades of gray. You play a werewolf character not because you agree with your werewolf character, but because you are getting into the mindset of something very different from yourself. Werewolves are a bunch of crazy assholes, but they are crazy assholes trying to save the world.<br /> <br /> The current developers are leftists. Of course, White Wolf writers have always been mostly leftists, but there has been a change of attitude in this edition. Instead of being subversive and controversial, I get the feeling like the current developers don\u2019t want anything that might offend their sensibilities. So no right wing werewolves, even if they are mostly not Nazis. The only extremist werewolves are the ones with an extreme ideology that they agree with. This, I believe, is the opposite of how WoD games were intended to be where players were encouraged to play characters different from themselves, to see things from a different perspective. It\u2019s gone from a mature game to an immature game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T09:26:51-07:00","id":1478374,"title":"","content":"Very disappointing. Get was one of my favorite tribes along with Fianna. Really would I have preferred no tribe falling or leaving but if I had to choose I would expect Shadow Lords to fall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T09:30:47-07:00","id":1478377,"title":"","content":"So how much does this discourage everyone from buying w5? I've got a w20 book which let's me play get, metis and mystery tribe so unless they've got some really good combat mechanics I fail to see the appeal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T09:37:42-07:00","id":1478380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478377#post1478377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So how much does this discourage everyone from buying w5? I've got a w20 book which let's me play get, metis and mystery tribe so unless they've got some really good combat mechanics I fail to see the appeal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn\u2019t sure about whether or not to buy W5, but now I\u2019m nearly certain that I won\u2019t buy it. Unless I learn that there are other things in there that I really love I won\u2019t get it.<br /> <br /> W20 is probably better suited for me and my interests anyway, since it\u2019s open ended and metaplot neutral. I can use that and make the GoF (along with the other factions) how I would like them to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T09:41:32-07:00","id":1478381,"title":"","content":"first they get rid of the garou nation then the metis and now this, what next they axe off gaia oh wait they already did that my mistake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27369-the-smiling-gun-knight","name":"The smiling gun-knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T12:09:35-07:00","id":1478401,"title":"","content":"I see 5E is continuing it's trend of bizarre and questionable decisions that seem to do nothing but annoy and frustrate longtime fans. While I'm not a big WtA, this has me continuing to fear for M5 and the Technocracy because it would be so easy for them to turn the Technocracy into Alt-Right White Fascists with the depth of a sheet of paper that make their early 1E version look good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T12:34:26-07:00","id":1478406,"title":"","content":"Setting here as a Scandinavian being annoyed.<br /> <br /> First, the Get was the racist, even Nazi, Tribe.<br /> <br /> Then they realized the problem with that.<br /> <br /> Now it might be the fallen tribe.<br /> <br /> Why, thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance Writer and Storyteller's Vault contributor. Find my work here: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/index.php?affiliate_id=17903\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.storytellersvault.com/ind...liate_id=17903</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1535-jackob","name":"Jackob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1535_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T13:28:32-07:00","id":1478417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jackob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478406#post1478406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Setting here as a Scandinavian being annoyed.<br /> <br /> First, the Get was the racist, even Nazi, Tribe.<br /> <br /> Then they realized the problem with that.<br /> <br /> Now it might be the fallen tribe.<br /> <br /> Why, thank you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah... that is one of the unfortunate parts of the Get being the Fallen Tribe. Then again the same could be said for most of the Tribes. Pretty much every one but the Bone Gnawers, Glass Walkers and Red Talons would have that problem.<br /> <br /> Truthfully when I first heard about the Fallen Tribe, I could only see it being one of two Tribes, the Get and the Talons. The Get because of their racism and Fascist ties in the past and the Talons because they were a bunch of angry Wolf-born that were the least human of the Tribes because of that. And of the two, I was hoping it would have been the Talons.<br /> <br /> But frankly like I said, with the questionable direction the 5E in general has been going, I should have known it would be the Get.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T15:09:58-07:00","id":1478431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jollycooperative</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478350#post1478350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The narrative and representational problems of the game aren't going to be solved by designating the Get as &quot;Nazi Tribe&quot; and making them into pure villains.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but it's certainly corporate style thinking of, &quot;how to we change the PR problem we had because people felt V5 was to sympathetic to Nazis besides denounce Nazism publicly?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478377#post1478377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So how much does this discourage everyone from buying w5?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was never going to pay money for W5. My current stance on the WoD 5e non-VtM books is that I'd take a free PDF if I was offered a legal copy of one so I could at least read it for myself and see if I found anything worth my time in it. V5 I only read other people's copies of so I can have an informed opinion on things. W5 has been moved to the V5 category now. So, I'm not even taking a free copy if I'm offered one. I'll just wait to see if I know someone who buys it/takes a legal free copy and then ask them to let me read it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T16:07:09-07:00","id":1478439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478362#post1478362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The current developers are leftists. Of course, White Wolf writers have always been mostly leftists, but there has been a change of attitude in this edition. Instead of being subversive and controversial, I get the feeling like the current developers don\u2019t want anything that might offend their sensibilities..</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> You're no longer supposed to play anyone who's wrong about anything. It used to be that there was something of the mindset that produced shows like &quot;All In the Family&quot;, &quot;Family Guy&quot;, &quot;American Dad&quot;, and &quot;Seinfeld&quot; where the protagonists were terrible people, but very entertaining to watch. At some point that changed to protagonists needing to be right about everything. Where did the idea of a deeply flawed protagonist go?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T16:58:41-07:00","id":1478443,"title":"","content":"Except, of course, that's 100% false.<br /> <br /> 1) One of those shows is still being made today, and another was cancelled last year after <b>twenty</b> seasons and years of slumping ratings over all metrics as later seasons failed to keep people interested.<br /> 2) One is made by a guy that continues to make shows about horrible people (Curb Your Enthusiasm is still going).<br /> 3) There are countless other examples out there: Rick and Morty, Bojack Horseman, Breaking Bad/Better Call Saul, Yellowstone, Ozark, Mad Men, Tiger King and the whole slew of true crime documentaries that have flooded streaming and podcasts, Veep... I could probably keep going for a long time here.<br /> <br /> The idea of deeply flawed protagonists hasn't gone anywhere. The problem was the late 90s/early 00s completely overplayed it. Millenials and Zoomers repeatedly poll that they're overwhelmed by the negativity in the real world, and want more affirming entertainment rather than entertainment that wallows in how banal and flawed the world is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 04-09-2022, 08:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T17:17:45-07:00","id":1478446,"title":"","content":"I don't think there are many doubts left at this point, W5 will get the same treatment as V5, they are going to axe whatever they think is not ok with current American political sensibilities and move on, not much to be done about it aside from biting the bullet and buy it for what it is or just stick with W20 stuff. All the V5 stuff I have are gifts and I don't plan of ever dropping a single euro on any of the future WoD stuff, I will stick with CoD and hope that Paradox doesn't decide to kill it at this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T17:24:29-07:00","id":1478447,"title":"","content":"I don't have any huge interest in WtA to be honest, but the turn the recent discourse took grabbed at me and I want to second some being baffled at the idea that the deeply flawed protagonist has gone anywhere. Peaky Blinders alone had a just finished pretty triumphant six season run that is getting a full out follow up movie, just to add onto Heavy Arms' list (and also because, y'know, I like excuses to mention that show. It's good stuff). Raised by Wolves is a tale up and down the stretch of it of often outright intentionally horrifying people/entities as the protagonists if you want a genre material example. Dexter of all things just came back for a season to redo the way it ended. Snowfall and Mayans are rolling along as from the perspective of the criminals crime dramas. Snowpiercer goes pretty grey pretty often. Even Foundation spends as much time with the Emperors as its outright protagonists as any other character (which, if you were into the novels, is honestly kind of exasperating for what you might have been expecting the show to do instead, but the example stands all the same). The list goes on.<br /> <br /> Deeply flawed protagonist stories are everywhere. Media is drowning in them. They're still heavily popular and acclaimed. Throw a rock and hit one. <br /> <br /> Honestly if anything we are still pretty much in that early 00s era overplay. It never went away. The only real difference is other stories are also being told with some amount of prominence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T17:32:29-07:00","id":1478449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The smiling gun-knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478381#post1478381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">first they get rid of the garou nation then the metis and now this, what next they axe off gaia oh wait they already did that my mistake.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If the Nation is gone, why do we still have Silver Fangs? Heck, we could get rid of the Lords as well, though admittedly they could be planning to create a Garou Nation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T17:51:08-07:00","id":1478450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Technoma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478374#post1478374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very disappointing. Get was one of my favorite tribes along with Fianna. Really would I have preferred no tribe falling or leaving but if I had to choose I would expect Shadow Lords to fall.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the one choice that'd be even less surprising/interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T18:35:06-07:00","id":1478455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478449#post1478449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If the Nation is gone, why do we still have Silver Fangs? Heck, we could get rid of the Lords as well, though admittedly they could be planning to create a Garou Nation.</div> </div> </div> </div>We don't really know a lot of details around some of these topics. Like, we have no idea of the Fenrir are going to join the Black Spirals, or if they're going to become a second Wyrm Tribe (or third if you want to count the Skindancers). We know the Garou Nation is going to fracture due to the metaplot, but we have no idea if that's going to just mean a different take on them like the Camarilla has changed in V5, or if it really is going to cease to exist as a functional entity.<br /> <br /> So, while I'm by no means optimistic about thing, do take some of the pessimism with a grain of salt. There's a lot of speculation and extrapolation going on in many of the concerns voiced - including my own - that may or may not end up turn in the final product.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T18:37:50-07:00","id":1478456,"title":"","content":"I don't agree with the position, but I do want to point out the people complaining about &quot;flawed protagonists&quot; disappearing are talking about them disappearing from Werewolf/White Wolf specifically.<br /> <br /> But regarding the idea that the Lefty White Wolf developers are only displaying protagonists that align with their values, I'd ask them to consider the entire Tribe of hereditary aristocrats and explain how elitist monarchy fits into a leftist political ideology? Or a bunch of back-stabbing elitist schemers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T19:08:24-07:00","id":1478459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478455#post1478455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We know the Garou Nation is going to fracture due to the metaplot, <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So it will be metaplot that ends the Garou Nation and not simply a retcon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 04-09-2022, 10:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T21:08:07-07:00","id":1478464,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Kharnov;n1478456]I don't agree with the position, but I do want to point out the people complaining about &quot;flawed protagonists&quot; disappearing are talking about them disappearing from Werewolf/White Wolf specifically./QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Even if this was just about WtA (which it really isn't) you don't see any examples specifically about V5 or Garou presented in material created by nWW/Paradox here do you?<br /> <br /> There's no real sign this is the case. The problem is that Paradox wants to update the political message of the WoD from the 90s to the 2020s... but doesn't seem to have a cohesive idea of what that actually means (this is also a downside of having V5 made by as many different teams as they have already). It's easy to mistake a lack of cohesive political message for a lack of wanting to have one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478459#post1478459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So it will be metaplot that ends the Garou Nation and not simply a retcon?</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as we know right now? Yes. But again, &quot;end&quot; is a strong word.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T21:48:28-07:00","id":1478467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478464#post1478464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even if this was just about WtA (which it really isn't) you don't see any examples specifically about V5 or Garou presented in material created by nWW/Paradox here do you?<br /> <br /> There's no real sign this is the case. The problem is that Paradox wants to update the political message of the WoD from the 90s to the 2020s... but doesn't seem to have a cohesive idea of what that actually means (this is also a downside of having V5 made by as many different teams as they have already). It's easy to mistake a lack of cohesive political message for a lack of wanting to have one.</div> </div> </div> </div>My post began with &quot;I don't agree with the position&quot; and concluded with two examples of why I thought the claim was wrong because I do agree that they are incorrect making that claim about Werewolf/White Wolf. And my using &quot;Werewolf/White Wolf&quot; was meant to acknowledge that, as you point out, they weren't just talking about Werewolf; they were talking about White Wolf/Paradox in general (or rather, Fifth Edition in general).<br /> <br /> My point was that quoting characters from completely separate TV shows and movies does nothing to challenge their claims about White Wolf/Paradox. You'd have to refer to actual White Wolf content to disprove the specific claim that they were making. Maybe someone did provide examples from White Wolf/Paradox in there and I missed them (I was posting from my phone while I was at work at the time), but I just kept seeing references to things like Dexter and Breaking Bad. Which are completely irrelevant to any complaints being made about White Wolf protagonists in particular.<br /> <br /> Which is why I provided examples of White Wolf content that, IMO, disproved their claims, in the form of two whole Werewolf Tribes that are very much not the reflection of an ideal &quot;lefty&quot; or &quot;&quot;liberal snowflake&quot;&quot; protagonist, the Silver Fangs and Shadow Lords.<br /> <br /> I was just essentially trying to say that none of the previous posts seemed to actually respond to their specific complaint, even if that specific complaint was absolutely incorrect IMO. If you want to prove them wrong, prove them wrong. As I demonstrated, not too hard to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T21:49:57-07:00","id":1478469,"title":"","content":"I liked the Get. I\u2019m disappointed to see them fall. I was hoping for the Red Talons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-10T14:40:06-07:00","id":1478515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478469#post1478469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked the Get. I\u2019m disappointed to see them fall. I was hoping for the Red Talons.</div> </div> </div> </div>It should have been the Silver Fangs. They had that high profile quality where their fall would have been shocking, while also having an aura where their value was questionable at best. And it would have fit with the dissolution of the Garou nation. <br /> <br /> The Get had their problems, but I really liked them. They are one of my favorite Tribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-10T16:06:23-07:00","id":1478520,"title":"","content":"I really don\u2019t want the Get to fall, in fact not only do I like them, but their moral flaws and shades of gray add a lot to the setting in my opinion. So if I absolutely had to have a Tribe fall, the GoF would be at or at near the bottom of the list. If I had to get rid of them, I would give them a heroic sacrifice where they stop the Wyrm while mostly dying themselves.<br /> <br /> Though, I really don\u2019t see why a Tribe has to fall. This setting has been around for 30 years and people have been attached to their favorite Tribes for all of that time. I bought W:tA first edition when it first came out when I was just a teenager. I have liked the Get all of that time and I know others feel the same way about the Tribes that they like. I know that this new edition has to shake things up, but there are other ways than this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1129,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","user":"Sergeant Brother","date":". 04-11-2022, 10:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-10T16:47:25-07:00","id":1478523,"title":"","content":"I didn't want to leave the World of Darkness, but the World of Darkness has left me...This was the final straw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2582-gangrel44","name":"Gangrel44","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-10T17:10:10-07:00","id":1478524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478515#post1478515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They had that high profile quality where their fall would have been shocking, while also having an aura where their value was questionable at best. And it would have fit with the dissolution of the Garou nation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda taking this in reverse order:<br /> <br /> Again, I'd caution against assuming too much about what Garou society is going to look like in W5 until we get far more concrete previews or the book itself. Even if the Garou Nation completely dissolves, it doesn't mean the end results are a society where the Silver Fangs don't make sense. The BNS metaplot was a division of the Garou Nation into two factions, with the Silver Fangs heading one, and the Shadow Lords heading the other. Dissolving doesn't mean we're going to have a W5 setting where a leadership oriented Tribe no longer has a purpose because there's no larger social structures.<br /> <br /> Also, I'd say the very fact that the value of the Silver Fangs being questionable is their most compelling reason to continue to exist. If the WoD is supposed to explore left-political criticisms off political issues, we want a vehicle to examine the role of the elite; esp. elite that claim the right to executive power. Even as we've moved away from absolute monarchies (though those still exist too), we still have autocrats, and we have constitutional chief executives that are still firmly controlled by the new elites. Even if some try to cultivate narratives to the contrary, presidents and prime ministers are people that had prestige and power before that. Since we need elites to do commentary on elites, if you cut the Silver Fangs, you run the risk of just diluting the Shadow Lords into being Silver Fangs but with different fur colors.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is me, I'm completely amenable to the argument that the Silver Fangs and Shadow Lords are redundant and we only needing one Tribe of rulers with factions around those currently in power vs those currently out of power. But that's reboot talk.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478520#post1478520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though, I really don\u2019t see why a Tribue has to fall.</div> </div> </div> </div>We haven't actually seen an argument from the creators yet around this. We should let them try to explain their thinking at some point. Even if you're completely right that the fact that it's not readily apparent is troubling and there are clearly other options.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-10T17:14:59-07:00","id":1478525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gangrel44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478523#post1478523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't want to leave the World of Darkness, but the World of Darkness has left me...This was the final straw.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well look on the bright side, we still have the 20th Edition and the Vault with all the like-minded people who will continue to create material for it. And odds are we'll get people that take the kernels of good things from W5 and port it back to W20 without the bad.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-10T19:29:30-07:00","id":1478540,"title":"","content":"The &quot;we still have 20th&quot; for WtA fans tends to not be as comforting as VtM and Mage fans; those lines are getting much more complete 20th editions.<br /> <br /> There's no Lore of the Tribes 20th. There's no Book of the Weaver or Wyld 20th. I would love to see if a Rage Across the Heavens 20th could do for that book that the V20 Black Hand book did.<br /> <br /> We still have the bad taste of Shattered Dreams and W20 Changing Ways public disagreements between nWW/Paradox and the Onyx Path freelancers doing the books.<br /> <br /> Are people going to address this in the STV? Sure. But it's not really fair to the fans to have to make the game we want, or the freelancers that should be getting their full rates to do full books instead of what they can scrounge up from books that don't get the support as official releases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-11T01:24:10-07:00","id":1478552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478540#post1478540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are people going to address this in the STV? Sure. But it's not really fair to the fans to have to make the game we want, or the freelancers that should be getting their full rates to do full books instead of what they can scrounge up from books that don't get the support as official releases.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it isn't....<br /> <br /> Well, I really liked W20 Changing Breeds approach to open development and I think those fans who wanted to contribute could. Rage across the world 20th (not sure about the name) also had it, and feedback was, that they didn't include the Den Parent sept office, so this was corrected, but the new entry is specifically stating that, for example, a Nana, like described in Kinfolk: Unsung Heros, was never ever something septs would do - and then there wasn't a second round of fan based proof reading...<br /> <br /> Currently, it seems, the process is reduced to crowdsourcing the typo search as opposed to really give feedback during the development process. And that is something I really can't part take in. I don't have the time to read a book and report the errors within a four weeks or so time window before the printing or POD starts. I'm thankful for all the fans who have the time and do so, though.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-11T01:49:47-07:00","id":1478553,"title":"","content":"I can understand why Onyx Path isn't doing the open dev thing as much as they used to. It makes the process even slower, the noise (bad feedback) to signal (good feedback) ratio is horrible, the open dev era led to lots and lots of unfounded speculation on the forums (that makes threads like this one look tame) as people poured over every word to divine the final product instead of voicing useful concerns, for the WoD specifically Onyx Path also has to consider Paradox's own feelings on open dev and how much control Paradox wants over the books, and you get really nasty things like Changeling: the Lost 2e where the first lead developer left the project and the second developer took the game in an entirely different direction which led to a lot of division between people that wanted the first version and all that drama that only happened because people saw so much during the open dev period.<br /> <br /> It's also not just Onyx Path. A lot of developers that used to do open dev have stopped because it was a fad people tried, and for the most part didn't really improve things as much as was hoped.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-11T02:03:55-07:00","id":1478554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gangrel44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478523#post1478523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't want to leave the World of Darkness, but the World of Darkness has left me...This was the final straw.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly I'm just watching out of morbid curiosity.to see how they're going wreck m5. It's a lot more ambigious than w5 since it's a lot harder to graft Awakening on than forsaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-11T02:38:58-07:00","id":1478555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478524#post1478524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We haven't actually seen an argument from the creators yet around this. We should let them try to explain their thinking at some point. Even if you're completely right that the fact that it's not readily apparent is troubling and there are clearly other options.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're 4 years in and we haven't even seen a release of whose working on it yet.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-11T03:08:59-07:00","id":1478557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478553#post1478553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can understand why Onyx Path isn't doing the open dev thing as much as they used to. It makes the process even slower, the noise (bad feedback) to signal (good feedback) ratio is horrible, the open dev era led to lots and lots of unfounded speculation on the forums (that makes threads like this one look tame) as people poured over every word to divine the final product instead of voicing useful concerns, for the WoD specifically Onyx Path also has to consider Paradox's own feelings on open dev and how much control Paradox wants over the books, and you get really nasty things like Changeling: the Lost 2e where the first lead developer left the project and the second developer took the game in an entirely different direction which led to a lot of division between people that wanted the first version and all that drama that only happened because people saw so much during the open dev period.<br /> <br /> It's also not just Onyx Path. A lot of developers that used to do open dev have stopped because it was a fad people tried, and for the most part didn't really improve things as much as was hoped.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't follow C:tL 2nd Edition's development. And I can see the problems you describe.<br /> Looking at Pathfinder 1st and comparing it to D&amp;D3.5 I see that going through the feedback and using it to improve the product works well.<br /> Same goes for V5, I guess. There were several ideas I didn't like in the game test at the WoD Convention in Berlin - and I'm glad they didn't make it to the final product. Settling for the CoD attributes, for example, in favour of some other ideas.<br /> <br /> Sure, it is a bit work work and for the those who just create a book, not a core book or new edition, it can be too much. On the other hand, I feel, freelance authors as well as the decision makers at nWW or OPP work from a kind of confirmation bubble that possibly leads to content that caters to some (felt) requirements (and possibly theories about long term brand development) but not necessarily to the majority of the fan base...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-11T04:11:50-07:00","id":1478558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478555#post1478555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We're 4 years in and we haven't even seen a release of whose working on it yet.....</div> </div> </div> </div>Well a second release. We got a first release before they switched which company was handling it and the first team announced was disbanded (though with no declarative statement that none of them would be involved or something like that).<br /> <br /> The fact that W5 is in a second completely restarted development cycle is its own big problem, but not really guiding to the point at hand.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478557#post1478557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There were several ideas I didn't like in the game test at the WoD Convention in Berlin - and I'm glad they didn't make it to the final product.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a huge difference between playtesting (something both Paradox and Onyx Path continue to do) and open development (which neither does as policy, and while Onyx Path leaves it up to individual developers it's fallen completely out of favor outside of a few blog posts here and there.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that large scale playtesting like Paizo, WotC, and nWW did are huge time consuming and costly endeavors to do right. Most companies, including Onyx Path, don't have the resources to do a global playtest. The sheer amount of data collection, sorting, and analysis for dealing with thousands of playtest reports is months of full time work for a small team of people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On the other hand, I feel, freelance authors as well as the decision makers at nWW or OPP work from a kind of confirmation bubble that possibly leads to content that caters to some (felt) requirements (and possibly theories about long term brand development) but not necessarily to the majority of the fan base... </div> </div> </div>Knowing what you do about open dev could you actually create a functional guide with a good accuracy rate at figuring out which books got open dev and which didn't for people that don't know where to look it up?<br /> <br /> And again, it's not just nWW or Onyx Path here. During the early 2010s, lots of smaller companies were doing open dev because it seemed like a good idea for a number of reasons. By 2020... almost nobody does them any more. Whatever the trades off are, lots of RPG developers have decided that open dev takes up more energy than it's worth.<br /> <br /> Is what you're talking about a risk? Sure. But it's also how RPGs were done for ~30 years before enough fans were online for open dev to even be real thing..The entire cWoD original run was closed dev. Meanwhile, D&amp;D 4e's failings are regularly pointed to it's quasi-open dev process that resulted in a &quot;designed by committee&quot; process that resulted in a fantastic system that completely lacked the enticing flavors of 3.X, PF1e, or 5e.<br /> <br /> There is no perfect solution here. But when the majority of the industry jettisons a design approach... there's probably a good reason for it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-11T06:35:11-07:00","id":1478560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478555#post1478555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We're 4 years in and we haven't even seen a release of whose working on it yet.....</div> </div> </div> </div>It's being developed by the WoD team at Paradox, lead by Justin Achilli. They announced when alongside when Paradox said they brought corebook development in-house.<br /> <br /> Werewolf's development was delayed a bit by the Hunter's, as they shifted it to the background as Paradox saw they could get Hunter out faster iirc.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-11T07:46:49-07:00","id":1478565,"title":"","content":"I'd really like to see a concerete source for this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-11T09:02:40-07:00","id":1478575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the weirdest parts for me is, when I check out some spaces to see how some are praising this decision the conversations seem very out of left field in comparison to what I remember about the Get during the height of WoD popularity. People certain talked about the evil camp from the tribe book(and a feature of the tribe books was including one evil, often hidden camp for each Tribe). But I don't remember too many conversations about how this made all Get Nazis. For that matter I don't remember all Get having to be Scandanavian. Maybe my memory is getting the best of me and I'm forgetting things so maybe I'm wrong. But many of the comments I am seeing around the internet about why it's good to get(zing) rid of the Get seem odd to say the least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Different groups, different takes. In the 2010s, I still ran into people talking about Fenrir having a Mixed Heritage flaw. A flaw from the 1st tribebook only. Some people never updated their knowledge of the tribes beyond 1st or 2nd ed. I've seen people claim ALL WtA players are toxicly masculine men,etc.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-11T10:14:52-07:00","id":1478580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478565#post1478565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd really like to see a concerete source for this?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Assuming you mean my post, sure. Always happy to provide them.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/media/press-releases/press-release/world-of-darkness-names-renegade-game-studios-publishing-partner-for-its-catalogue-of-tabletop-rpgs\" target=\"_blank\">Press release from Paradox</a>: They announce Renegade is the new publisher, and that further corebooks will be developed in-house<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2L9Cj3VMHzw&amp;t=303s\" target=\"_blank\">World of Darkness Brand Update</a>: They announce Hunter, which they had in the backburner for a while, and decided to go prioritize it since it needed less work than W5. This is further corroborated by other News streams where Outstar mentions that after Hunter releases, all focus will be on Werewolf. Though considering the development parts of Hunter have been ready for a while, it is safe to assume it is already the focus. Of the Writing team at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-11T12:37:22-07:00","id":1478590,"title":"","content":"For me, the Get were simply the guys you picked if you wanted to play Thor as a werewolf. This idea that you absolutely positively had to be a Nazi as a Get is, to say the least, news to me.<br /> <br /> All werewolves have a subtext of social darwinism, except maybe the COG, but that subtext was about behavior, not race. If you behaved with strength, honor, and courage, you were worthy, if you didn't, you weren't worthy. Your skin color meant jack. The Get seemed to buy into that even more than most werewolves, and that was about it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-11T12:53:52-07:00","id":1478592,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27145_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27145\" data-vbnamecard=\"27145\">SetiteFriend</a> Sorry, I meant <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar479_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"479\" data-vbnamecard=\"479\">Damian May</a> and the Fenrir being removed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-11T13:25:48-07:00","id":1478594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478592#post1478592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27145_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27145\" data-vbnamecard=\"27145\">SetiteFriend</a> Sorry, I meant <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar479_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"479\" data-vbnamecard=\"479\">Damian May</a> and the Fenrir being removed.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I might as well give a source for that too.<br /> <br /> We knew 2 Tribes weren't going to be present in the corebook of W5, since the Brand Updated I previously linked. Though no mention of them not being playable ever or being Antagonists was made. We knew they still exist in-lore but wouldn't be a core option. One of those Tribes would have left the nation looking for new allies or something, and the other fell to Hauglosk, and to quote Justin, &quot;arguably to the Wyrm&quot;. Hauglosk being a new concept introduced in W5, counterpart to Harano, representing extreme zealotry <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/WhiteWolfRPG/comments/tzhz41/this_blows_from_one_of_the_people_involved_with/\" target=\"_blank\">The print on this reddit post is true</a>, though I believe it happened inside a facebook group and can't check it myself. With it we know the Get were the ones who fell to Hauglosk. <br /> <br /> Furthermore the Stargazers are the other tribe, the one that left for new allies, <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/i1BH9ta\" target=\"_blank\">they were also confirmed</a> by Flyos. However, this post has since been archived or deleted.<br /> <br /> Flyos is a board game developer, based on Montreal, who developed VTM: Chapters and is developing WTA: Retaliation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27145,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","user":"SetiteFriend","date":".  Clarifying which tribe was which, in case it wasn't clear 04-11-2022, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-11T13:38:49-07:00","id":1478595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478590#post1478590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, the Get were simply the guys you picked if you wanted to play Thor as a werewolf. This idea that you absolutely positively had to be a Nazi as a Get is, to say the least, news to me.<br /> <br /> All werewolves have a subtext of social darwinism, except maybe the COG, but that subtext was about behavior, not race. If you behaved with strength, honor, and courage, you were worthy, if you didn't, you weren't worthy. Your skin color meant jack. The Get seemed to buy into that even more than most werewolves, and that was about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not entirely. The Get of Fenris care more about ancestry than some other tribes. &quot;Mixed Heritage&quot; was a even a Flaw with some social repercussions among the tribe.<br /> <br /> That said, their ideology was not based on human race. It is their believe, that they are of Fenris (the mythological wolf turned tribal totem) and the other garou are not (which is backed up partly by mythology of other tribes as well). If ever a Get of Fenris would have a true born child with a human of latin, african, asian or other than north-european heritage the child would have his or her place among the get of fenris, if the Rite of Passage if passed - not necessarily being of mixed heritage since no other garou line is bred in, just &quot;human&quot;. That said, such a garou would still be educated in the ways of the tribe and their mythology and all that to be a proper Get of Fenris. Skin color doesn't matter, acting in accordance with the tribal virtues, does.<br /> <br /> And while the Get of Fenris are said to have, in the past, conquered caerns from other tribes (both pre- and post- the discovery of the Americas by the Europeans) and have a tendency to possibly see some of the other tribes as &quot;lesser&quot; - they do not automatically share the same inhuman racial thoughts that Nazis have.<br /> <br /> But, one can see why early authors made that connection (and at the same time said that the tribe is also fighting against these individuals internally).<br /> Also, early authors credited the Get with extreme sexism (to the point where a female Get is being adopted into the Uktena tribe in an early short story of &quot;When will you Rage?&quot;) and outright mentioning of the need of women to submit to men in the 1st Ed TB.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 04-11-2022, 04:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-11T13:58:13-07:00","id":1478597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478590#post1478590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, the Get were simply the guys you picked if you wanted to play Thor as a werewolf. This idea that you absolutely positively had to be a Nazi as a Get is, to say the least, news to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;...had to be a Nazi as a Get...&quot; is a strawman.<br /> <br /> Thor is actually a great pop culture example of the problem! Look at Thor in his first MCU solo movie and the first Avengers movie (though there's plenty in the later movies too, but Loki's redemption arc muddies things): watch how Thor bends over backwards to try to defend Loki. Loki is his brother (if adopted). Loki is Asgardian. Loki's cleverness is &quot;strength&quot; in Thor's eyes even if not Thor's way of being strong. And because of all of that Thor never stops giving Loki another chance even while Loki is still unapologetic for being a mass murderer and only really cares about the damage he's caused when it gets Frigga killed. <br /> <br /> Thor is, if you stop and think about it, complicit in a huge amount of harm that Loki caused because Thor just chalks it up to Loki being Loki and it not really mattering because Loki's toying with lesser species (so are Odin and plenty of others of course). You can play Thor-Get all you want, but you're playing the guy that stands up for Nazi-Loki because he's in your Tribe and you can't bring yourself to cast him out no matter how much twisting of your dad's teachings he does.<br /> <br /> That's the problem the Get have always had, and had even after the Swords were wiped out: you can't play a Fenrir without being the Thor that ends up enabling a Loki. The Thor/Get way of exalting the strong is inseparable from the Loki/Swords ideals of oppressing the weak. That's why MCU Thor exalts in seeing Captain America being worthy of wielding Mjolnir: Steve's idea of strength is better than the one Thor inherited from Odin. That's why he gives up ruling the remaining Asgardians to Valkyrie. Thor grows up and learns that being the strongest doesn't actually make you the best; it just makes you strong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All werewolves have a subtext of social darwinism, except maybe the COG, but that subtext was about behavior, not race. If you behaved with strength, honor, and courage, you were worthy, if you didn't, you weren't worthy. Your skin color meant jack. The Get seemed to buy into that even more than most werewolves, and that was about it. </div> </div> </div>This is ignoring something that's been in every edition of WtA: The Fenrir don't like how the spirits judge strength, honor, and courage. There has always been a conflict between their ideals, and the fact that &quot;weaker&quot; Garou like the Bone Gnawers and Black Furies somehow still manage to attain Renown and Rank.<br /> <br /> &quot;Strength&quot; is the sticking point because who's strong and who's weak, and thus who's worthy of power and who has power they don't deserve is a completely arbitrary cultural norm the Get have constructed. That's why they're fertile soil for bigots. The Valkyrie Camp of Fenrir have always been on the verge of defecting to the Black Furies because they're sick and tired of mainstream Get &quot;strength&quot; being biased towards masculine associated ideals of strength: a female Get has to be twice as strong than a mediocre male Get to be acknowledged as strong &quot;We don't care what's between your legs, we just care about strength! Pay no attention to the fact that all our tests of strength at biased towards people with high levels of testosterone.&quot; &quot;We don't care about the color of your skin, we just care about strength! Pay no attention to the fact that all our tests of strength are biased towards Garou with strong breeding with the right kind of people.&quot;<br /> <br /> Institutional discrimination is a thing, and the Get are extremely guilt of it. Claiming you only care about personal merit doesn't work in a world that starts people on unequal ground.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-11T14:51:24-07:00","id":1478605,"title":"","content":"And Thor is interesting because he has those character-flaws. Werewolves are barbarians, and by modern human ethics anti-heroes at best. Player characters may be more politically evolved, and oppose the worst elements of their tribes, essentially being Worf in a world of Klingons, but the tribes themselves should remain backwards savages. The werewolf world is more interesting that way, than if you make them all perfect progressives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-11T15:04:02-07:00","id":1478607,"title":"","content":"Is there some point where you seem to think I've been arguing that:<br /> <br /> 1) Having the Get be the ones to fall was a good idea (I will note I have called it the &quot;safe&quot; pick from a corporate perspective).<br /> 2) The Tribes shouldn't be flawed.<br /> 3) The Tribes should be perfect representations of modern progressive politics.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-11T16:19:07-07:00","id":1478615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478597#post1478597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Valkyrie Camp of Fenrir have always been on the verge of defecting to the Black Furies because they're sick and tired of mainstream Get &quot;strength&quot; being biased towards masculine associated ideals of strength: a female Get has to be twice as strong than a mediocre male Get to be acknowledged as strong.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I always found a difficult situation. Revised made Karin a prominent Jarl a female, but also build upon the Valkyrie/Fury relationship and actually added to the Furie TB that they actively seek out unsatisfied females from other tribes (not clear if that was limited to cubs or even garou with rank).<br /> The Valkyries should have been presented more like an elite Sisterhood who's members would show off or even flaunt their strengths and accomplishments and with proper Galliard support be a force within the tribe to be reckoned with. Instead authors always seem to make female Gets apart from Karin look like they are already with one foot out the proverbial door and signing up for the furies.<br /> That is actually the reason female get players in our LARP diminish the existence of the Valkyries within the tribe.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-11T17:28:01-07:00","id":1478621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478590#post1478590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, the Get were simply the guys you picked if you wanted to play Thor as a werewolf. This idea that you absolutely positively had to be a Nazi as a Get is, to say the least, news to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>After the 2nd tribebook, playing a Thor-alike as a werewolf would also be odd, because the Fenrir hated Odin's brood and were out for their blood. That's part of the reason why the Get, as presented in the later book, didn't really see it as their duty to stop conversions of pagans to Christianity, for example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All werewolves have a subtext of social darwinism, except maybe the COG, but that subtext was about behavior, not race. If you behaved with strength, honor, and courage, you were worthy, if you didn't, you weren't worthy. Your skin color meant jack. The Get seemed to buy into that even more than most werewolves, and that was about it. </div> </div> </div>Fenrir's history in the later tribebook presented him as being about never wanting to do things the easy way, to a degree that could seem comical (for one example, he couldn't bring himself to be mushy about feelings for a mate, making him seem extremely tsundere). The tribe sort of follows in that, being the type to stack on challenges and suffer extreme pain to prove that they're strong, even though those aren't strictly necessary to any process of development or personal cultivation; after all, both the Get and the CoGs have Resist Pain as an in-splat Gift, as does the Philodox auspice. You don't need to be macho to have determination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-12T16:17:22-07:00","id":1478718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478597#post1478597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;...had to be a Nazi as a Get...&quot; is a strawman.<br /> <br /> Thor is actually a great pop culture example of the problem! Look at Thor in his first MCU solo movie and the first Avengers movie (though there's plenty in the later movies too, but Loki's redemption arc muddies things): watch how Thor bends over backwards to try to defend Loki. Loki is his brother (if adopted). Loki is Asgardian. Loki's cleverness is &quot;strength&quot; in Thor's eyes even if not Thor's way of being strong. And because of all of that Thor never stops giving Loki another chance even while Loki is still unapologetic for being a mass murderer and only really cares about the damage he's caused when it gets Frigga killed.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, in the MCU, do we know Loki's past before he went insane? Thor might have been weighing more than their familial bonds, but everything Loki has done up until that point. He could have SAVED entire worlds with his cunning, and might do so again if he could figure out what was wrong with him or how to bring him back. Also, Thor isn't a Jedi who has been trained from near birth to let go of all bonds so he can wield his awesome power with absolute clarity and impartiality. He might have even felt guilty in retrospect for being the family's favorite, golden child, confusing his choices even more. Simply put, I don't think he was really making conscious, thought out choices so much as instinctively trying to figure someway to get his little brother away from where he could hurt someone or be hurt himself.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478597#post1478597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can play Thor-Get all you want, but you're playing the guy that stands up for Nazi-Loki because he's in your Tribe and you can't bring yourself to cast him out no matter how much twisting of your dad's teachings he does. That's the problem the Get have always had, and had even after the Swords were wiped out: you can't play a Fenrir without being the Thor that ends up enabling a Loki.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thor Get ultimately kill the Loki Get. And, you are talking about MCU Thor killing someone he has a bond of over thousands of years with which might not have been something he could just do. The Get on the other hand killed a diminishing number of their people and family needed to protect Caerns and wilderness and kinfolk. But they still did it because they knew it was the right thing to do and the war gave them some serious introspection.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478597#post1478597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Thor/Get way of exalting the strong is inseparable from the Loki/Swords ideals of oppressing the weak. That's why MCU Thor exalts in seeing Captain America being worthy of wielding Mjolnir: Steve's idea of strength is better than the one Thor inherited from Odin. That's why he gives up ruling the remaining Asgardians to Valkyrie. Thor grows up and learns that being the strongest doesn't actually make you the best; it just makes you strong.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. My bro is a Marine. His branch of the military like to say they are the strongest of the strong, but that doesn't mean he believes in oppressing the weak.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478597#post1478597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is ignoring something that's been in every edition of WtA: The Fenrir don't like how the spirits judge strength, honor, and courage. There has always been a conflict between their ideals, and the fact that &quot;weaker&quot; Garou like the Bone Gnawers and Black Furies somehow still manage to attain Renown and Rank.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are perhaps forgetting how the Garou can &quot;corrupt&quot; spirits? How generations of interacting with werewolves that are bigoted towards metis can make the spirits bigoted towards them as well? Or the story of Dire Rat? A simple Totem Avatar of Rat that was adopted by a hyper aggressive pack and it was corrupted from a guerilla warrior into a spirit that led the charge into battle and then either became its own Incarna or was eaten by Rat, depending on who is telling the story? The spirits are ancient, so who knows what they believe now compared to what they believed back before humans discovered fire? I suspect that the spirits who award the Get their Renown wouldn't accept some of the things that snag renown for other Tribes. Remember that the spirits are not all of one mind. The Red Talons, if I remember correctly, have Gifts and Rites that help them with eating human flesh. Something that a lot of Gaian spirits might condemn, especially the ones that associate with the other Tribes, but which others, probably the ones that associate with the Reds in particular, apparently think is about time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478597#post1478597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Strength&quot; is the sticking point because who's strong and who's weak, and thus who's worthy of power and who has power they don't deserve is a completely arbitrary cultural norm the Get have constructed. That's why they're fertile soil for bigots.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, to be fair, lets examine the situation and see if it is really &quot;arbitrary.&quot; The Fera all have their own unique tasks. The Garou were made by Gaia to kill things. They kill things that are bigger, stronger, and more numerous than they are. They are fighting a war that they are not simply losing, but apparently will have lost in W5E. Being strong and being able to use that great strength effectively isn't just an advantage, it gives hope to the Tribe and the kinfolk and to the spirits. It is what THEIR spirits, especially Great Fenris, demands of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478597#post1478597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Valkyrie Camp of Fenrir have always been on the verge of defecting to the Black Furies</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that changed in their Revised book? I don't have mine on hand, so I cannot be sure<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478597#post1478597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">because they're sick and tired of mainstream Get &quot;strength&quot; being biased towards masculine associated ideals of strength: a female Get has to be twice as strong than a mediocre male Get to be acknowledged as strong &quot;We don't care what's between your legs, we just care about strength! Pay no attention to the fact that all our tests of strength at biased towards people with high levels of testosterone.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Problem: physical power means a LOT in battle when you are typically fighting the same way your elders did 10,000 years ago. And to make matters complicated, it is hard for women to achieve equity on W:tA's particular battlefield, because it isn't just the Wyrm that wants Gaia dead, it is the Weaver as well. So going a more Glass Walker route (which to varying degrees have made them and the BG pariahs) and using fetish guns and high tech weaponry to level the playing field and achieving martial equity is urrah and sometimes close to sacrilege as it celebrates and strengthens the Weaver and its children in the eyes of many Garou, not just the Get. Many Garou tribes, even the BFs, are basically your &quot;noble savages&quot; trope who fight in the modern era with tools only a couple steps above what a neanderthal might have fought with.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478597#post1478597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;We don't care about the color of your skin, we just care about strength! Pay no attention to the fact that all our tests of strength are biased towards Garou with strong breeding with the right kind of people.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Err... Are you referring to the Pure Breed background? I am confused if you are not. Technically, that is verifiably a form of strength as your children have a higher chance of breeding true. Though I am given to understand that it can be possessed by people of all ethnicities, and for all Tribes that have that background. Heck, a bunch of wild dogs in Africa can have up Level 3 Pure Breed in the Red Talons and they aren't even wolves. Other than that, I am not sure what you are getting at. The Get Rite of Passage is to be flung by more experienced Get into a hellhole or something and then only accepting those who are able to survive and climb out. Women might suffer a disadvantage, depending on the circumstances, but I am lost at how skin color can do that, unless you mean to imply that the people of non Nordic descent get thrown into worse hellholes? Or maybe easier ones, and thus robbing them of Glory and standing?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478597#post1478597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Institutional discrimination is a thing, and the Get are extremely guilt of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely, but when you are basically Tribe: Seal Team Six, and are fighting an army that has already beaten you and destroyed your home, you can kind of see how it is understandable why physical power is cherished among the Get who see it as their duty to be the supreme warriors of a warrior race, especially when things like technology are still taboo, and fights to save the world are often barehanded, unless you are one of those blessed with something like a klaive or fang dagger. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478597#post1478597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Claiming you only care about personal merit doesn't work in a world that starts people on unequal ground.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are referring to the way men and women's bodies develop differently, I certainly agree in the real world. In the fantasy world that has been constructed, that might be more difficult given the parameters of that world. And the stakes.<br /> Like I said, achieving equity on a magical battlefield when the spirit of all technology itself seems to want to kill you as well, and you are a RELIGIOUS warrior, so are going to be strongly observing ancient taboos, is a conundrum. Still, realistically, even if we don't like a culture that sees ripping a BSD Elder in half with a single blow from their paws as the final pinnacle of Garouhood, given where they are and where they come from, they aren't bad guys for having that as their ideal. Although, I naturally agree there are problems with it that creates all sorts of injustices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 04-12-2022, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-12T18:27:04-07:00","id":1478722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478718#post1478718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, in the MCU, do we know Loki's past before he went insane?</div> </div> </div> </div>When did Loki ever go insane? Loki is always presented as lucid and knowing what he's doing. Loki's plan to murder his biological family to show both his allegiance to his adoptive family and that he can make the hard decisions as king needs to be able to do while Thor is too naive for the throne is rational from Loki's perspective and knowledge. Evil frequently is done easily because it's easy to be in a place where it seems rational.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> He could have SAVED entire worlds with his cunning and might do so again if he could figure out what was wrong with him or how to bring him back. </div> </div> </div>Trying to convince me there's a valid moral or ethical argument to not using everything in your power to stop someone you know for certain is attempting to murder millions of people from executing their plans on the basis of they might save millions of people later is not going to work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, Thor isn't a Jedi who has been trained from near birth to let go of all bonds so he can wield his awesome power with absolute clarity and impartiality. </div> </div> </div>Yes. That's a huge part of my point. Thor (and by metaphor the Get) have strong biases that led him to tolerate a lot of horrific things from his brother that he really shouldn't have. Let's recall the scene in Thor 3 where Thor talks about the time Loki disguised himself as a snake in order to sneak attack Thor and stab him. Thor thinks this is an amusing anecdote about their fun childhood. Everyone else instantly recognizes how fucked up that is; even fellow Asgardian Valkyrie.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Simply put, I don't think he was really making conscious, thought out choices so much as instinctively trying to figure someway to get his little brother away from where he could hurt someone or be hurt himself. </div> </div> </div>And that's how the Swords existed in the Fenrir for as long as the did. It's the same exact kind of thing. It's classic broken stair excuses. Like Loki, the Swords didn't learn their lesson and stop pushing, they just saw that the mainstream Get would ultimately keep them self from outsiders no matter how many horrible things they did until they finally pushed so hard the Get couldn't justify it any longer.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thor Get ultimately kill the Loki Get. </div> </div> </div>Sure. And how much evil was done in their decades of indulgence? What have the Get changed in their culture to stop a new Swords from forming?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And, you are talking about MCU Thor killing someone he has a bond of over thousands of years with which might not have been something he could just do. </div> </div> </div>Technically, I'm just saying Thor bares moral culpability for not stopping Loki sooner; killing Loki in the context of the MCU wasn't necessary as Asgard had the capability to imprison Loki (we're not talking about Batman and the Joker and the morality of continuing to toss the Joker in Arkham no matter how many times he escapes and goes on another murder spree).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> His branch of the military like to say they are the strongest of the strong, but that doesn't mean he believes in oppressing the weak. </div> </div> </div>Your bro might make Steve Rogers look compromised by being the most honorable marine that's ever served. That doesn't change all the evils the Marines specifically have committed as an organization, and the evils of the system that allows the Marines as they currently exist to continue to exist.<br /> <br /> That's the point. It doesn't matter how morally upstanding one soldier is. The system is broken. You can abandon the system, or you can compromise your honor and figure out how you live with that. Even if your bro not only never oppressed the weak, but also spend every day of his service empowering people, the Marines as an institution absolutely engage in oppressing the weak on behalf of the military industrial complex. How do you think we have extrajudicial facilities to use to illegally detain people? Why does our military's budget include manufacturing illegal weapons so we can sell them to autocrats that them drop them on civilian targets (ex: Yemen)? Why are the Marines resisting their principle of subservience to civilian oversight when it comes to their own admitted problems with rampant sexual assaults in their ranks?<br /> <br /> Your bro might have never personally taken part in any of that. But he was part of the system that generated those evils.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You are perhaps forgetting how the Garou can &quot;corrupt&quot; spirits? </div> </div> </div>Nope, that's certainly part of my thinking on the subject. If the spirits couldn't be &quot;swayed&quot; than the Get's idea that other Garou &quot;cheat&quot; the system doesn't have any authentic weight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Fera all have their own unique tasks. </div> </div> </div>That's in-game mythology, not something the books say is absolute truth. The books repeatedly point out that this belief doesn't really hold up to deep examination as many shifters have overlapping portfolios. This belief has proven to be one of the most destructive elements in shifter culture: the idea that &quot;we have a job that's uniquely ours, so we get to say what happens in this circumstance,&quot; is the thinking that fueled the Wars of Rage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Garou were made by Gaia to kill things. </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure the Ratkin, Bastet, and Nagah would beg to differ that the Garou are the exclusive killers in the name of Gaia. Even plenty of shifters that don't see killing as a major part of their duties, are still just as capable of being killers as those that do (like the Rokea and Gurahl).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Being strong and being able to use that great strength effectively isn't just an advantage,... </div> </div> </div>Is it the specific way the Get define strength that enables this? If you want to show it's not arbitrary you have to actually show it at some point, not just assert it. Why isn't the CoG definition of strength just as good for this as the Get's? If they are equally valid, than they're also arbitrary.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Problem: physical power means a LOT in battle when you are typically fighting the same way your elders did 10,000 years ago. </div> </div> </div>1) The war the Garou are fighting is one where muscles are one of the least efficient tool for winning the war. The Get stress methods that hold the line, but not press the enemy back.<br /> <br /> 2) 10,000 years ago anything resembling &quot;battle&quot; in a war-like context was not a gender segregated activity. 10,000 years ago, if it came to fighting at that level of urgency, everyone capable of fighting fought. The idea of war being a masculine activity is a rather recent one in the longer scale of human existence, because we needed societies large enough to support people that could specialize in soldiering (even if not full time) before it could become linked to specific demographics. Women have been engaging in war that whole time too; even to the point of there being a long history of women pretending to be men to get into the fight..<br /> <br /> 3) The Garou's biggest strength is something you already mentioned: combining wolf and human cooperative hunting into being highly effective fighting units (something that does separate them from the Fera rather than killing). Packs give Garou the edge in most conflicts they engage with, not individual raw physical prowess. Five Garou that are in a well coordinated pack can easily defeat five Garou that are fighting as individuals even if the individuals are technically of greater physical prowess.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And to make matters complicated, it is hard for women to achieve equity on W:tA's particular battlefield, because it isn't just the Wyrm that wants Gaia dead, it is the Weaver as well. So going a more Glass Walker route (which to varying degrees have made them and the BG pariahs) and using fetish guns and high tech weaponry to level the playing field and achieving martial equity is urrah and sometimes close to sacrilege as it celebrates and strengthens the Weaver and its children in the eyes of many Garou, </div> </div> </div>I fail to see how this actually complicates anything. It just demonstrates how wrong headed the Get philosophy is, and demonstrates that the Get aren't alone in the Garou Nation in this particular wrong-headedness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Many Garou tribes, even the BFs, are basically your &quot;noble savages&quot; trope who fight in the modern era with tools only a couple steps above what a neanderthal might have fought with. </div> </div> </div>Again, your chronology here is amazingly off. The Iron Age period (the weaponry the Garou tend to like the most, like swords and big metal axes) started ~3,500 years ago. Neanderthals died out 40,000 years ago. No Neanderthal fought with anything nearly as technologically advanced as a klaive, jarlhammer, or labrys. The Garou like weapons far closer to backup weapons modern soldiers still train in than our ancient hominid cousins had. Comparing a Garou's Crinos claws to flint tipped spears is... I'm not even sure where to start with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Err... Are you referring to the Pure Breed background? </div> </div> </div>Remember that you add Pure Breed to formal challenge dice pools, not just social ones. Any test of strength that qualifies is innately biased towards Pure Breed, and Pure Breed is strongest when the Tribes highly curate breeding between Garou and kin in specific communities. It's explicitly one of the ways the Silver Fangs maintain their power in the Garou Nation.<br /> <br /> A BP 0 Garou that makes it into the Get has to compete with Garou that have a multiple dice advantage just because they were born to better curated families rather than having personal merit.<br /> <br /> I'm mostly talking about post-initiation issues and how the Get philosophy inherently biases their internal political advancements around traits that aren't actually personal strength.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Although, I naturally agree there are problems with it that creates all sorts of injustices. </div> </div> </div>Then... what was the rest of this all about? This is my point. The Get's philosophy inherently creates injustice. The Swords were just a extreme case of what's a natural element of the Tribe's philosophy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-12T18:59:20-07:00","id":1478726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478515#post1478515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It should have been the Silver Fangs. They had that high profile quality where their fall would have been shocking, while also having an aura where their value was questionable at best. And it would have fit with the dissolution of the Garou nation. <br /> <br /> The Get had their problems, but I really liked them. They are one of my favorite Tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked the Silver Fangs cause they had that old world old money charm. I didn\u2019t really like the Talons because in spite of liking both WtA and WtF (though I\u2019m much more familiar with WtA) I\u2019m not really into wolves as rl animals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-12T19:32:01-07:00","id":1478731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478722#post1478722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then... what was the rest of this all about? This is my point. The Get's philosophy inherently creates injustice. The Swords were just a extreme case of what's a natural element of the Tribe's philosophy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will go into more detail tomorrow evening, but THIS is the point:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478722#post1478722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why isn't the CoG definition of strength just as good for this as the Get's?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is just as valid. When you are a CoG doing CoG things. Just like the unique &quot;strength&quot; of the people who go around and test your city's water to make sure it is safe is just as valid as the &quot;strength&quot; of a Green Beret or a firefighter. But they are doing different tasks. The CoG win hearts and minds and can even recruit ordinary people and turn them into kinfolk. The Get holds the line long enough for them to do that and do other CoG things, like planting Glades and opening homeless shelters. The Get are not the CoG. They are trained as soon as possible to be a berserking wall of fang, claw, and muscle. To be specialists in way THEY focus on the war against the Wyrm and Weaver. The differences between the CoG and the Get are the Nation's strengths, just like the differences between a medic and a commando are a military's strength. If the Get gave up their unique focus, the Garou as a whole would be diminished.<br /> <br /> Do you not have the muscle to cleave your foe in half, the stamina to take sledgehammer to the face and not even blink, the Rage to throw yourself into the maw of a thunderwyrm so you can tear its throat out from the inside even as you die, or the speed to kill four banes before anyone can blink? The CoG or the Gnawers are right over there, waiting to take you in. Grab a shovel and start planting gardens in your cities, in between going on your own hunts for wyrm spawn. Or the Black Furies, who would love to give the chest thumping braggarts in the Get a middle finger and a smirk behind your back while giving you a hug. The Get are the full time FIGHT/KILL/DIE Tribe of Garou. Their standards are the way they are, because you need to come to the Tribe physically and mentally equipped to do the job that they focus all of their Tribe's time and identity and pride on. Otherwise, why do you even want to join?<br /> <br /> Also, just being born a human, and in a decidedly unequal world, lays down the groundwork for an unjust society. We all have the responsibility to create equity where we can, but just because a type of organization might be more prone to creating injustice than another, that doesn't actually necessitate that they are evil or unnecessary. Take jobs, like the ones that existed during the olden days like lumberjacking or coal mining (the way they were done back in the 1800s rather than now). There you had hideous injuries, poverty, death, and sickness were common, resulting from the circumstances they had to create and perpetuate by building the mines and clearing the woodland and so on. That doesn't mean these things were unnecessary at the time, even if the environment was likely to create more toxicity than, say, a university campus. These atmospheres had the potential to, and usually did, become toxic due to the misfortunes and hardships they dealt with. This in turn helped create toxic masculine mindsets like &quot;real men don't need to read&quot; or &quot;real men settle things with their fists.&quot; However, just because these places could potentially be a breeding ground for toxic mind sets doesn't mean they were not necessary or even good for society at the time. All it means is introspection is harder, because of the magnitude and nature of distractions you have around you.<br /> <br /> Garou live even harder lives. The Get, seeing just how dark things can be in their world, and who have been fighting a horrifying war for thousands upon thousands of years, live even harder ones, as they strive not to just chase off wyrm creatures, but to annihilate them wherever they can, with less regard to the danger than other Tribes. They see the world dying, and they strive to be the ideal warrior that Gaia needs and who, according to their legends, Great Fenris actually was. They are of the most perfect, invincible warrior Gaia ever had, and so they desperately try to follow the example of Great Fenris. And they get results, just like the CoG. Sadly, just like the CoG, it is not enough. But the Get's way of doing things is just as valid as splitting your time between fighting the wyrm directly and diplomacy and kindness towards others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478722#post1478722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty sure the Ratkin, Bastet, and Nagah would beg to differ that the Garou are the exclusive killers in the name of Gaia. Even plenty of shifters that don't see killing as a major part of their duties, are still just as capable of being killers as those that do (like the Rokea and Gurahl).</div> </div> </div> </div>Those were not their Gaia assigned roles. Or not the way they are to the Garou. Gaia made the Ratkin to cull humans. The Nagah to watch, judge, and if need be execute individual Fera. The Garou were created to be her wrecking ball. They exist to remind the cosmos that no one screws with Gaia. That is their purpose. Bastet find secrets. That is the REASON the living spirit of the entire WORLD made them. What the Fera do on their own time is their own business as long as it does not distract from the meaning of their lives. This isn't supposition. The authors in and out of game tell us WHY this or that splat was created. Heck, each of their splat books go into deep detail EXPLAINING why any particular splat was given the gift of existence by Gaia, and what she wants back from them. <br /> <br /> EDIT: If you want proof that their purposes are real, just look at the extinct Fera, and notice how the world is dying for a lack of them and their roles going unfulfilled. The Changing Breeds book even talked about the confusion of the Garou turning on them, IIRC, because the Garou did not have their purpose or their tools to do their appointed jobs. <br /> <br /> Last thought before I go to bed: I am pretty sure that the magic that gets the Garou nation, a nation of beings that are dying due to attrition, a lot of their new babies is also a big part of why Garou who have Pure Breed are auto respected. Remember, Pure Breed is a thing that they can feel. It is a thing of spirit. Just like the real, physical reality of how men and women are different can be unfair at times, the fantasy, metaphysical reality is also unfair. You and your mom or dad did all sorts of cool things when they were alive and became heroes? Your kids will get special blessing that will ensure that the rest of the Garou instinctively treats them extra well when you are gone. Yay! In the real world, magical bloodlines are racist hogwash. In THEIR world, it is just reality, like the way metis are punished for the sins of their parents. The Shadow Lords have Pure Breed, but insist they don't really care about it. The GW and BG don't even have it. And yet, no matter how much they like to think they are enlightened and evolved past such notions as to care about who you were born of, that doesn't mean that it doesn't work on them. Even BSDs can theoretically have it, (as throwbacks) and I believe get the bonuses for it. The Get did not invent this system. But they DO have a system where you can get respect if you weren't born with any special backgrounds, and that is by proving to them that you BELONG with the Get. Like all Tribes, the Get have their own unique focus on how to fight the wyrm. Like all Tribes, they respect results.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 04-12-2022, 11:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-12T19:33:26-07:00","id":1478732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478726#post1478726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I liked the Silver Fangs cause they had that old world old money charm. I didn\u2019t really like the Talons because in spite of liking both WtA and WtF (though I\u2019m much more familiar with WtA) I\u2019m not really into wolves as rl animals.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think my sister's dog is a Talon. He is frighteningly smart, seems to understand everything we say, and has a real preference for human flesh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 04-12-2022, 10:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-12T23:06:58-07:00","id":1478739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478731#post1478731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is just as valid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then how can you consider the Get definition non-arbitrary? That's something you have not addressed at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Get holds the line long enough for them to do that and do other CoG things, like planting Glades and opening homeless shelters. </div> </div> </div>The important thing here, is while this might be the effect the Get have, it is not <b>why</b> they do what they do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They are trained as soon as possible to be a berserking wall of fang, claw, and muscle. </div> </div> </div>So, are we talking about the Tribe in the books, or some hyper stereotyped version of them that makes their 1e material look like a masterwork of nuance?<br /> <br /> First off, the Get have all five Auspices, they're not all Ahrouns. They're not all meant to be frontline fighters. Get Theurges are still healers and spirit mediators. Fenrir Philodoxes are still thoughtful seekers of truth and justice. Even otheir Ahrouns are expected to learn how to lead during fights and become generals; not become the ultimate raging grunt.<br /> <br /> Second, the Get are very aware that regardless of their pride and training, the rest of the Tribes have their own specialists in fighting even if the other Tribes are a bit happier to leave more of it to the Ahrouns. They know they're not special forces dealing with civilians, at best (for them) they're special forces dealing with other soldiers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the Get gave up their unique focus, the Garou as a whole would be diminished. </div> </div> </div>I've been playing the game too long to buy that. The Get aren't actually that much better than any other combat focused Garou. I've played a Child of Gaia that regularly handed Fenrir their asses in sparring matches. One of the reasons I call cutting out the Get a &quot;safe&quot; move on Paradox's part (and why I feel the same way about the Red Talons) is that they're actually redundant. All the Tribes have excellent fighters, so a Tribe focused on martial strength isn't really adding anything. All the Tribes (even the Urrah ones) have lupus to give a wolf's perspective on things, so the Red Talons don't add much there either.<br /> <br /> Their stubborn approaches are part of the problem. Green Berets don't work as a unit without regular military behind them. If all the Green Berets died tomorrow, the US military's combat readiness wouldn't change. If the entire US military turned into fully trained Green Berets tomorrow, the whole DoD would be fucked. Special forces soldiers that want to be effective understand that they're part of a larger machine no matter how much more elite their units are. The Get don't respect the other Tribes the same way. That lack of respect does more damage to the Garou Nation and its war efforts as a whole than the Fenrir's combat prowess could ever add (to be clear, I'm not talking about numbers, just the Tribal philosophy, obviously losing hundreds of Garou would be worse).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Otherwise, why do you even want to join? </div> </div> </div>Um... because it's a Tribe? Most of the Tribes are familial oriented organizations; that's why the name is fitting. There's a huge pressure to join your family's Tribe even if it's not a great fit for you (esp. if your Tribe is Pure Breed accessible). It takes a lot to be born and raised into Get life and then pick a different Tribe. The Tribes also have pressure to keep members born into their Tribes in instead of chasing them off. Only Lost Cubs can really be given the kind of consideration you're talking about here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We all have the responsibility to create equity where we can, but just because a type of organization might be more prone to creating injustice than another, that doesn't actually necessitate that they are evil or unnecessary. </div> </div> </div>I said individuals are morally culpable to the consequences of the injustices their actions have allowed to happen due to the inequities their organizations promoted. I never called the Get evil or unnecessary (yes I did just call them redundant though). My claim is that the Get aren't off the hook just for wiping out the Swords, because everything that let the Swords fester within the Tribe is still there, and thus nothing is going to prevent a new version of the Swords from sprouting among their ranks. Killing the Swords was (or should have been considering the thread) the start of reforming the Fenrir, not the end.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That doesn't mean these things were unnecessary at the time, even if the environment was likely to create more toxicity than, say, a university campus. </div> </div> </div>This use of the concept of necessity doesn't work for me. No coal mine has ever been abstractly and objectively &quot;necessary.&quot; Coal mines were and are now only &quot;necessary&quot; to plans that rely on burning coal for power. Universities are similarly only necessary in the context of a situation where higher learning and education is an essential aspect of a large goal designed by actual people. There has never been a coal mine that was &quot;needed&quot; outside of the context of humans deciding on a slew of other priorities that required coal as a power source that balanced power output and speed of mining to achieve. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This in turn helped create toxic masculine mindsets like &quot;real men don't need to read&quot; or &quot;real men settle things with their fists.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Yet again, your chronology is baffling. There is ample evidence of such toxic masculinity that well predates the industrial revolution and the jobs it created. You're not inherently wrong on how civilization creating specialist jobs created the basis for toxic masculinity, but that goes back to the agricultural revolution (which is, in the WtA context, when the Weaver ensnared humanity and started tying us down to settlements and we lost track of our older ways of living...).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, just because these places could potentially be a breeding ground for toxic mind sets doesn't mean they were not necessary or even good for society at the time. All it means is introspection is harder, because of the magnitude and nature of distractions you have around you. </div> </div> </div>And? Even if Get philosophy was ever a net positive for Garou society in the past, you've yet to make a particular case for them being a net positive for the Garou in the present W20 to W5 metaplot limbo (aka not the end of Revised with the Apocalypse hitting).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Get, seeing just how dark things can be in their world, and who have been fighting a horrifying war for thousands upon thousands of years, live even harder ones, as they strive not to just chase off wyrm creatures, but to annihilate them wherever they can, with less regard to the danger than other Tribes. </div> </div> </div>I fail to see how fighting stupidly compared to the other Tribes is something in the Get's favor. If anything, this is the perfect argument for the Fenrir being the Tribe to fall. Who was the Tribe that fell before them? The White Howlers. Why? Because they did exactly what you're saying and chasing the Wyrm to the point of stupid tactics in the name of annihilating the enemy just lead them straight down the Spiral.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the Get's way of doing things is just as valid as splitting your time between fighting the wyrm directly and diplomacy and kindness towards others. </div> </div> </div>Again, this just speaks poorly of the Get. The CoG aren't dividing their time. They're fighting the Wyrm in a place the combat happy Get can't hope to reach: people's hearts. Humans that hate empower Banes and make the Wyrm stronger. All the time spent reducing hate via understanding is, in fact, still fighting the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> This is why I find the &quot;ideal warrior&quot; argument so unconvincing as to the importance of the Fenrir. Every Garou is born with the potential to be a skilled fighter, but they've known for thousands of years that the Wyrm (and the Weaver) isn't an enemy you can just claw into submission. It's an insidious force that needs to be combated everywhere it dwells, not just by killing Wyrm creatures. Ideal warriors are adaptable to their enemies, not hard set in their tactics. Ask a Red Talon if the best hunters treat all prey like deer, or if the pack needs to use different hunting approaches for different prey.<br /> <br /> Going back to that whole special forces thing? One of the key skills in a lot of the US special forces is diplomacy. Special forces are frequently tasked with finding and recruiting friendly allies in enemy territory to obtain intel and supplies to aid the larger war effort. I really don't think you appreciate how much modern special forces have reprioritized things like language skills and cultural integration over high marksmanship scores (and that's with US special forces always having a strong bias towards non-combat specialists with good combat skills). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Those were not their Gaia assigned roles. </div> </div> </div>Whether or not Gaia assigned roles is not a settled issue. All of the shifters have strengths and weaknesses. A lot of them like to claim those strengths and weakness are signs of divine duty assigned to them (and not all of them say it was Gaia that gave them their jobs), but the facts in evidence are that Gaia was either really bad at this whole &quot;assigned everyone duties&quot; thing, or that's a lot more wishful thinking on the shifters' parts that's influenced by things like how they're shaped by their intermediary patron spirits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gaia made the Ratkin to cull humans. </div> </div> </div>Then why were the Garou doing that for so long? Did the Garou really manage to do the Ratkin's job for thousands of years and Gaia, the divine assigner of jobs, not bother to say anything about that? Or maybe &quot;keep humanity in check,&quot; was always supposed to be a group activity they shared?<br /> <br /> Also &quot;culling humans&quot; means the Ratkin are good at killing. Culling is killing. Killing thus is not just a Garou specialty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Nagah to watch, judge, and if need be execute individual Fera. </div> </div> </div>Executioners also need to be good killers; especially ones that are also the judge and jury and don't expect their targets to be brought to them for punishment..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Garou were created to be her wrecking ball. They exist to remind the cosmos that no one screws with Gaia. That is their purpose. </div> </div> </div>According to who?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bastet find secrets. </div> </div> </div>Hrm. Isn't that the Corax (and formerly the Camazotz) job? The Bastet guard secrets, with violence when necessary. Maybe Helios and Luna/Selene got their wires crossed or something?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That is the REASON the living spirit of the entire WORLD made them. </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure the books have made of point of Gaia never actually saying this to any of the changing breeds. They're told their purpose from their more direct spiritual patrons who may or may not say it's Gaia's purpose for them.<br /> <br /> Also the Ananasi are pretty clear (and their writers are very clear) that they weren't created by Gaia. The Kitsune were Luna's idea and Gaia supposedly didn't even have a purpose for them to the point of almost not making them because the original fox managed to get on the all loving Gaia's shit list for pointing out that the foxes were free to do what they wanted because they weren't worth giving a job to. When one of the shifter's has a &quot;job&quot; of &quot;IDEK, come back to me later,&quot; it should cause one to question how much you're reading the in-game fiction as out-of-game setting fact (which is annoying, because the WoD books are generally very bad at designating the two for you).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you want proof that their purposes are real, just look at the extinct Fera, and notice how the world is dying for a lack of them and their roles going unfulfilled. </div> </div> </div>Just because someone needs to be doing something for a healthy environment and has a natural talent for it doesn't prove that a creator deity specifically handed out the job to them.<br /> <br /> Gaia is dying for a lot of reasons; the multiple wars her children and her allies' children have fought against it each other means her forces are depleted regardless of assigned roles. If ten Apis were still alive, it would be a drop in the bucket of all the problems the Gaian forces have facing them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the real world, magical bloodlines are racist hogwash. In THEIR world, it is just reality, like the way metis are punished for the sins of their parents. </div> </div> </div>It's still racist hogwash, just racist hogwash with better in-universe PR. The very fact that it's magical, but also kinda biological, means it's a corrupt system.<br /> <br /> Also, the games are written the way they are for a reason. Pure Breed is unfair (also it's a bad mechanic which is a separate issue) because the game wants class and race conflicts represented in Garou society. The fantasy part of this is playing characters that can fight for a better world despite how shitty the WoD is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And yet, no matter how much they like to think they are enlightened and evolved past such notions as to care about who you were born of, that doesn't mean that it doesn't work on them. </div> </div> </div>Huh? The GWs and BGs hate that Pure Breed still works on them It's not something they're proud to not have, it's something they don't get because the spirits decided to screw them for doing work nobody else would do. No Gnawer is sitting around honestly thinking that they're better because they don't have Pure Breed. Pure Breed is just another way the Garou Nation treats them like shit for being the &quot;omega&quot; Tribe even though they're one of the most vital to the Garou actually winning the war because they can master the city without becoming Weaver freaks like the GWs. The Urrah Tribes might be smug about just how much they can do without needing to rely on magical ancestor power ups, but they'd much rather have access to all the toys instead of being stuck with less (esp. since it would make it easier for them to change the system instead of having to rely on the CoGs and their Pure Breed to do deal with high Pure Beed traditionalists)..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Get did not invent this system. But they DO have a system where you can get respect if you weren't born with any special backgrounds, and that is by proving to them that you BELONG with the Get. </div> </div> </div>And that system is still biased to favor those with the special backgrounds, which then diminishes the idea that the Get are actually just focused on results. The Get didn't invent the system, but they also didn't invent a system where results are what really matters, because those born with special backgrounds can get a leg up on those that get equal or even greater results if they play their privilege right.<br /> <br /> The Get system is like a school where how much money your family donates improves your grades. No student can get more than 100%, but if you luck into the right family, and they support you, you get +X% added to everything. So some students get test at 75%, but their grades are recorded at 100% anyway. Sure, kids that don't have that kind of luck could get 100% if they manage to never ever screw up, but most likely even if they're regularly doing better than 75%, their recorded grades aren't 100%, so they're ranked lower.<br /> <br /> The Get don't have to engage with that (the Shadow Lords actually do try to get around it because it's good training for dealing with pesky high Pure Breed Silver Fangs to know how to even the playing field, even if they're not going to pass up using Pure Breed if they have it because they really want results, not getting stymied by other Tribes' Pure Breed), but they continue to do so.<br /> <br /> Some Get have to work harder to prove they belong with the Get than others. It's not just results and personal merits.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-13T00:35:32-07:00","id":1478742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478739#post1478739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off, the Get have all five Auspices, they're not all Ahrouns. They're not all meant to be frontline fighters. Get Theurges are still healers and spirit mediators. Fenrir Philodoxes are still thoughtful seekers of truth and justice. Even otheir Ahrouns are expected to learn how to lead during fights and become generals; not become the ultimate raging grunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. Still, all auspices value &quot;strength&quot; and that makes them relatively good fighters. So even the rotagar and godi might be on the same level as average garou of other tribes when it comes to combat prowess.<br /> That said, it is also stated, that &quot;strength&quot; for the Gets isn't limited to how hard they punch. It also relates to endurance, conviction/faith, stubbornness (in some instances), general health, being free of mental impairments, among other things.<br /> <br /> What good is a Get who waivers in the face of the enemy or falls to the whispers of the Wyrm?<br /> <br /> 1st Edition TB, for all it's flaws, stated that Get education is harsh, but that it aims to build character. It is not the way of the Get to beat their cubs into submission so they will do their push ups and marathon runs before breakfast. Such educational approaches would only make them cowardly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478739#post1478739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure the books have made of point of Gaia never actually saying this to any of the changing breeds. They're told their purpose from their more direct spiritual patrons who may or may not say it's Gaia's purpose for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Kitsune legend from the Hegeyokai sourcebook has their legendary founder present when Gaia and Luna discuss their duty and thereby mention the other duties of the other breeds. Since the first kutsune might technically still be alive, this legend could be an eyewitness report.<br /> <br /> But, you are right, the duties are part of oral tradition and mythology and not necessarily something that is set in stone. Especially since times change and so can the opinions even of Celestines.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-13T01:11:58-07:00","id":1478743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478742#post1478742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, it is also stated, that &quot;strength&quot; for the Gets isn't limited to how hard they punch.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was kind of part of my point yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Kitsune legend from the Hegeyokai sourcebook has their legendary founder present when Gaia and Luna discuss their duty and thereby mention the other duties of the other breeds. Since the first kutsune might technically still be alive, this legend could be an eyewitness report. </div> </div> </div>Considering that legend includes that she's such a trickster and liar that it leads to the whole &quot;Gaia got royally pissed at her,&quot; thing, even if you could ask her you probably wouldn't get a reliable answer anyway. Of course, there's the whole thing where there even is a &quot;legendary founder&quot; as a specific individual. The Kitsune legend suggests heavily that the shifters exist in some way before Gaia picked a duty for them and empowered them into what they are now. Or at least the Kitsune are a giant exception to things (which is also heavily hinted at anyway).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-13T01:15:25-07:00","id":1478744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478739#post1478739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some Get have to work harder to prove they belong with the Get than others. It's not just results and personal merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ethan Skemp once pointed out, that Pure Breed is tribal specific and actually makes a garou a paragon of the tribal virtues. So, this might be a chicken/egg-situation depending on what you believe pure breed is.<br /> <br /> If it is a combination of mythical and biological 'traits' that were determined when papa's sperm combined with mama's egg to form what eventually becomes the garou, that just gives you social bonuses but does nothing else, then that is one approach that is supported by RAW. But, looking at W20, there is considerable peer pressure for those garou to live up to the Pure Breed and you are frowned upon, if you don't.<br /> <br /> What does that mean, is the difficulty raised for you are frowned upon, but you still get bonus dice? Seems that way, right?<br /> W20 also states you loose Pure Breed if you do not join the tribe of the ancestry. I think ROI is, that you also loose it, when you change your tribe by Rite of Adoption or dancing the spiral, later. It attributes the Tribal Totem with removing Pure Breed, what I find an unnecessary clarification close to godly intervention, that should, imo, just have been &quot;the trait decreases until it's gone&quot;.<br /> <br /> My point being, that the society molds the Pure Breed character into being a paragon of the tribal virtues, because it is what they expect and the garou will know. This of course is a more difficult approach since W20 doesn't allow to easily discern between garou and kin in pre-change kids. So, all the character building and tribal society forming the pure breed garou into his role has to be limited to post-change cub education and possibly well into the cliath rank.<br /> <br /> IMO, W20 should not only have pointed out, that the NPCs expect from the garou with high pure breed to act a certain way, but that the player who chooses pure breed for their character should have that ambition for the way the character is played, too.<br /> And while the purest of a generation, Arkady, went astry for a while, this should not be the norm or an desirable character concept within WtA.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-13T01:37:05-07:00","id":1478745,"title":"","content":"Personally I always liked purebred, largely due to running jokes about my glossy glossy hair and suggesting it as a background for other supernaturals but still....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-13T03:19:35-07:00","id":1478752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478744#post1478744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ethan Skemp once pointed out, that Pure Breed is tribal specific and actually makes a garou a paragon of the tribal virtues. So, this might be a chicken/egg-situation depending on what you believe pure breed is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pure Breed debates go back three or four versions of the Onyx Path/White Wolf forums.<br /> <br /> Here's the problem with your supposition: when Pure Breed kicks in.<br /> <br /> Pure Breed is determined at birth (with some vague talk of it possibly going up or down if you really do something notable in the eyes of the spirits but with no real examples and lots of things that don't seem to have mattered that set the bars pretty high/low), but has no mechanical effect until being initiated into a Tribe. But according to the books it kicks in, in full, at that moment. Once a Get succeeds in their Initiation Rite, their PB (whatever it maybe) starts working full force. That's why it's a mix of biology and spirit. So it's Fenris, not Tribal elders, that has signifies how much the breeding counts towards the individual Fenrir being a paragon of the Tribe.<br /> <br /> Which, as you note with an example like Arkady, doesn't really make a lot of sense if they go off the rails at some point. If a PB 5 character does something completely contrary to Tribal virtues, their paragon status is (in no mechanically enforced way) is tarnished but the mechanical effects are still in full force. If the books aimed to be consistent, either such actions should lower PB, or the Tribes should be forced to reconsider what their virtues are if their Totem continues to be OK with such behavior. Both options are technically possible, but ultimately so vaguely defined that it's just ST fiat on what happens, if anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...that just gives you social bonuses but does nothing else,... </div> </div> </div>And bonus dice to formal challenges, which is socially oriented because that's how Garou politics tend to get settled, but trails by gamecraft or combat can benefit from PB dice too.<br /> <br /> As for what W20 should have done? It should have wildly redone the Background. Some of us lobbied heavily during the W20 corebook open dev period to not repeat the mistake of V20 doing the Generation Background exactly like it used to be. Ultimately the devs opted to adjust the wording a bit but kept the mechanics the same.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-13T04:07:16-07:00","id":1478753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478752#post1478752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... but has no mechanical effect until being initiated into a Tribe. But according to the books it kicks in, in full, at that moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that explicitly stated?<br /> WtA books, except for entertaining the idea of doing character preludes, usually don't go into detail about being a cub and if this has mechanical differences...<br /> <br /> I mean, it makes sense, for the fact that there is a tribal aspect to pure breed. But it doesn't make sense that with the Rite of passage it would go from zero to hundred (or to five <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) in an instant.<br /> <br /> I believe there should be some middle ground. Baby Arkady should not get five bonus dice for crying when the diaper is full.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478752#post1478752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pure Breed debates go back three or four versions of the Onyx Path/White Wolf forums.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I remember.<br /> But I always find new approaches and ideas to the topic when new discussions arise. For, it works quite differently in the head canon of a lot one players/STs...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478752#post1478752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why it's a mix of biology and spirit. So it's Fenris, not Tribal elders, that has signifies how much the breeding counts towards the individual Fenrir being a paragon of the Tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I don't like that W20 addition, for it can lead to the conclusion that Pure Breed, much like tribal membership, is god given. Or Totem given, if you will. But that is not the case, or doesn't make sense in the broader context of the game. It is garou who decide whom to educate into their tribe and send to the rite of passage. It is also garou who perform punishment Rites to throw someone out (or Adoption Rites or what ever else might change or end tribal membership). And sure, Tribal Totems have a an option to intervene, that is a given. But they aren't onipresent, all-knowing or have knowledge of the future. As Incarnae they should not engage in micromanaging their tribe and it should not foster a situation in which garou would delegate their responsibilities for their brethren and culture to the Totem. Totem involvement should be an option used for story driven purposes.<br /> <br /> For me, it makes more sense, if pure breed is fate, happenstance, not completely random but much like breeding true a probability game. Ancestry furthers the changes of having pure breed, as per the books, obviously. But there is not power that grants it or rules over it, it simply is. With the option of being gradually developed between birth and first-change.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478752#post1478752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which, as you note with an example like Arkady, doesn't really make a lot of sense if they go off the rails at some point. If a PB 5 character does something completely contrary to Tribal virtues, their paragon status is (in no mechanically enforced way) is tarnished but the mechanical effects are still in full force. If the books aimed to be consistent, either such actions should lower PB, or the Tribes should be forced to reconsider what their virtues are if their Totem continues to be OK with such behaviour. Both options are technically possible, but ultimately so vaguely defined that it's just ST fiat on what happens, if anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>True.<br /> As for Arkady, he redeemed himself, possibly, depending on how you judge his actions after Silver Crown. Also, his deeds prior to and during Silver Crown were never publicly known - just that Albrecht banished him from House Wyrmfoe territory, iirc.<br /> Even the deed for which the european garou want to put him on trail is circumstantial. He exercises control over a Thunderwyrm, allowing a fellow garou to flee. While the garou suggest foul play, the deed is not necessarily against Falcon's Ways.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478752#post1478752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And bonus dice to formal challenges, which is socially oriented because that's how Garou politics tend to get settled, but trails by gamecraft or combat can benefit from PB dice too.</div> </div> </div> </div>True and not really well defined. Is in a formal combat challenge each roll subject to Pure Breed Bonus?<br /> Damage rolls?<br /> Soak solls?<br /> The roll to channel Rage if incapacitated?<br /> Is 'Lunas Armour' more powerful for Pure Breed characters if used in a Klaive Duell as opposed to regular combat?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478752#post1478752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for what W20 should have done? It should have wildly redone the Background. Some of us lobbied heavily during the W20 corebook open dev period to not repeat the mistake of V20 doing the Generation Background exactly like it used to be. Ultimately the devs opted to adjust the wording a bit but kept the mechanics the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly.<br /> But I really don't have a better mechanic in mind myself. I would change the description and possibly try to aim for a clarification in the whole &quot;formal challenge&quot; situation...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 04-13-2022, 07:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-13T11:28:02-07:00","id":1478782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478718#post1478718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My bro is a Marine. His branch of the military like to say they are the strongest of the strong, but that doesn't mean he believes in oppressing the weak.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Marines see themselves as an elite, and the &quot;every Marine is a rifleman&quot; is part of that ethos. In my own depiction of the Get of Fenris tribe, I base them heavily as that. The Get of Fenris see themselves as elite warriors of the Garou Nation, and want every auspice to be functional like an Ahroun in other tribes (they do have many useful combat gifts as Tribal gifts after all). It's just that THEIR ahrouns are more like special forces (ideally).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478718#post1478718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Problem: physical power means a LOT in battle when you are typically fighting the same way your elders did 10,000 years ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>More than any connection to Nazis (even the first edition corebook that mentioned a small faction of the Get embraced this, mentioned it as a PROBLEM. And the first edition Players Guide further designated them as a problem. This was meant primarily as antagonists, and every tribe had some camp in them that was meant to be antagonists), I thought the supposed Get oppression of women to be a problem. It didn't make sense to me since in general the ancient Germanic and Nordic peoples were known for their women to be much more equal to men than the Classical civilizations. (I think the game designers eventually realized this, as this was downplayed heavily in second edition and ignored in Revised. It's really just an early first edition thing.)<br /> <br /> But it did make sense that a tribal culture that prized physical excellence would be tough on Garou who lacked sufficient physical strength. And while in terms of game mechanics, a female PC is not disadvantaged to a male PC - anyone can decide to make their character have 5 Strength or whatever - in terms of setting, this is not the case. Since human females have less upper body strength than males on average, it would make sense that there'd be a higher number of female NPCs that &quot;wash out&quot; as cubs because they can't meet the physical standards of the tribe. So I used that as the basis of &quot;the Get discriminate against women&quot;. But this was only based on the Get insisting on high upper body strength. The other tribes may not like a cub who is physically weak, but it is not a deal breaker for them. But at a first glance, the results of the Get's standards would create the impression that they are rejecting more women as members as discrimination due to their sex.<br /> <br /> We rarely see any NPCs who only have a Strength (or any other stat) of 1. But as &quot;Below Average&quot;, anywhere from a third to half of the population should have that as a stat. Even if you argue that among Garou, that would be lessened, there is still going to be a fair number of people with lack that strength. And a higher proportion of them are more likely to be women. So these are the Get cubs who end up going to other tribes. And certainly a group like the Black Furies, who are equally aggressive and militant as the Get, would see potential in these rejected cubs and see this as shortsighted, stupid, and prejudicial. It's just like how the Marines rejected Audie Murphy because he was too underweight so Murphy joined the Army and became the highest decorated US soldier in WWII for bravery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-13T13:25:17-07:00","id":1478790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478753#post1478753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that explicitly stated?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but there's no other coherent conclusion to make from the collection of other statements. Anything other than &quot;0 to 5&quot; would contradict something, while &quot;0 to 5&quot; doesn't.<br /> <br /> Also.. you don't need to keep telling me how much Pure Breed doesn't make sense. I've been saying that on the official forums for as long as I've been on them. I'm just trying to engage with what we have and how it applies to where the conversation is going.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, I don't like that W20 addition, for it can lead to the conclusion that Pure Breed, much like tribal membership, is god given. Or Totem given, if you will. </div> </div> </div>That was a Revised clarification in the ST Handbook FAQ, not a W20 addition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I really don't have a better mechanic in mind myself. I would change the description and possibly try to aim for a clarification in the whole &quot;formal challenge&quot; situation... </div> </div> </div>Try this out:<br /> <br /> 1) Pure Breed ceases to be its own trait. Instead it is an in-universe concept that's a side effect of Garou that have/that have high ratings in other Traits. The more of these Traits, and the higher they are if rated, the more a given Garou tends to have Garou children, and the more their kin children tend to have Garou children as well. These Traits include, but are not limited to: Renown greater than the character needs to qualify for Elder, Rank, Spirit Heritage, Garou Heritage, Fate, any mental or social Merits that represent inner strength or conviction, any Merit rated 5 for higher. Effectively Garou culture has a causation vs. correlation issue where the concept of Pure Breeding mistakes the correlation of these traits with &quot;breeding true&quot; for there being a causal relationship between controlled breeding and seeing these traits manifest more often.<br /> <br /> 2) Pure Breed is replaced by the Garou Heritage Background. Garou Heritage represents well known Garou heroes (or maybe even extrarordinary kinfolk) in the character's lineage. This heritage provides a -2 difficulty bonus to all social rolls not including Gift activation or Rites when dealing with Garou that identify with those past heroes, and a -1 difficulty bonus to those familiar with their stories. The character's rating in this Background determines how well known their ancestor's exploits are, from adored officers of their birth Sept that are unknown to most of the Nation at 1, to the greatest heroes in Garou history that everyone in their Tribe endeavors to aspire to, and ever Garou of any Tribe has head of at 5.<br /> <br /> 3) New Supernatural Merit: Tribal Paragon (1 pt). A character's Garou Heritage is recognized by their Tribal Totem, who has high hopes for the character and creates great expectations for them. They gain an effective Spirit Heritage rating in their Tribal Totem's brood equal to half their Garou Heritage rounded up as long as they remain members of the Tribe in good standing. Any time the character would lose Renown, increase the loss by 1 temporary Renown of the most appropriate type. This Merit can only be taken if the character joins the Tribe of their most recent Garou ancestor. It usually manifests during the Rite of Initiation, but any loyal member of the Tribe with heroic lineage might find themselves blessed after an act of high Tribal virtue.<br /> <br /> 4) Optional: Garou Heritage is only Restricted for Silver Fangs, who have to take it. Any Tribe that was formerly Restricted from Pure Breed is now Discouraged for Garou Heritage (even Bone Gnawers can have legendary parents). Tribal Paragon is not available to Tribes that are Garou Heritage Discouraged (Rat still doesn't give a shit who your parents were).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478782#post1478782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it did make sense that a tribal culture that prized physical excellence would be tough on Garou who lacked sufficient physical strength.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really don't like the oversimplification of this as presented.<br /> <br /> For example, the recent group of women athletes that were banned from international competitions in racing (not a measure of upper body strength) for having abnormally high testosterone for women; despite that being celebrated for men like Usain Bolt. We live in a world where women that luck into the genetic lottery for a specific sport get classified as non-women for competition (but not as men either) because woman aren't allowed to have physical prowess that's too good and still be women.<br /> <br /> Gender does not define your genetics. And genetics are a lot more complicated than XY vs XX.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-13T17:53:51-07:00","id":1478812,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve never really liked the idea that the GoF were misogynistic. I don\u2019t object to having factions that are, but I don\u2019t think that the GoF would be and I don\u2019t think that there should be a particularly high level of gender based animosity within the GoF. I feel like it\u2019s another example of some people (including authors) oversimplifying and stereotyping the supposedly \u201cright wing\u201d Tribe.<br /> <br /> Now, if we assume standard levels of realistic human sexual dimorphism among werewolves, then male Get should make up the majority of the Tribe\u2019s warrior elites, then again so should the Ahrouns, and once you add in Gifts you can have plenty of female warrior Get who are forced to be reckoned with. Assuming the Get have an extremely militaristic culture, then both males and females would be trained to fight from a young age, made to endure strenuous exercise and physical trials, and pushed to achieve their full fighting potential or die trying. Even without Gifts or shape changing, a human woman growing up in that culture would be a formidable opponent for a man who had a more relaxed upbringing and lifestyle.<br /> <br /> I imagine the female Get buying into their Tribe\u2019s own macho chauvinism, not wanting to be members of a weakling Tribe just because it\u2019s a girl\u2019s only club.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1