ith their stories. The character's rating in this Background determines how well known their ancestor's exploits are, from adored officers of their birth Sept that are unknown to most of the Nation at 1, to the greatest heroes in Garou history that everyone in their Tribe endeavors to aspire to, and ever Garou of any Tribe has head of at 5.<br /> <br /> 3) New Supernatural Merit: Tribal Paragon (1 pt). A character's Garou Heritage is recognized by their Tribal Totem, who has high hopes for the character and creates great expectations for them. They gain an effective Spirit Heritage rating in their Tribal Totem's brood equal to half their Garou Heritage rounded up as long as they remain members of the Tribe in good standing. Any time the character would lose Renown, increase the loss by 1 temporary Renown of the most appropriate type. This Merit can only be taken if the character joins the Tribe of their most recent Garou ancestor. It usually manifests during the Rite of Initiation, but any loyal member of the Tribe with heroic lineage might find themselves blessed after an act of high Tribal virtue.<br /> <br /> 4) Optional: Garou Heritage is only Restricted for Silver Fangs, who have to take it. Any Tribe that was formerly Restricted from Pure Breed is now Discouraged for Garou Heritage (even Bone Gnawers can have legendary parents). Tribal Paragon is not available to Tribes that are Garou Heritage Discouraged (Rat still doesn't give a shit who your parents were).<br /> etics. And genetics are a lot more complicated than XY vs XX.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a bit of book keeping, but I like it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-14T02:09:22-07:00","id":1478833,"title":"","content":"While drifting very far into the tangent, what do you see as extra bookkeeping here? #1 isn't meant to be some mechanic like the Pure Breed percent chances of having a Garou kid that were in some of the books. Just the traits that the Garou think designate someone of pure breeding that is likely to have lots of Garou kids down the line, with no actual hard numbers or anything to back that up. Just enough observations to be plausible that it could be true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-14T02:19:00-07:00","id":1478834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478833#post1478833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While drifting very far into the tangent, what do you see as extra bookkeeping here? #1 isn't meant to be some mechanic like the Pure Breed percent chances of having a Garou kid that were in some of the books. Just the traits that the Garou think designate someone of pure breeding that is likely to have lots of Garou kids down the line, with no actual hard numbers or anything to back that up. Just enough observations to be plausible that it could be true.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I read #1 as still being a numerical value that is calculated...<br /> <br /> At character creation you would have to check for all the things that would factor in Pure Breed and you would need to keep in mind to update it when permanent renown and rank change within the game. This happens rarely enough, that it might be forgotten, but then again, players have an incentive to remind the ST <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-18T07:36:44-07:00","id":1479080,"title":"","content":"Get sometimes assaulted other caerns to take them from other tribes to ,, better defend sacred places&quot;. Maby that makes them main antagonists in retribution but not in rpg<br /> Besides there was a difficulty to chose get as tribe in hearth of the forrest. First signes of abandoning fenris in wod?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-25T06:23:38-07:00","id":1479484,"t