sts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-25T09:54:00-07:00","id":1479489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1479484#post1479484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great. Now that I know that there's no salvaging 5th edition, I can comfortably look forward to a 6th edition where none of 5th is canon.</div> </div> </div> </div>From your lips, to God's ears...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2582-gangrel44","name":"Gangrel44","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-25T16:20:29-07:00","id":1479514,"title":"","content":"From all the options, they took the dumbest. Second most obvious and dumbest.<br /> <br /> They could have done it with the Red Talons. It would be stupid and obvious, but at least would be the most sensible choice (aside the actual most sensible choice of not ditching a tribe that way and adding nuance where they needed it). They could have done it with Young Brother and make space to better work Natives through the other tribes and/or deepen Old Brother. They could have done it with any other tribe and at least get creative explaining it away.<br /> <br /> Instead, they got the easy WP-like target (as if the other didn't had WP variations all over the place, directly or by proxy).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-26T04:57:28-07:00","id":1479539,"title":"","content":"I'm starting to think some people at the helm of current WoD don't like to sell much books<br /> <br /> I'm kidding of course, but really what was the need of cutting off a player option and a popular one (viking werewolf, or thor werewolf, or whatever stereotype you prefer to give the idea in a few words)?<br /> I mean, it's just going to upset about 8% of player base maybe.<br /> And anyway it's never a good idea to eliminate player options without valid reasons<br /> <br /> I was getting on board of this W5, with the Malady and other changes I find interesting ideas to be explored.<br /> But this excess of &quot;pruning&quot; of the setting is the same thing that gave me a hard time getting passionate about V5.<br /> Hence my &quot;maybe they don't like to sell much books&quot;. I mean, it's really needless and silly decision<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-26T05:56:17-07:00","id":1479541,"title":"","content":"What is &quot;the Malady&quot; referring to?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-26T07:22:38-07:00","id":1479544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1479541#post1479541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is &quot;the Malady&quot; referring to?</div> </div> </div> </div>Either Gaia dying or Nazism, apparently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-26T07:37:33-07:00","id":1479545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1479544#post1479544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Either Gaia dying or Nazism, apparently.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I thought it might be a specific new element in the W5 Setting.<br /> <br /> Something like Garou spreading being Garou through sickness as it partly is in BNS's Werewolf Setting - which again was contributed to by Martin Ericsson. Not sure how many of his ideas are still floating around White Wolf development notes and guidebooks....<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-26T12:34:01-07:00","id":1479555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1479541#post1479541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is &quot;the Malady&quot; referring to?</div> </div> </div> </div>The new difficulty in stepping sideways, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-26T13:46:05-07:00","id":1479558,"title":"","content":"We haven't gotten a real solid look on what it is, though it seems to be a fairly broad term to refer to &quot;all the shit that's gone wrong metaphysically because of the metaplot events between Rev. and W5.&quot; It doesn't seem to be as specific as the metamorphic plague or Bitten in BNS WtA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-26T21:48:43-07:00","id":1479571,"title":"","content":"I'd like to leave it alone, but I just can't.<br /> Shit like this, this.. Corperate, faux-progressive, social justice stuff as seen in the likes of Star Trek Pickard... IE You can't play Fenrir because they're badwrong nazis, is just directly harmful to actual social liberation because it makes socially liberal ideas seem absolutely toxic. What do you mean GoF are a fallen tribe? Do you mean your ideas must avoid fair comparison with alternatives to seem good? Have the authors commited a crime if an unbiased audience could size up the GoF and the CoG and decide Fenrir has more merit? Is that why a tribe must be trashed?<br /> <br /> I refuse to believe that successful billion dollar corporations are taking franchises sometimes worth billions of dollars and absolutely tanking them with &quot;bold new directions&quot;/terrible writing by sheer coincidence. Yeah, WoD and paradox are only a few million, but it's the same thing: Why are they just making bad decisions with the IP? Do they understand the IP? Are they part of an international conspiracy to make lefties into a vile caricature in order to promote reactionary politics and thus enable a continuation of the widening wealth gap? Or do we just have a lot of aging corporate leaders who earnestly don't know how to appeal to the youth and their strange tiktok dances? It's not just Paradox, it seems endemic across all entertainment nowadays.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 04-27-2022, 01:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-26T23:31:09-07:00","id":1479573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1479541#post1479541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is &quot;the Malady&quot; referring to?</div> </div> </div> </div>From the Changing Ways (what was already influenced towards the new direction):<br /> <br /> &quot;The second great catastrophe is the Malady and the Betrayal. The increased global temperature caused by climate change is not just a physical phenomenon, it is Gaia\u2019s fever manifest in the physical world. Sick and close to death, She distances herself from the world to protect herself, slipping into a comatose state as she does. Her dreams and nightmares make caerns and other places close to the spirit world more dangerous to be in, but they are the only places the Garou can cross. The Wyrm, by contrast, can only lash out at places of particular corruption: sites of environmental disasters, industrial \u2018accidents,\u2019 great oppression and injustice.<br /> For Garou, increase the Gauntlet rating (W20, p. 310) of all places by 4. The Garou cannot step sideways at any place with a Gauntlet higher than 9. Spending five minutes getting into the appropriate mindset reduces the difficulty of stepping sideways by 1, but still does not allow crossing at a place with a Gauntlet higher than 9.&quot;<br /> <br /> A bulls*t decision which almost totaly cut of more than half of the game-arena because of well, reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-26T23:42:02-07:00","id":1479575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1479573#post1479573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The second great catastrophe is the Malady and the Betrayal. The increased global temperature caused by climate change is not just a physical phenomenon, it is Gaia\u2019s fever manifest in the physical world. Sick and close to death, She distances herself from the world to protect herself, slipping into a comatose state as she does. Her dreams and nightmares make caerns and other places close to the spirit world more dangerous to be in, but they are the only places the Garou can cross. The Wyrm, by contrast, can only lash out at places of particular corruption: sites of environmental disasters, industrial \u2018accidents,\u2019 great oppression and injustice.<br /> For Garou, increase the Gauntlet rating (W20, p. 310) of all places by 4. The Garou cannot step sideways at any place with a Gauntlet higher than 9. Spending five minutes getting into the appropriate mindset reduces the difficulty of stepping sideways by 1, but still does not allow crossing at a place with a Gauntlet higher than 9.&quot;<br /> <br /> A bulls*t decision which almost totaly cut of more than half of the game-arena because of well, reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, they changed (in that specific book, lets see if it remains) the whole &quot;human pollution is literally killing the World and serving corruption&quot; to &quot;human pollution isn't actually causing anything, because it is just the world having a fever&quot;?<br /> <br /> Forget the Fenrir, for the purposes of this game, this is actually a more disgusting thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-27T07:35:18-07:00","id":1479584,"title":"","content":"It doesn't say that global warming is ONLY Gaia having a fever, but rather that it's both. This stuff having both a physical and spiritual component has been part of the game since day one. And you aren't cut off from the Umbra. You can still cross at a Cairn and then physically walk to any other part of the Umbra. You just can't use the Umbra as a Rick Sanchez portal-gun to escape danger or walk past physical defenses and pop out on top of someone's head.<br /> <br /> This effectively means that you can either fight a problem in the Umbra, or fight it physically, but you can't constantly teleport to face only the softest foe at his softest defense point. You either go Umbra at a Cairn and walk to the Umbral enemy, or you go physical at a Cairn and walk to the physical enemy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-27T08:18:20-07:00","id":1479585,"title":"","content":"I think the human pollution is what causes Gaia to fall sick and the fever is the reaction. It is a hen/egg-situation again. Imagine a world where there was other pollution, like if we'd still used leaded fuel in cars, but there were no Greenhouse gases - would temperatures still rise because Gaia was still trying to rid herself or sickness with a fever? Who knows?<br /> <br /> Mechanically it changes the world a lot, but W20 already reverted to the need of a reflective surface, without a meta-plot reason.<br /> <br /> How is that practically working in a storytelling sense. What had difficulty 5 is now at difficulty 9 - still reachable for the Garou. Which is deep wilderness. Is that even found in western Europe?<br /> Rural countryside is 6, so it is off limits, except after five minuted of getting in the mood. I assume that allows the roll, the transition can still take minutes, as successes are unlikely and botches are likely at this difficulty. Average City is totally gone, as are inner cities and science labs - well, if you are an Ananasi.<br /> <br /> Do Gifts, Minor Rites and Fetishes that lowered difficulty for passing the Gauntlet now have a Renaissance? I hope so.<br /> In revised the mirror prevented botches, that certainly would help, but in W20, not so much - as a mobile mirror is increasing the difficulty even.<br /> <br /> So, you better stay at your caern an only go to the umbra there. Learn Gifts and such.<br /> On the positive side, banes seem to be cut off from the world to, unless there is a Wyrm Tainted area around. I hope this lowers the gauntlet, for if not, garou would be pretty helpless against banes that don't want to materialize.<br /> <br /> I find the general idea entertaining, but this execution lacking.<br /> The Penumbra should be more than a place PC venture to make use of Moon Paths, or bypass doors or see if there is a bane around on whom to blame the wyrm taint they are sensing. But making it hard to reach seems wrong, unless - like I said - Wyrm activity also lowers the Gauntlet significantly.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-27T08:20:11-07:00","id":1479586,"title":"","content":"Honestly the Get falling is boring. It's The Extremists Are Evil, and very heavy handed version at that.<br /> <br /> Plus let's be honest, it's not just going to be 'the Fenrir have fallen'. They're going to V5 Sabbat them, take the more interesting parts for another Tribe and turn them into one-dimensional villains. Potentially even sidelining the BSDs in the process.<br /> <br /> The Malady is potentially interesting. Not the best element, not the worst, if it's mainly just limiting your ability to switch battlefields on occasion it's probably fine. It's all going to depend on how it's presented.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-27T08:27:15-07:00","id":1479587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1479584#post1479584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can still cross at a Cairn and then physically walk to any other part of the Umbra. You just can't use the Umbra as a Rick Sanchez portal-gun to escape danger or walk past physical defenses and pop out on top of someone's head.<br /> <br /> This effectively means that you can either fight a problem in the Umbra, or fight it physically, but you can't constantly teleport to face only the softest foe at his softest defense point. You either go Umbra at a Cairn and walk to the Umbral enemy, or you go physical at a Cairn and walk to the physical enemy.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, this was one of the things that made Werewolf more than big furry beasts: The fact that they can *naturaly* shift onto the spirit/mirror worlds trully brings home the idea that they were &quot;half spirit&quot;. That they are creatures of two realms. Being kinda able to enter and leave at will (as I remember, it wasn't that easy but it was doable), have someone &quot;peek&quot; the other side, and strategize arround the otherworlds like that, gave them an almost &quot;ghostly&quot; feel - you can't know if the spirit-wolves are hunting you from the other side. I thought that was a cool thing <hr /><br /> I can't help to note - at the observation that &quot;you can still cross at a Cairn&quot; - how on some of the first books of &quot;Mage: Revised&quot; there was a way to safely enter the Umbra in spite of the much criticized Storm:<br /> It was trough special - rare - places, called Shallowings where the worlds touched. I think it was in Book of the Traditions that the authors talked about the fans complaints about &quot;being barred from the Umbra&quot;, stating that &quot;this wasn't true&quot; because Shallowings were a thing ... latter the authors added so many methods to cheat the Storm, that - to me - felt like an interesting thing to do.<br /> <br /> But, of course, it's a different thing, a different game...and WW never hid their interest on gaining a different, new, fanbase too ...<br /> <br /> I do wonder how this new move to make the Umbra harder to access will fare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-27-2022, 11:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-27T09:27:09-07:00","id":1479589,"title":"","content":"The problem with entering at a Caern and physically walk where you want to go in the Penumbra was something that wasn't supposed to be easy. There were umbra travel hazards and without Wits+Enigmas one could easily walk from the penumbra representation of a physical street in suburbia into the near umbral representations the concept of streets in suburbia without noticing and without the chance of reversing the process by simply tracing back one's own steps. One could prevent that fate, and for example track a person in the physical world by smell, while peeking. But, one was cut of from sensory input regarding the penumbra and therefore needed a pack for protection. That option is kind of difficult, with the Gauntlet risen....<br /> <br /> Turning travel in the penumbra into something trivial, because travel in the physical world and side stepping isn't an option any more, seems to be the wrong approach, too. Making reach any part of the penumbra that isn't reachable by stepping sideways therefore seems to have become an effort that warrants its own story entirely. If that is the case, the whole affair is more hindering storytelling, that providing an interesting new aspect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-27T11:26:39-07:00","id":1479594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1479589#post1479589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with entering at a Caern and physically walk where you want to go in the Penumbra was something that wasn't supposed to be easy. There were umbra travel hazards and without Wits+Enigmas one could easily walk from the penumbra representation of a physical street in suburbia into the near umbral representations the concept of streets in suburbia without noticing and without the chance of reversing the process by simply tracing back one's own steps. One could prevent that fate, and for example track a person in the physical world by smell, while peeking. But, one was cut of from sensory input regarding the penumbra and therefore needed a pack for protection. That option is kind of difficult, with the Gauntlet risen....<br /> <br /> Turning travel in the penumbra into something trivial, because travel in the physical world and side stepping isn't an option any more, seems to be the wrong approach, too. Making reach any part of the penumbra that isn't reachable by stepping sideways therefore seems to have become an effort that warrants its own story entirely. If that is the case, the whole affair is more hindering storytelling, that providing an interesting new aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect they consider that a feature, not a bug. They want the Umbra to be a truly separate location and an epic adventure, not a means of teleporting past defenses and appearing on top of surprised opponents. They don't want werewolves to be Rick Sanchez. That's my guess, anyway.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-27T11:56:57-07:00","id":1479595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1479584#post1479584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't say that global warming is ONLY Gaia having a fever, but rather that it's both. This stuff having both a physical and spiritual component has been part of the game since day one. And you aren't cut off from the Umbra. You can still cross at a Cairn and then physically walk to any other part of the Umbra. You just can't use the Umbra as a Rick Sanchez portal-gun to escape danger or walk past physical defenses and pop out on top of someone's head.<br /> <br /> This effectively means that you can either fight a problem in the Umbra, or fight it physically, but you can't constantly teleport to face only the softest foe at his softest defense point. You either go Umbra at a Cairn and walk to the Umbral enemy, or you go physical at a Cairn and walk to the physical enemy.</div> </div> </div> </div>You never could use it that conveniently, unless you were a Rank 5 Silent Strider. Which, well, at that point, you've definitely earned it, and maybe more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-27T13:20:17-07:00","id":1479597,"title":"","content":"And even if the garou were able to portal in and out \u00e0 la Rick and Morty, that is hardly the most OP part of the game. Your basic character, unless you take a flaw to deny it, has a form where their strength score is at MINIUM 5, the max amount of dots on the sheet. They natively do agg damage with their claws/fangs in that form, with +1 damage for claws. They also can soak ALL but silver agg damage in ANY form but their birth (unless metis), with a dicepool of +3 in the war form. This form has no timer to it, you can chill in it all you want.<br /> <br /> This is not even going to the gifts or rites or fetishes.<br /> <br /> Portal in and out, at that point, is just business as usual.<br /> <br /> WtA is a game of spiritual combat against corruption. Its stakes are high and the umbra is essentially a way to fight the corruption head-on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 04-27-2022, 04:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-27T15:59:01-07:00","id":1479607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1479595#post1479595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You never could use it that conveniently, unless you were a Rank 5 Silent Strider. Which, well, at that point, you've definitely earned it, and maybe more.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think what you could actually do matters more than what they think you could do. AFAIK the people making the decisions are far more familiar with Vampire. Take from that what you will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-27T16:52:54-07:00","id":1479616,"title":"","content":"I don't think you can just chalk this up to what games the developers know better.<br /> <br /> WtA's relationship to how easy it is to get into and out of the Umbra is a mess. Do you need a mirror, or do mirrors just help? What's good enough to be a mirror? What should modify the Gauntlet rating beyond the very basic chart?<br /> <br /> Those all shift around depending on edition. WtA has yet to really settle on a singular idea of how easily the Garou should be able to readily access the Umbra.<br /> <br /> Forsaken was not made by people that don't understand the needs of a werewolf game, and changed a bunch of things that included making getting in/out of the Shadow more complicated narratively until you get more potent powers to overcome certain restrictions. Of course, they changed a lot more to keep the game fun, but getting rid of the &quot;portal hop&quot; thing as a perception is something you can do without breaking everything.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-27T18:29:43-07:00","id":1479631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's the problem the Get have always had, and had even after the Swords were wiped out: you can't play a Fenrir without being the Thor that ends up enabling a Loki. The Thor/Get way of exalting the strong is inseparable from the Loki/Swords ideals of oppressing the weak. That's why MCU Thor exalts in seeing Captain America being worthy of wielding Mjolnir: Steve's idea of strength is better than the one Thor inherited from Odin. That's why he gives up ruling the remaining Asgardians to Valkyrie. Thor grows up and learns that being the strongest doesn't actually make you the best; it just makes you strong. </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure Thor handing control of Asgard over to a alcoholic slave trader that kidnapped and sold people to a gladiator blood sport arena for drinking money isn't really an example of him triumphing over the flaws that led to him constantly covering for Loki being shitty because he was 'one of Thor's fellow tribe'. &quot;Oh I was in a big traumatized haze just wanting to get drunk and die&quot; isn't an excuse for spending who knows how long condemning people to slavery as you hoped one of them would kill your drunken ass in the attempt. But Thor forgave her just like he forgave Loki then made her Queen of the Asgardians after she spent a few years doing nothing we saw in the way of particular atonement besides going back to doing the job she always should have been doing while THor got fat and played Fortnite (meaning he handled his haze way better then her since he didn't make anyone slaves to get his drinking money to earn that beer belly).<br /> <br /> Don't know why so many people seem to forget what an awful shitty person she is, I guess because she did most of her slave trading off screen?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 04-27-2022, 09:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-27T20:07:00-07:00","id":1479638,"title":"","content":"I really don't see how that actually impacts the point I made.<br /> <br /> If you really want to have a discussion about Valkyrie as a character and why people respond to her the way they do, perhaps start one in Off-Topic?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-27T21:10:39-07:00","id":1479642,"title":"","content":"It <i>strengthens </i>the point you made, Thor went through all sorts of character development and he had his 'Fenrir cleans house of Nazis' moment when he threw Loki in Asgard jail but in the end he backslide into bad old habits because achieving permanent long term change is a long ongoing process instead of one decisive moment where you flip a switch and become a completely new person/group totally free of the personal issues that caused the problem. Once trouble hit and he lost his drive to stay a better person to depression he went right back to overlooking the wrongdoings of fellow Asgardians that were committed against 'lesser' beings and happily handed his crown over to a never punished slave trader just because she hadn't done anything bad <i>recently </i>and he really wanted to go off on awesome space adventures with the funny raccoon man instead of put in the work to be a worthy king himself. So Thor is actually potentially a good example of what they might possibly go for in their explanation, &quot;for a moment they went to do the right thing but then they backslide as a result of this or that and in the end they fell'.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-28T00:33:03-07:00","id":1479649,"title":"","content":"That doesn't really strength my overall point, because I don't think the Get falling is a good narrative take. It only strengthens a small fraction of my point (Thor isn't really good at making sure his own house is clean while going around thinking that he's hot shit for cleaning up houses nobody asked him to), and mostly seems to be an excuse to rant about a very specific interpretation of a character that ignores a lot of context (both in-universe and her out-of-character design and writing) that's only viable because of a considerable amount of narrative ambiguity that never proves or disproves some of its base assumptions.<br /> <br /> Regardless of any debates about his choice in successor being a good choice, the fundamental (and overt part of the narrative) is that Thor realizes that being Odin's son was never qualification to be king. Thor realizes that there being a &quot;worthy&quot; king was something he was never going to be. The pressure to be one drives him to do morally and ethically questionable things (because that's what Odin did), and/or use his massive personal power to simply force issues in his favor (also one of Odin's habits). While Loki's desire for power is not really rooted in any &quot;worthy&quot; purpose, all of his repeated points about why Thor would be a horrible king are consistently show to be astute observations of his adoptive brother's personality and all the bad lessons Thor picked up from Odin. Thor wants to go on space adventures with the funny raccoon man because he realizes that's where he can be happy and productive for the universe instead of wallowing in his failings as a leader.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-28T12:25:00-07:00","id":1479664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1479594#post1479594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect they consider that a feature, not a bug. They want the Umbra to be a truly separate location and an epic adventure, not a means of teleporting past defenses and appearing on top of surprised opponents.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I'm well onboard with the goal they aim at, just not with the means they employ to achieve it.<br /> <br /> And, yes, the portal hopping is a problem. But just as with Rage rolls, one approach would be to limit difficulties to a range of 5 to 8, so the really unpredictable very high and very low difficulties are gone. Make leaving the penumbra as entering it. Do not require a mirror, but have it prevent botches and speed up the transition. Make the transition take longer, not have it one round, or ten, or fifty, depending on just one success difference. Make the time happen &quot;in transit&quot; but take the approach from &quot;WoD: Combat&quot; that a person is concentration for at least one round and can be attacked before the blueish shimmer makes the person disappear. Make the appearing work in the same way. Make taking damage during this round break the process of Reaching (or at least call for a Willpower roll to continue).<br /> <br /> There might be a myriad of other ideas players might come up with. That is why open development can be an asset....<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-29T22:07:01-07:00","id":1479785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1479584#post1479584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't say that global warming is ONLY Gaia having a fever, but rather that it's both. This stuff having both a physical and spiritual component has been part of the game since day one. And you aren't cut off from the Umbra. You can still cross at a Cairn and then physically walk to any other part of the Umbra. You just can't use the Umbra as a Rick Sanchez portal-gun to escape danger or walk past physical defenses and pop out on top of someone's head.<br /> <br /> This effectively means that you can either fight a problem in the Umbra, or fight it physically, but you can't constantly teleport to face only the softest foe at his softest defense point. You either go Umbra at a Cairn and walk to the Umbral enemy, or you go physical at a Cairn and walk to the physical enemy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Bear in mind the same info also implies that Caerns are far rarer and lower in power going forward and with a fractured Nation far harder to gain access to..<br /> <br /> Though anyone who thinks moving in and out of the Gauntlet is a remotely valid or plausible combat strategy anywhere other than virgin wilderness has likely played in some extremely homebrewed or ' rules-adjacent' campaigns anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T23:20:52-07:00","id":1485456,"title":"","content":"Listening to Achilli from the brand update of October 14th and reading in crimson thaw, I honestly dont think the Get are &quot;fallen to the wyrm&quot;.<br /> I think they will just be antagonistic, zealot werewolves, (which only makes them cooler to me), most likely like the pure from forsaken. Achilli talks about Hauglosk just after saying &quot;pheraphs&quot; and &quot;arguably&quot; about the Fenris being wyrm tainted. Also in crimson thaw , it says a tribe left the nation so convinced they are about their methods. And says nothing about a tribe being of &quot;the wyrm&quot;.<br /> <br /> I don't know, maybe I'm just keeping hope for my most played tribe.<br /> <br /> In all honesty, those 5th editions seems to be a tabula rasa of many things and forced choices to refresh the games. I'm gonna play them anyway. <br /> Remember that in Heart of the Forest there is a playable camp. Werewolf is a mine camp for many things, but I prefer the Get unplayable than softened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":3773,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","user":"Helur","date":". 07-01-2022, 05:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T01:42:58-07:00","id":1485462,"title":"","content":"That sound better then Wyrm shifting. By the way is there any source or leak about release date? I think that the release campaingn involves announced comics from the Vault and I wonder what they would release first- 5th edition or Records.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T02:05:58-07:00","id":1485465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485456#post1485456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Listening to Achilli from the brand update of October 14th and reading in crimson thaw, I honestly dont think the Get are &quot;fallen to the wyrm&quot;.<br /> I think they will just be antagonistic, zealot werewolves, (which only makes them cooler to me), most likely like <b>the pure from forsaken</b>. Achilli talks about Hauglosk just after saying &quot;pheraphs&quot; and &quot;arguably&quot; about the Fenris being wyrm tainted. Also in crimson thaw , it says a tribe left the nation so convinced they are about their methods.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the reason that this Fenrir thing bothers me so much; Both Apocalypse AND Forsaken are published by the same company. That is, there is already a game that does the pure thing by design. Why try to force it into the game that is -not- Forsaken?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T02:43:57-07:00","id":1485469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485465#post1485465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is the reason that this Fenrir thing bothers me so much; Both Apocalypse AND Forsaken are published by the same company. That is, there is already a game that does the pure thing by design. Why try to force it into the game that is -not- Forsaken?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh.<br /> To me the 5th editions are clearly a chronicles of darkness cannibalization act. Cod seems dead and they are taking the best from it to make the wod more horror and street level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T02:53:44-07:00","id":1485472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485469#post1485469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh.<br /> To me the 5th editions are clearly a chronicles of darkness cannibalization act. Cod seems dead and they are taking the best from it to make the wod more horror and street level.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 5th editions are trying to take the best from CoD and failing miserably at that, vampire is a good example of it, unfortunately Paradox already dropped the big bucks on WoD with an impressive marketing campaign because otherwise, the best course of action would have been to focus on the CoD line which is better in every way compared to WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T03:02:35-07:00","id":1485473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485472#post1485472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> 5th editions are trying to take the best from CoD and failing miserably at that, vampire is a good example of it, unfortunately Paradox already dropped the big bucks on WoD with an impressive marketing campaign because otherwise, the best course of action would have been to focus on the CoD line which is better in every way compared to WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly love them both. In the specific case of werewolf, apocalypse is great for environmental, social and epic structures which allow me to create controversial and very mature characters and chronicles. Forsaken is amazing for its street level design, gangster attitude and brutal depiction of the hunt. <br /> <br /> I would probably like w5, because I will see my 2 favourite things mixed together, but this is far from saying that this is the right thing to do from a game design perspective. <br /> <br /> But after 15 years of play I honestly don't care if the fenris are not playable or whatever. I will make them playable, and I will keep old apocalypse separated from the new one and forsaken. <br /> <br /> All editions exists and all editions are playable. I'm not gonna renounce certain things just because time changes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":3773,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","user":"Helur","date":". 07-01-2022, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T03:13:04-07:00","id":1485474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485473#post1485473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I honestly love them both. In the specific case of werewolf, apocalypse is great for environmental, social and epic structures which allow me to create controversial and very mature characters and chronicles. Forsaken is amazing for its street level design, gangster attitude and brutal extermination of the hunt.<br /> <br /> I would probably like w5, because I will see my 2 favourite things mixed together, but this is far from saying that this is the right thing to do from a game design perspective.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is just my opinion, but I don't the games mix very well.<br /> <br /> Forsaken (2nd ed) is about hunters and the chase for prey. The pack is a mini-sept with multiple layers of membership and no species is really banned from joining and gaining totem benefits. The uratha are also pretty free to do whatever as long as they don't break their own laws.<br /> <br /> Apocalypse is about trying very hard to deter the end of the world. It is a game about things bigger than yourself. Plus the Garou Nation is extremely structured and there really is little freedom of movement. I don't really see any way for Apocalypse to ever manage street level the same way Forsaken does, the garou just aren't as free to do whatever.<br /> <br /> Mind, there is a way to do Forsaken stuff in Apocalypse; Ronin. This is why I wish there was more time put into allowing players who might not want to play the Epic War Against The Wyrm to still play werewolf on the street level.<br /> <br /> Honestly, if 5th ed. would focus on ronin and their relationship with the Nation, the pure dynamic would work fine.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T03:18:45-07:00","id":1485475,"title":"","content":"My main thought about the get falling is who profits? We know get fans are effectively getting the middle finger but who actually benefits from this decision? How does it improve the game?<br /> <br /> So far I've only seen one person proactively happy about this move and that's because they wanted get players ostracised....effectively making him what we brits call a complete arse at best. Pretty much everyone else seems to be either downplaying it or engaging in apologetics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T03:51:40-07:00","id":1485477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485475#post1485475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My main thought about the get falling is who profits? We know get fans are effectively getting the middle finger but who actually benefits from this decision? How does it improve the game?<br /> <br /> So far I've only seen one person proactively happy about this move and that's because they wanted get players ostracised....effectively making him what we brits call a complete arse at best. Pretty much everyone else seems to be either downplaying it or engaging in apologetics.</div> </div> </div> </div>None. It's clear they don't care about the old players.<br /> It's basically a new brand, a,&quot; tabula rasa &quot; lines of games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T04:08:46-07:00","id":1485480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485474#post1485474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is just my opinion, but I don't the games mix very well.<br /> <br /> Forsaken (2nd ed) is about hunters and the chase for prey. The pack is a mini-sept with multiple layers of membership and no species is really banned from joining and gaining totem benefits. The uratha are also pretty free to do whatever as long as they don't break their own laws.<br /> <br /> Apocalypse is about trying very hard to deter the end of the world. It is a game about things bigger than yourself. Plus the Garou Nation is extremely structured and there really is little freedom of movement. I don't really see any way for Apocalypse to ever manage street level the same way Forsaken does, the garou just aren't as free to do whatever.<br /> <br /> Mind, there is a way to do Forsaken stuff in Apocalypse; Ronin. This is why I wish there was more time put into allowing players who might not want to play the Epic War Against The Wyrm to still play werewolf on the street level.<br /> <br /> Honestly, if 5th ed. would focus on ronin and their relationship with the Nation, the pure dynamic would work fine.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The best thing about forsaken compared to apocalypse is that you are actually playing as werewolves instead of eco terrorists space marines with extra fur, there is greater emphasis on what a werewolf condition means to them (although still not enough in my opinion) compared to apocalypse which is basically non stop balls to the walls action, also the freedom you have in making your stories compared to apocalypse tight structure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T04:12:04-07:00","id":1485481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485473#post1485473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I honestly love them both. In the specific case of werewolf, apocalypse is great for environmental, social and epic structures which allow me to create controversial and very mature characters and chronicles. Forsaken is amazing for its street level design, gangster attitude and brutal extermination of the hunt.<br /> <br /> I would probably like w5, because I will see my 2 favourite things mixed together, but this is far from saying that this is the right thing to do from a game design perspective.<br /> <br /> But after 15 years of play I honestly don't care if the fenris are not playable or whatever. I will make them playable, and I will keep old apocalypse separated from the new one and forsaken.<br /> <br /> All editions exists and all editions are playable. I'm not gonna renounce certain things just because time changes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I used to play apocalypse mostly for the absolutely bonkers action but frankly, I think it never held a candle to the complexity of the other settings, garous were never as interesting as vampires or mages, it was always the combat game and that's it, forsaken meanwhile actually made me interested in the Uratha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T04:15:54-07:00","id":1485483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485480#post1485480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The best thing about forsaken compared to apocalypse is that you are actually playing as werewolves instead of eco terrorists space marines with extra fur, there is greater emphasis on what a werewolf condition means to them (although still not enough in my opinion) compared to apocalypse which is basically non stop balls to the walls action, also the freedom you have in making your stories compared to apocalypse tight structure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, the games have different tones and different audiences.<br /> <br /> So why try to combine them into something that won't be as good as the two separate? Unless Helur is right and CoD is left to rot.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T04:28:06-07:00","id":1485485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485483#post1485483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep, the games have different tones and different audiences.<br /> <br /> So why try to combine them into something that won't be as good as the two separate? Unless Helur is right and CoD is left to rot.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Beats me, I would understand using CoD mechanics because they are just better than WoD but tring to also port the themes is asinine, masquerade and requiem shared enough superficial similarities that you could at least attempt it (and it failed miserably anyway) but forsaken and apocalypse are just too different to make it work, there is nothing official about CoD but it doesn't look good...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T04:45:04-07:00","id":1485486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485474#post1485474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Apocalypse is about trying very hard to deter the end of the world. It is a game about things bigger than yourself. <br /> <br /> Mind, there is a way to do Forsaken stuff in Apocalypse; Ronin. This is why I wish there was more time put into allowing players who might not want to play the Epic War Against The Wyrm to still play werewolf on the street level.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still can't get what W5 suppose to BE about?<br /> War is over, Gaua's dead,Garou didn' even had a glorious death (not like they deserve anything glorious, but my hateboner aside) - what's the point now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T04:56:00-07:00","id":1485487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485477#post1485477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> None. It's clear they don't care about the old players.<br /> It's basically a new brand, a,&quot; tabula rasa &quot; lines of games.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Even then it doesn't make sense, since it works on the assumption new players wouldn't want Get present. It's the equivelant of Disney saying &quot;you know what? fuck wolverine no zoomers would like him. Scott and Jean only.&quot; After getting their grubby mits on xmen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T05:35:02-07:00","id":1485490,"title":"","content":"I just want to note that I like Forsaken a LOT. Especially the 2nd edition is one of the best examples of how to create a cohesive structure in a loose society without limiting the players. This lack of limits is important because uratha packs are not just werewolves. The Pack supplement basically outlines that -anything- can join a pack. Mage, Lost, Vampire, Promethean? Sure. Regular arse wolves? Absolutely! The core description of a 2nd ed pack is of a werewolf inner circle and a human outer one. Sort of like cults to Mummies.<br /> <br /> All of this is possible because there are no pre-existing hateboners between species. All interaction is person to person basis.<br /> <br /> This... isn't possible with the very well-established setting of oWoD. There are centuries-long feuds still going on.<br /> <br /> Trying to mix these two together makes them weaker because both lose what made them work so well. Forsaken NEEDS the lack of greater structure to exist and be as loose as it can. While Apocalypse's selling point is that it is basically a fully realised urban fantasy setting.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T06:50:46-07:00","id":1485496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485487#post1485487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Even then it doesn't make sense, since it works on the assumption new players wouldn't want Get present. It's the equivelant of Disney saying &amp;quot;you know what? fuck wolverine no zoomers would like him. Scott and Jean only.&amp;quot; After getting their grubby mits on xmen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didnt day it has sense. I'm just saying what is obvious. Hunter was a total different game ad vampire was forced to change in many ways screwing many things of the old lore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T06:58:31-07:00","id":1485497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485469#post1485469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cod seems dead</div> </div> </div> </div>From which perspective?<br /> <br /> As RPGs go, CoD is as alive as anything else. Paradox is actively investing in raising WoD above the cut, but that's that.<br /> <br /> On the matter of them cannibalizing one for the other, I still hold that this is less of a thing than some people say. It is both an obvious move and not as strong as actually making X5 its own thing, which I do think to be what they're really trying.<br /> <br /> The Fenrir being unplayable is still a bad move. Making it independent, not so much, but unplayable is what'll be a problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T07:02:05-07:00","id":1485500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1478315#post1478315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you sure?<br /> <br /> If so, that sucks, but it just strengthens my already significant misgivings about W5.</div> </div> </div> </div>We might all agree here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27469-ilsaena","name":"Ilsaena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T07:19:33-07:00","id":1485504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485480#post1485480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The best thing about forsaken compared to apocalypse is that you are actually playing as werewolves instead of eco terrorists space marines with extra fur, there is greater emphasis on what a werewolf condition means to them (although still not enough in my opinion) compared to apocalypse which is basically non stop balls to the walls action, also the freedom you have in making your stories compared to apocalypse tight structure.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no singular take on the &quot;werewolf condition&quot;. If you don't like a particular take on werewolves, whatever, but don't try to proscribe the absolute for a monster that's never been told the same way twice ever, before or after early 20th century movies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T08:09:00-07:00","id":1485506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485504#post1485504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is no singular take on the &quot;werewolf condition&quot;. If you don't like a particular take on werewolves, whatever, but don't try to proscribe the absolute for a monster that's never been told the same way twice ever, before or after early 20th century movies.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Apocalypse is built around tribalistic zealots shapeshifters who fight a cosmic force of evil, their powers are just as varied and bonkers as you would expect from that premise and the fact that their form is that of a werewolf is almost secondary to all the rest, Forsaken meanwhile is built around the wolf itself, forsaken and pure live in packs and they hunt prey, their powers are built around hunting and tracking said prey and are all extremely thematic and very fitting to the image of a werewolf, I'm not saying that one is better than the other but anyone who played both will say that forsaken does a better job at evoking a more familiar image of a werewolf compared to Apocalypse, just my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T08:33:18-07:00","id":1485508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485497#post1485497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From which perspective?<br /> <br /> As RPGs go, CoD is as alive as anything else. Paradox is actively investing in raising WoD above the cut, but that's that.<br /> <br /> On the matter of them cannibalizing one for the other, I still hold that this is less of a thing than some people say. It is both an obvious move and not as strong as actually making X5 its own thing, which I do think to be what they're really trying.<br /> <br /> The Fenrir being unplayable is still a bad move. Making it independent, not so much, but unplayable is what'll be a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They are probably doing something similar to the sabbat for V5, they will make it an &quot;antagonist&quot; faction but give you all the rules to build and play a character from them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T09:10:48-07:00","id":1485510,"title":"","content":"Except we didn't even get that for the V5 Sabbat since there aren't enough rules to make PCs out of them with just the official books?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T09:17:21-07:00","id":1485511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485510#post1485510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except we didn't even get that for the V5 Sabbat since there aren't enough rules to make PCs out of them with just the official books?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Didn't read the sabbat supplement but isn't there enough to make a character? Still removing a faction is a stupid idea regardless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T09:36:53-07:00","id":1485514,"title":"","content":"Nope. The Sabbat book has almost no mechanics in it (there's a few new Discipline powers). The Paths and Rites are described on a narrative level, but there's no way to use them as presented for PCs.There aren't even Loresheets for ex-Sabbat characters that defected to other Sects because the book is that dedicated to making sure you know it's not a book for players to use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T10:03:50-07:00","id":1485517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485514#post1485514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. The Sabbat book has almost no mechanics in it (there's a few new Discipline powers). The Paths and Rites are described on a narrative level, but there's no way to use them as presented for PCs.There aren't even Loresheets for ex-Sabbat characters that defected to other Sects because the book is that dedicated to making sure you know it's not a book for players to use.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, glad I didn't drop an euro on V5 yet then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T12:41:34-07:00","id":1485534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485506#post1485506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Apocalypse is built around tribalistic zealots shapeshifters who fight a cosmic force of evil,</div> </div> </div> </div>Who all kill one or several people when they change for the first time, minimum, and are encouraged to do horror monster things to continue the war so that they don't die/lose. Also, evil is a definition up for grabs; a lot of what Gaian Garou do would be considered evil, but their foe is more like a manifestation of the Shinto concept of kegare, adjusted for concerns of poison above bodily fluids and corpses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> their powers are just as varied and bonkers as you would expect from that premise </div> </div> </div>More that they're a bit poorly organized and named. Jam Technology sounds both too technical and gives the impression that they can control devices via radio waves, when the description of the Gift is that the werewolf sics chaos gremlins on every device around. This has the same end result as someone in a horror movie whose fancy gadgets go dead. Some Gifts are far more obvious about this than others; the Fenrir and Red Talons probably don't need any creative interpretation about their Gift lists. I can only agree with this on the grounds of it not being particularly well explained to the reader.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and the fact that their form is that of a werewolf is almost secondary to all the rest, </div> </div> </div>Not when Crinos or Hispo is a part of why the First Change frenzy gives a virtually guaranteed body count. Perhaps the rest of the game is light on emphasis of frenzy, but they can't avoid this one, nor a forced change.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Forsaken meanwhile is built around the wolf itself, forsaken and pure live in packs and they hunt prey, their powers are built around hunting and tracking said prey and are all extremely thematic and very fitting to the image of a werewolf, I'm not saying that one is better than the other but anyone who played both will say that forsaken does a better job at evoking a more familiar image of a werewolf compared to Apocalypse, just my opinion. </div> </div> </div>Technically, resembling real wolves in any way, shape, or form would tend to work against them in being &quot;actual werewolves&quot;. You don't have solitary, cursed wanderers in werewolf fiction because it's attempting to make a human more like a wolf, nor do you get Omegaverse fiction from an analysis of actual wolf behavior.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T13:09:43-07:00","id":1485538,"title":"","content":"Honestly, this whole argument about the folkloric &quot;invalidity&quot; of WtA seems like utter claptrap considering the fact that:<br /> <br /> A) There's the whole thing about Werewolves of Livonia, Ossory Werewolves, and all the weird priests/sorcerors who wear skins of wolves<br /> B) Vampire The Masquerade has zero basis in myth, yet it gets a pass. It's Anne Rice + the horror/SF novel that a certain writer was liking at the time. Unless you're playing Night's Black Agents or Thousand Year Vampire, you're pretty much NOT playing vampires of myth, and I'm honestly insulted when people start claiming the Vampires of VtM are anything like the ones of myth.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T13:26:02-07:00","id":1485540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485534#post1485534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Who all kill one or several people when they change for the first time, minimum, and are encouraged to do horror monster things to continue the war so that they don't die/lose. Also, evil is a definition up for grabs; a lot of what Gaian Garou do would be considered evil, but their foe is more like a manifestation of the Shinto concept of kegare, adjusted for concerns of poison above bodily fluids and corpses.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> More that they're a bit poorly organized and named. Jam Technology sounds both too technical and gives the impression that they can control devices via radio waves, when the description of the Gift is that the werewolf sics chaos gremlins on every device around. This has the same end result as someone in a horror movie whose fancy gadgets go dead. Some Gifts are far more obvious about this than others; the Fenrir and Red Talons probably don't need any creative interpretation about their Gift lists. I can only agree with this on the grounds of it not being particularly well explained to the reader.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Not when Crinos or Hispo is a part of why the First Change frenzy gives a virtually guaranteed body count. Perhaps the rest of the game is light on emphasis of frenzy, but they can't avoid this one, nor a forced change.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Technically, resembling real wolves in any way, shape, or form would tend to work against them in being &quot;actual werewolves&quot;. You don't have solitary, cursed wanderers in werewolf fiction because it's attempting to make a human more like a wolf, nor do you get Omegaverse fiction from an analysis of actual wolf behavior.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Urathas first change can be just as bloody if not more, make no mistakes, the fact that Forsaken and CoD as a whole take a more &quot;grounded&quot; (and that is only by comparison) approach compared to WoD does not mean it is any less of an horror game, if anything, the horror aspects are even more marked and developed than apocalypse since it actually goes beyond the casual splatter fest that quickly lose impact after a while and actually take a look at the psycology behind the monster and what does it mean to it when it does what it does, something that apocalypse never really did beside some token efforts here and there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T13:35:37-07:00","id":1485542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485538#post1485538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, this whole argument about the folkloric &quot;invalidity&quot; of WtA seems like utter claptrap considering the fact that:<br /> <br /> A) There's the whole thing about Werewolves of Livonia, Ossory Werewolves, and all the weird priests/sorcerors who wear skins of wolves<br /> B) Vampire The Masquerade has zero basis in myth, yet it gets a pass. It's Anne Rice + the horror/SF novel that a certain writer was liking at the time. Unless you're playing Night's Black Agents or Thousand Year Vampire, you're pretty much NOT playing vampires of myth, and I'm honestly insulted when people start claiming the Vampires of VtM are anything like the ones of myth.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is just not true, masquerade wasn't just Anne Rice, it was also Stoker, Polidori, Le Fanu and many other, the powers were, for the most part, stuff that was presented in pop culture or folklore one way or another, werewolves in apocalypse meanwhile look more like a reskin of a space marine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T15:25:33-07:00","id":1485550,"title":"","content":"The fact that the pop-culture codification of &quot;vampire,&quot; is older than the pop-culture codification of &quot;werewolf,&quot; doesn't mean either is actually terribly reflective of mythology and folklore. All those older vampire authors you cited helped craft an image of what &quot;vampire&quot; means that is highly divorced from mythology. Stoker himself left ample notes how how he picked things he liked from dozens of different cultures, and also made stuff up from other sources that weren't based in vampire folklore at all, to craft his idea of Dracula.<br /> <br /> WtA werewolves are a giant blender of mythology, folklore, and genre conceits. It's just a mix that's newer than the ones VtM vampires are based on, so it doesn't feel as familiar. I'm fairly confident you could try to name five of the &quot;least werewolf&quot; things about WtA, and we could cite something from mythology/folklore where that aspect of WtA is actually based in a real world cultural element even if in a completely different context (but again, that's the same as VtM even if it was done a century earlier).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T15:33:52-07:00","id":1485551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485534#post1485534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who all kill one or several people when they change for the first time, minimum [...]</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there a neef for Frenzy when there is a Fist Change?<br /> If the garou was deliberately put into a stressful situation to trigger the fist change and frenzy, wouldn't there garou with the proper gifts or at least the ability to subdue the youngster be on site?<br /> Shouldn't kinfetch spirits be alert to sense the possibility of a imminent first change and fetch garou of the proper tribe to help the youngster navigate through it?<br /> <br /> W20 specifically put more emphasis on lost cubs being the norm then editions before. But that wasn't always the case. Evan had a first change but wasn't in a frenzy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T16:11:26-07:00","id":1485562,"title":"","content":"For me, the reason Garou don\u2019t feel entirely like \u201cwerewolves\u201d isn\u2019t due to a lack of mythological grounding, but rather due to the lack of drawbacks and personal horror inherent in being one (things that do tend to be present in other depictions of werewolves). To me, \u201cwerewolf\u201d implies at least a certain degree of being \u201ccursed\u201d, where any benefits are always offset by an underlying risk of losing control, that you\u2019re risking letting a beast out by using them. <br /> <br /> By contrast, Garou shapeshifting is basically effortless, they get all kinds of spirit powers, superhuman durability, and so forth. Things that are strictly beneficial, and don\u2019t come tied to any real personal cost or drawback. It\u2019s like if vampires could go out in sunlight, and only needed blood to fuel disciplines. By my reading, there\u2019s only two inherent downsides of being Garou: the risk of frenzy and the Curse. While neither are bad concepts, they just aren\u2019t present enough in the themes and psychology of the game to create a \u201cwerewolf\u201d feel. In fact, the setting basically encourages characters to all but withdraw from human civilization, rendering these drawbacks somewhat moot. <br /> <br /> Now, of course, the argument against this is that there\u2019s all kinds of drawbacks to being Garou. Namely, the variety of things that want to kill you, the societal conflicts you\u2019re drawn into, and the wider apocalyptic dread that gives the game its name. But this is my point: none of these things evoke a inherently \u201cwerewolf\u201d feeling, and none of them are inherent to the Garou nature itself, they\u2019re consequences of the setting. In isolation, being Garou is almost strictly beneficial.<br /> <br /> The end result is that the game is centered much more around being \u201cfurry Captain Planet\u201d than actually being, you know, a werewolf. You could replace the wolf shapeshifting with combat mechas and the things Garou do on a day to day basis wouldn\u2019t really change. This analysis is a bit reductive, I admit, but it highlights the thematic shortcomings I, and I think others, have with the game\u2019s depiction of werewolves. This doesn\u2019t mean that WtA is necessarily going be a bad game, and that someone can\u2019t enjoy it for what it is, just that it doesn\u2019t feel nearly as much like a \u201cwerewolf\u201d game as it seems it should. Forsaken is indeed improved in this respect (even if I personally I think it could have been better still).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T16:33:12-07:00","id":1485566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485562#post1485562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, the reason Garou don\u2019t feel entirely like \u201cwerewolves\u201d isn\u2019t due to a lack of mythological grounding, but rather due to the lack of drawbacks and personal horror inherent in being one (things that do tend to be present in other depictions of werewolves). To me, \u201cwerewolf\u201d implies at least a certain degree of being \u201ccursed\u201d, where any benefits are always offset by an underlying risk of losing control, that you\u2019re risking letting a beast out by using them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf isn't sold as a game of personal horror, that's Vampire's thing.<br /> <br /> Also the Garou literally have something call &quot;the Curse&quot; because of the impact of the Rage trait on interacting with other beings. There's plenty of personal horror on, beyond you control until you have high level powers just to temporarily negate this at cost, around the fact that most Garou can't walk down a city street without causing social complications as people respond to their innate danger with fear and suspicion. The Garou are forced into isolation from both humanity and nature, because their Rage poisons relationships.<br /> <br /> WtA is by no means perfect. I like Forsaken better for a game about werewolves too. But too many of these discussions cherry pick from WtA instead of dealing with its totality. Downplaying the drawbacks the Garou have (esp. around Rage which is the source of a lot of their combat prowess) does not mean the game lacks in personal drawbacks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While neither are bad concepts, they just aren\u2019t present enough in the themes and psychology of the game to create a \u201cwerewolf\u201d feel. In fact, the setting basically encourages characters to all but withdraw from human civilization, rendering these drawbacks somewhat moot. </div> </div> </div>How can you say the Curse isn't &quot;present&quot; enough in the core of the game when it's the very reason the Garou are so withdrawn in the first place?<br /> <br /> Garou society is massively impacted by the need to keep the Rage from having Garou constantly going on murder-benders... so how can that be absent? It's just well enough addressed so that the characters are playable.<br /> <br /> How is your argument any different than saying that because of Elysiums and Racks, there's no personal horror in VtM because they can easily address their blood needs and be in places safe from the risks to their humanity or their inner beasts being riled to frenzy?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You could replace the wolf shapeshifting with combat mechas and the things Garou do on a day to day basis wouldn\u2019t really change. </div> </div> </div>You could replace blood sucking with being a crewperson of the starship Enterprise, and the things the Kindred do on a day to day basis wouldn't really change either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This analysis is a bit reductive, I admit, but it highlights the thematic shortcomings I, and I think others, have with the game\u2019s depiction of werewolves. </div> </div> </div>It's so hyperbolic in its reductive nature, it makes any highlighting lost and how obviously inaccurate it is. WtA fans have been dealing with this sort of nonsense for decades. Blathering on about &quot;furry captain planet&quot; is as impactful as trying to claim that VtM is just Dragonball Z the game and has nothing to do with vampires. It's a meaningless trope that only makes the people repeating it look to uniformed on WtA to be worth listening to.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T16:56:34-07:00","id":1485570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485566#post1485566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's so hyperbolic in its reductive nature, it makes any highlighting lost and how obviously inaccurate it is. WtA fans have been dealing with this sort of nonsense for decades. Blathering on about &quot;furry captain planet&quot; is as impactful as trying to claim that VtM is just Dragonball Z the game and has nothing to do with vampires. It's a meaningless trope that only makes the people repeating it look to uniformed on WtA to be worth listening to.</div> </div> </div> </div>This and also, why come to the WtA forum only to complain it isn't 'werewolf' enough?<br /> <br /> That and can we please stop treating 'furry captain planet' as a bad thing. The game is about combating social and environmental wrongs. That is not 'cringe.'<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T17:00:35-07:00","id":1485571,"title":"","content":"I'm just going to Like Heavy Arms post here and leave a simple comment about how easy and nice Garou life is. This is my favourite illustration in Werewolf as it really underscores how messed up being one is, and how close you are to doing something utterly unspeakable.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/pgs57CF.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T17:06:55-07:00","id":1485572,"title":"","content":"I'm also reminded of the time the WtA authors admitted, in one of the books, that they wanted to make Pentex more like Captain Planet villains, but the reality of what some companies were doing already was so over-the-top at the time that there was no way to make it more so.<br /> <br /> It's extremely potent of a statement on multiple levels. One of which is that WtA purposefully uses fantasy and simplified narratives to try to address extremely complex real world problems (yes, that's also what a cartoon for kids did too, but that's how stories work), and sometimes there's just no way but to face those problems head on without that layer of fantasy to help you out.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T17:31:47-07:00","id":1485577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485571#post1485571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just going to Like Heavy Arms post here and leave a simple comment about how easy and nice Garou life is. This is my favourite illustration in Werewolf as it really underscores how messed up being one is, and how close you are to doing something utterly unspeakable.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/pgs57CF.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>I also feel it should be noted, uratha don't have to deal with this. Even the most angry Rahu Blood Talon can go to their work, not worry about scaring everyone around them, go home and have dinner with their spouse. They do not have to fear tearing apart their spouse because they did not do the dishes. To garou, this is a legit concern. There is a reason why some refuse to stay long with their mates, they fear what might happen.<br /> <br /> Mind uratha being able to hold a human life is not a bad thing, as I've seen many people who want to give their ahroun military background or job. Forsaken is just a better game for that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T18:56:10-07:00","id":1485581,"title":"","content":"Evidently I tripped a few nerves. Apologies. I didn\u2019t intend to sound like I was making a value judgment about WtA as a game, but to help the conversation by sharing my perspective on why it\u2019s presentation of werewolves fails to feel properly \u201cwerewolfy\u201d to some (as it indisputably does). <br /> <br /> To try and clarify: WtA is not a game focused on personal horror and is not trying to be. My point is that this has the consequence of downplaying concepts many consider quintessentially werewolf, in favor of concepts more unique to the game and its setting. This is only a failing insofar as the fact that no one game can do everything. But is forgivable for someone looking for a \u201cwerewolf game\u201d to find that Apocalypse doesn\u2019t quite fit their expectations. <br /> <br /> I did go too far downplaying Garou drawbacks; I meant to illustrate that they just don\u2019t quite fit the fantasy of being a werewolf that I have in my head, not that they don\u2019t exist. Upon reflection, they compliment the intended mood of Apocalypse remarkably well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T19:05:38-07:00","id":1485582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485581#post1485581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Evidently I tripped a few nerves. Apologies. I didn\u2019t intend to sound like I was making a value judgment about WtA as a game, but to help the conversation by sharing my perspective on why it\u2019s presentation of werewolves fails to feel properly \u201cwerewolfy\u201d to some (as it indisputably does). <br /> <br /> To try and clarify: WtA is not a game focused on personal horror and is not trying to be. My point is that this has the consequence of downplaying concepts many consider quintessentially werewolf, in favor of concepts more unique to the game and its setting. This is only a failing insofar as the fact that no one game can do everything. But is forgivable for someone looking for a \u201cwerewolf game\u201d to find that Apocalypse doesn\u2019t quite fit their expectations. <br /> <br /> I did go too far downplaying Garou drawbacks; I meant to illustrate that they just don\u2019t quite fit the fantasy of being a werewolf that I have in my head, not that they don\u2019t exist. Upon reflection, they compliment the intended mood of Apocalypse remarkably well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont like WtA either. But I understand people that do","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T21:01:24-07:00","id":1485595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485581#post1485581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point is that this has the consequence of downplaying concepts many consider quintessentially werewolf, in favor of concepts more unique to the game and its setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem, and the reason why this kind of argument seems lacking to others, is that those things some think to be quintessential to the concept just aren't so to others, while the concepts you think as unique to the game aren't really, and are found in other werewolf stories, to the point that some of them are quintessential to other people.<br /> <br /> Put in another way, there was not a single idea of what is a werewolf in pop culture, there was several and frequently contradicting, so your personal concept of what's a werewolf (or mine, or anyone's) necessarily contradicts that of another person. What to do in this case?<br /> <br /> WtA is something for werewolves no other line managed to be for their monsters: <b>the</b> Trope Codifier. Not because it is a perfect werewolf game, but because there was no single werewolf trope before. So much so that even Forsaken is far more similar to Apocalypse than it is to any other particular legend, story, movie, game, you name it, except those that also follow Apocalypse closely.<br /> <br /> You don't have to like it, it has problems, Forsaken is a better game for a lot of people for a lot of reasons. It is just that the precise argument that WtA isn't &quot;werewolfy&quot;, albeit common, <b>literally means nothing</b> except lack of knowledge about the setting and the many sources about werewolves in some form or another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T01:43:52-07:00","id":1485613,"title":"","content":"To give an example:<br /> <br /> The &quot;hulking brute&quot; Crinos form (that Forsaken copied) is basically a pop-culture invention from 1981 with The Howling, coupling with the special effects advances shown in An American Werewolf in London, where this specific giant man-wolf hybrid thing suddenly became what werewolves &quot;looked like.&quot; The 1941 Wolf Man more Glabro style werewolf was much more common in pop culture (if for no other reason than a lack of special effects and make up to do much else than a really hairy person with pointy teeth), or just turning into normal wolves. Pop-culture didn't even have giant wolves like An American Werewolf in London much.<br /> <br /> So, now, the giant hulking werewolf hybrid murder form is a staple that's been around for a few generations of horror enthusiasts (41 years will do that), but when WtA first came out it was just over a decade old, and Lon Chaney Jr. with a lot of facial hair added was what most people thought of if you said &quot;werewolf.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Crinos form also isn't really part of the folklore/mythology record. Most older stories are normal wolves, maybe particularly large wolves capable of some odd things like walking on their hind legs like humans while still having lupine bodies, or more visually strange things like a human body with a wolf head on it.<br /> <br /> So, yes, modern audiences are completely used to the idea of a human turning into a 9-foot tall wall of muscle, fangs, and claws... but go back 50 years and that was groundbreaking/not proper werewolf at all. That's kind of how pop culture works, a specific framework of what a concept is gets set as what things are &quot;supposed&quot; to be and that last for some amount of time (maybe a few decades, maybe hundreds of years) before some other idea displaces it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T01:54:51-07:00","id":1485614,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Forsaken mostly shifted the focus on which parts of the werewolf it was looking at. In Apocalypse you're a barely contained ball of rage taught to direct it at the corporation's harming the environment, whereas in Forsaken it all comes back to family.<br /> <br /> I mean that, I honestly think family is a stronger theme for Forsaken than hunting is. Uratha have a duty because of what their ancestors did thousands of years ago, these ancestors help them by serving as tribal totems, they form packs, they treat their Wolf-blooded friends and family with respect (although mixed with condensation), and they will rip your arm off if you don't show their sibling some fucking respect. The lack of trouble interacting with humans, and 2e's abandonment of 'don't stick tab A in slot B', mainly serves to support this.<br /> <br /> But Apocalypse is as much werewolfy as Changeling: the Lost is changelingy. A lot of it's changes have to do with playability rather than not being a werewolf, because turning into a rampaging monster every 28 days is fine when you're not supposed to be controlling the character at that point, but Apocalypse (and Forsaken) want you playing at that point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":4507,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","user":"TwoDSix","date":". 07-02-2022, 12:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T08:56:25-07:00","id":1485627,"title":"","content":"Another set of examples of how those tropes weren't codified before.<br /> <br /> How many people already complained that Apocalypse is about magical shamans instead of werewolves? There are arguably as much or even more legends about werewolves as shamans than not. In some werewolves are shamans that learn to shapeshift, in others the shepeshift into a wolf and shamanic powers are a part of the same package. In some the beginning of a shaman's life as such is an astral projection as an animal spirit, wolf being a very common one. For <b>a lot</b> of people the idea of werewolves dissociated from spirit powers is just Hollywood shenanigans (some of those <i>can</i> be involuntary, others cannot).<br /> <br /> Werewolves as defenders of wild spaces? There are a lot of legends about creatures that defend the sanctity of wild spaces around the world, from far before environmental concerns became a thing. On one hand a lot of people have always had religious experiences with such places, and in the other wild places are dangerous, and for eons we developed legends about supernatural powers being behind such dangers, fairies, elves, ghosts, and yes, werewolves that were either wild entities that assumed human form to communicate with a warning, people blessed with wolf form for their connection with such places, or people cursed for desecrating them.<br /> <br /> Even the other WoD splats carry a bit of older werewolf legends and pop-culture references. Werewolf as a vampire, wizard, shaman or fairy that turns into wolf form are all older tropes. As wolves that are/become vampires, fairies or wizards too, by the way. For some the quintessential Werewolf is like the Gangrel, and for others is like the Pooka, while others still identify with one Tradition or another more than with anything else.<br /> <br /> Lineages of werewolves? At the very least older than the Greek Alphabet. Werewolves as poets and musicians? Ascribing those arts to wolf howls in legend isn't new, either. Werewolves as exotic tribes, as the hidden power of a secret cabal within society, as cunning tricksters before hunger/rage send them to a frenzy, as sexual predators (Little Red Riding Hood, anyone?), you name it, it was either a thing everyone now considers a werewolf trope or it is far older than Apocalypse. And which of those are more ingrained in pop culture? None. Where you live and what kind of media and stories you like is far more defining of what tropes you'll come across among those.<br /> <br /> It is easy to talk about pop-culture based only on your own experience with it, but when it comes to werewolves there's a lot more too it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T12:10:30-07:00","id":1485637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485627#post1485627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another set of examples of how those tropes weren't codified before.<br /> <br /> How many people already complained that Apocalypse is about magical shamans instead of werewolves? There are arguably as much or even more legends about werewolves as shamans than not. In some werewolves are shamans that learn to shapeshift, in others the shepeshift into a wolf and shamanic powers are a part of the same package. In some the beginning of a shaman's life as such is an astral projection as an animal spirit, wolf being a very common one. For <b>a lot</b> of people the idea of werewolves dissociated from spirit powers is just Hollywood shenanigans (some of those <i>can</i> be involuntary, others cannot).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually untrue.<br /> <br /> Werewolves before the advent of Catholicism, as in people who shapeshift into wolves specifically and not general shapeshifters, have been either a curse by the gods(king Lycan, heroditus's Neupoi), a very limited magic trick(, a roman soldier in petronius's satyrecon) or 1 family in ireland that got it as a power from a hero-ancestor. The only account even similar to what you described is moeris from virgil's eclogues, who is Said to have been able to turn into a wolf, raise the dead, and steal corn from the fields, but I don't believe that he does any of that in the poem proper.<br /> <br /> After the rise of Catholicism, belief in &quot;pagan&quot; magic actually being able to work became heresy(because their god was the only Real god), so werewolves were re-codified(Largely by Bishop Augestine of Hippo as seen in the book &quot;City of God&quot;) as a kind of mass hallucination. Werewolves in this interpretation where one person would hallucinate(if awake) or fever dream(if asleep) So Hard that it would make other's nearby hallucine as well. This is the origin of people steeping and projecting animals, it had nothing to do with animal spirits, but everything to do with the catholic church trying to re-write folklore to convert people to their religion(something they're infamous for).<br /> <br /> Werewolves consorting with spirits Also originates from a little after this era, because the belief wasn't that they were consorting with nature, it was that they were consorting with The Devil. This was the same time Heinrich Kramer wrote the Maleus Maleficarum, a book written for the specific purpose of saying the pagan magic was Real because came from the devil and that women were evil witches that needed killing. This in-turn catalyzed the belief that werewolves Also got their powers from the devil(and in reaction to this we got the benedanti, werewolves of the christian god who fought witches, protected harvests and went into hell to find things/people that demons stole).<br /> <br /> Werewolves as a type of magical being that transforms at will into physical animals and communes with spirits of nature is 100% pop-culture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T14:52:38-07:00","id":1485652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485637#post1485637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is actually untrue...</div> </div> </div> </div>You do realise, you're focusing on christianity's influence on europe and skipping the skinwalkers, kurtadam, nagual, taltos or any of a number of other myths mixing mysticism with shapeshifting and wolf men. Even with the fact that your blanket statement is partially true, there are quite a few paganic cultures and myths speaking of heroic werewolves blessed by god or rising from the magicmen of Europe.<br /> <br /> Sure you've just given context to the Werewolf Trials, but not the actual myths and appearances in different cultures. Heck, even in relation with the Werewolf trials, Thiess of Kaltenbrun is all about people becoming werewolves to fight wicked witches and satan's spawn in faraway realms and even hell itself, if that's not folklore, what is?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T15:58:49-07:00","id":1485659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485652#post1485652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do realise, you're focusing on christianity's influence on europe and skipping the skinwalkers, kurtadam, nagual, taltos or any of a number of other myths mixing mysticism with shapeshifting and wolf men. Even with the fact that your blanket statement is partially true, there are quite a few paganic cultures and myths speaking of heroic werewolves blessed by god or rising from the magicmen of Europe.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be a massive stretch to call the things you listed werewolves.<br /> <br /> Skinwalkers weren't shapeshifters, they were shamans that wore animals skins. They're more like Norse Berserks(bear-shirts) than werewolves.<br /> <br /> Nagual is not a shifter, they're a guardian spirt that possesses an animal. They don't traditionally take human form and are closer to the european concept of a witches familiar than a werewolf.<br /> <br /> Taltos are straight up vanilla shamans. They aren't closely associated with wolves anymore than any other animal, so they're more like mages than werewolves.<br /> <br /> I'll admit that I've never heard of &quot;Kurtadam&quot; before, but looking it up only gives me a a number of sources that say it's the turkish Work for werewolf with no context and a single un-cited wikipedia entry that talks about turkish shamans. Trying to find turkish &quot;Kurtadam&quot; shamans has given me nothing. Closest thing I could find to werewolves with an actual citation was something called the &quot;Itbarak/dog-headed men&quot;(which might just be a racial slur) mentioned in a poem publish in an ecyclopedia of turkish mythology by a <span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Bahaeddin \u00d6gel. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> &quot;Heroic&quot; werewolves did exist(I mention as much with the benedanti, but others like Demaenetus the boxer[Pliny's natural histories] and the werewolf knight [Bisclavret by Marie de France], but they weren't closely associated with shamanism is my point.<br /> <br /> In fact the &quot;Kurtadam&quot; might be the Only werewolf associated with shamanism that I've seen, If that doesn't turn out to be Citogenesis.(I've already wasted days trying to find a myth talking about capricon as a time-traveling goat-fish while researching the origins of astrology, only for it to turn out to originate from a tumbler post. Please don't put me through that again.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485652#post1485652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure you've just given context to the Werewolf Trials, but not the actual myths and appearances in different cultures. Heck, even in relation with the Werewolf trials, Thiess of Kaltenbrun is all about people becoming werewolves to fight wicked witches and satan's spawn in faraway realms and even hell itself, if that's not folklore, what is?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what that has to do with shamanism, animism, and nature spirits?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T16:10:28-07:00","id":1485661,"title":"","content":"You're trying to draw bright line distinctions between things that didn't have those. &quot;A shaman that turns into a wolf,&quot; is just as much a part of what informs pop-culture werewolves as, &quot;a human cursed by the gods to become a wolf,&quot; is. Again, pop culture vampires are a blender of different source material, some of which intrudes on &quot;witches&quot; or whatever other broad categories people use that have extremely fuzzy edges. It's like complaining that VtM includes a way for vampires to be repelled by crosses, because Dracula is repelled by crucifixes, even though that's not part of 99% of mythology and folklore that is in the vague conceptual body of &quot;vampire&quot; sources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T16:17:38-07:00","id":1485662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485661#post1485661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're trying to draw bright line distinctions between things that didn't have those. &quot;A shaman that turns into a wolf,&quot; is just as much a part of what informs pop-culture werewolves as, &quot;a human cursed by the gods to become a wolf,&quot; is. Again, pop culture vampires are a blender of different source material, some of which intrudes on &quot;witches&quot; or whatever other broad categories people use that have extremely fuzzy edges. It's like complaining that VtM includes a way for vampires to be repelled by crosses, because Dracula is repelled by crucifixes, even though that's not part of 99% of mythology and folklore that is in the vague conceptual body of &quot;vampire&quot; sources.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not complaining about WTA being shamanist or that pop culture werewolves are tied to animism. That's the best part of the setting and folkloric werewolves are kind of bland as is.<br /> <br /> My initial comment is a response to someone claiming that there are more folkloric shaman werewolves than not, which is blatantly untrue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T16:22:34-07:00","id":1485663,"title":"","content":"And my objection is still that you're trying to claim a bright line between &quot;shaman that turns into a wolf,&quot; and other things that inspire pop culture werewolves as if one is a &quot;werewolf&quot; and one isn't. You're basically just saying, &quot;this doesn't fit my personal definition of folklore werewolf, therefore it doesn't count, therefore other people are wrong.&quot; Or, in other words, you're claiming people are factually incorrect with no evidence other than your opinions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T17:25:34-07:00","id":1485666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485663#post1485663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And my objection is still that you're trying to claim a bright line between &quot;shaman that turns into a wolf,&quot; and other things that inspire pop culture werewolves as if one is a &quot;werewolf&quot; and one isn't. You're basically just saying, &quot;this doesn't fit my personal definition of folklore werewolf, therefore it doesn't count, therefore other people are wrong.&quot; Or, in other words, you're claiming people are factually incorrect with no evidence other than your opinions.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean?<br /> <br /> The only shamans I claimed weren't a werewolf were the Taltos and skinwalkers, who aren't known for turning into wolves. Taltos are straight up just vanilla shamans(source: \u0150si magyar hitvil\u00e1g by Vilmos Di\u00f3szegi. and L\u00e1szl\u00f3 Sz\u00f6r\u00e9nyi.)<br /> <br /> Skinwalkers have taken on new meaning in pop-culture, but that isn't the folklore(we don't actually know much of the folklore because navajo aren't really comfortable speaking about them to outsiders). In fact, the modern interpretation of skin-walkers is known to really piss off those that still follow the navajo religion(sources: The Journey of Navajo Oshley by robert mcpherson and &quot;manners, customs, and conditions of the north american indians&quot; by George Catlin)<br /> <br /> I'm not drawing some vague line to pick and choose which is or is not a werewolf. Those things straight Aren't werewolves.<br /> <br /> \u200bKurtadam could potentially prove me wrong about there being no shaman association between werewolf folklore and shamanism(they seem to be wolf associated shamans from their wikipedia footnote at least), but I can't find any sources on them or their practices.<br /> <br /> How do I have no evidence, I've been citing my sources? I'm not just slapping my opinions on thinks and calling it fact","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T17:52:26-07:00","id":1485667,"title":"","content":"Your sources are only being cited as a positive attestation of things you're saying are &quot;werewolves,&quot; not things that have any authority on whether or not something should be considered a werewolf or not.<br /> <br /> I get that you don't think you're being the, &quot;my opinions are facts because I need to proof I'm right on the Internet&quot; guy... but you're being that guy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T18:29:04-07:00","id":1485669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485667#post1485667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your sources are only being cited as a positive attestation of things you're saying are &quot;werewolves,&quot; not things that have any authority on whether or not something should be considered a werewolf or not.<br /> <br /> I get that you don't think you're being the, &quot;my opinions are facts because I need to proof I'm right on the Internet&quot; guy... but you're being that guy.</div> </div> </div> </div>What would be the authority of what should be considered a werewolf or not?<br /> <br /> Personally, I feel like the definition of &quot;werewolf&quot; that you're using is being stretched too far to include things it shouldn't. As for my own definition, it's probably not strict enough as it's just &quot;person who turns into wolf that is not a general shapeshifter that turns into a number of/any animal equally&quot;. A person that shapeshifts into multiple animal types equally wouldn't really be a were<b>wolf</b> after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T19:49:09-07:00","id":1485671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485669#post1485669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would be the authority of what should be considered a werewolf or not?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the exact problem: there isn't one. &quot;Werewolf&quot; is a completely arbitrary concept that means whatever the speaker wants it to mean. That's why I'm point out that you're being &quot;that guy.&quot; You're trying to assert there's a factual, or even functional, definition here that supports your method or approach to this when there simply isn't.<br /> <br /> Here's the only definition of &quot;werewolf&quot; that actually matters:<br /> <br /> Is this something that has been used to inspire werewolf associated stories by later storytellers? If it is, it counts.<br /> <br /> The reason why this is the only thing that matters is because it's the only thing that impacts what the pop-culture ideas of what a werewolf is to the mainstream culture. Fighting over whether X example is &quot;werewolf enough&quot; is utterly pointless. If later stories about werewolves are inspired by it, it's part of the mythology and folklore basis of modern imaginings of werewolves. Anything else is trying to assert personal opinion as fact because there is no objective way to say who's definition of &quot;appropriately werewolf-y&quot; is correct when there's no Platonic ideal of werewolf to compare it to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T19:59:52-07:00","id":1485672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485671#post1485671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's the exact problem: there isn't one. &quot;Werewolf&quot; is a completely arbitrary concept that means whatever the speaker wants it to mean. That's why I'm point out that you're being &quot;that guy.&quot; You're trying to assert there's a factual, or even functional, definition here that supports your method or approach to this when there simply isn't.<br /> <br /> Here's the only definition of &quot;werewolf&quot; that actually matters:<br /> <br /> Is this something that has been used to inspire werewolf associated stories by later storytellers? If it is, it counts.<br /> <br /> The reason why this is the only thing that matters is because it's the only thing that impacts what the pop-culture ideas of what a werewolf is to the mainstream culture. Fighting over whether X example is &quot;werewolf enough&quot; is utterly pointless. If later stories about werewolves are inspired by it, it's part of the mythology and folklore basis of modern imaginings of werewolves. Anything else is trying to assert personal opinion as fact because there is no objective way to say who's definition of &quot;appropriately werewolf-y&quot; is correct when there's no Platonic ideal of werewolf to compare it to.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think were talking about two different things.<br /> <br /> I'm not talking about werewolves in context what historic people would call a werewolf, not pop-culture werewolves. Modern pop culture is whatever people want it to be, but that doesn't change history.<br /> <br /> Unless you're saying that anything that inspired modern pop culture of werewolves can be retroactively called a werewolf, which I would disagree Vehemently on multiple levels. That's like saying the imperial family of a country can be considered a type of prostitute because their style of clothes became popular among prostitutes in a later century. That's straight-up historically revisionist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T20:30:17-07:00","id":1485674,"title":"","content":"You're already engaging in this so-called revisionism if you consider anything from Greek mythology a &quot;werewolf&quot; when that word didn't exist yet. You can't say that Demaenetus was a werewolf unless you accept retroactively assigning of the concept of werewolf onto cultures that didn't use that word and even predated it. Or you're going to have to cite Pliny the Elder actually calling the boxer a werewolf, not some word that could idiomatically be translated as a werewolf.<br /> <br /> What it is, is classification. Anthropologists and related fields looked for common features in myth and folklore and gave them names if they felt like they represented something that goes beyond a small specific group. These labels frequently used words from specific cultural expressions of some larger concept, but when they got turned into labels they stopped being about those specific cultural expressions to the point of exclusion or there was no point in the label in the first place.<br /> <br /> The second you acknowledge that something is a &quot;werewolf&quot; despite coming from a culture that never used the word until interaction with Europeans that did use the word, you accept that it is a retroactive categorization of a type of cultural expression.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T20:52:29-07:00","id":1485676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485674#post1485674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're already engaging in this so-called revisionism if you consider anything from Greek mythology a &quot;werewolf&quot; when that word didn't exist yet. You can't say that Demaenetus was a werewolf unless you accept retroactively assigning of the concept of werewolf onto cultures that didn't use that word and even predated it. Or you're going to have to cite Pliny the Elder actually calling the boxer a werewolf, not some word that could idiomatically be translated as a werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demaenetus was called a lyk\u00e1nthropos in his own culture because of the association with king lycan. Literally the origin of the word Lycanthrope or the southern european word for werewolf. Technically, he's one of the original werewolves that all werewolves since are measured against.<br /> <br /> Very bad example there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485674#post1485674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What it is, is classification. Anthropologists and related fields looked for common features in myth and folklore and gave them names if they felt like they represented something that goes beyond a small specific group. These labels frequently used words from specific cultural expressions of some larger concept, but when they got turned into labels they stopped being about those specific cultural expressions to the point of exclusion or there was no point in the label in the first place.<br /> <br /> The second you acknowledge that something is a &quot;werewolf&quot; despite coming from a culture that never used the word until interaction with Europeans that did use the word, you accept that it is a retroactive categorization of a type of cultural expression.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf and Lycanthropos literally translate to Man-wolf and Wolf-man-look respectively. They are &quot;person who turns into wolf&quot; both derived from european cultures known to have influenced each other. Neither of these things are holes in my arguments.<br /> <br /> European cultures aren't isolated, they cross-pollinated A Lot. The idea that &quot;wolf-man&quot; evolved independently across europe and share no relation is a bit weird, considering they shared many other mythical monsters and gods since the time of the sumerians..<br /> <br /> Comparing &quot;Werewolf&quot; myths from europe isn't the same thing as pulling some random myth from mesoamerica and trying to say it's a werewolf, they didn't have the same cultural cross-pollination that europeans had. I can see a shamanic culture in turkey being influenced by european werewolf myths so there can be an argument there, but taking a navajo creature that's entirely unrelated to european mytho-history and saying &quot;no, this is a werewolf now&quot; is just disrespectful to the culture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T21:20:34-07:00","id":1485677,"title":"","content":"And now you're predictably shifting goal posts. We're not talking about things contemporaneously called &quot;werewolves,&quot; but words that translate into something akin to &quot;wolf man&quot; or &quot;man wolf.&quot;<br /> There's no point to this, you don't care about any sort of logical consistency to something you're trying to claim is about some sort of objective fact.<br /> <br /> If you want to continue this, really go back and reread this and how inane your argumentation is.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-03T07:09:41-07:00","id":1485689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485677#post1485677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And now you're predictably shifting goal posts. We're not talking about things contemporaneously called &quot;werewolves,&quot; but words that translate into something akin to &quot;wolf man&quot; or &quot;man wolf.&quot;<br /> There's no point to this, you don't care about any sort of logical consistency to something you're trying to claim is about some sort of objective fact.<br /> <br /> If you want to continue this, really go back and reread this and how inane your argumentation is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Went back and read because I have no idea what you're talking about here. I did find that 2 points changed though so thanks for pointing that out.<br /> <br /> I initially said that skin-walkers weren't shape-changers, which was wrong, they can have the ability to shapeshift into whatever animal they wear the skin of depending on the myth. My argument <br /> <br /> I also made a point that werewolves are a concept born of cross-pollination of european cultures, but that had nothing to do with the definition of werewolf that I presented earlier(Person who changes into a wolf, but isn't a general purpose shape-changer).<br /> <br /> I don't understand your objection to my point about Lykanthropos? They are people who shapeshift into a wolf specifically, as per the definition I presented earlier. Culturally they are literally the origin of many werewolf myths and the etymology of their name is the origin of the Word for werewolf in many cultures. If they aren't werewolves, what Is a werewolf? The logical consistency of that specific point was 100% sound, and it being one that you called out specifically confuses me.<br /> <br /> If we go to argue the anthropology, then you should read [The werewolf in Lore and Legend by Montague Summers] or [Werewolf Histories by Willem de Bl\u00e9court] books which break down the cultural background of werewolves and their etymology. The studies define werewolves as a myth of creatures known for shifting into wolves that are local exclusively to europe.<br /> <br /> Granted, reading through this also shows that there were the norse myths of animal-shifters that blended the ideas from &quot;City of God&quot; with their natively rooted shamanistic practices of drinking animal blood and wearing animal skin to gain supernatural strength. So I am also wrong in my thinking that the norse didn't have &quot;Werewolves&quot; and they were in fact a denomination of &quot;shamanic&quot; werewolf myths, spirit animals and all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-03T12:56:28-07:00","id":1485710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485637#post1485637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is actually untrue.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with your whole argument is that it comes from a very, very strict focus on one rendition of the myth and its history, through a very narrow focus.<br /> <br /> For example, it ignores completely that the huge number of stories affected by Christian theology in the Middle Ages originated as independent local myths before that theology, they're not just retellings of Lykaon or something. You're passing through a lot of stuff without even considering that they may exist.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if the argument was precisely that there's no single, closed definition of werewolf in folklore, saying that some stories don't count because they don't follow your single, closed definition is a fallacy to say the least.<br /> <br /> Montague Summers was a weirdo from the turn of the 19th to the 20th century with no formal training outside theology (area where he was polemic enough) and an intense interest <i>and belief</i> in the supernatural. That's not to say that he didn't did an incredible job with it, but his work compiling and analyzing the origins of pop-culture horrors, while seminal for the field, is biased and limited, and shouldn't be assumed to account for every single legend that existed even at his own time.<br /> <br /> Werewolf Histories does not support the idea that the stories you cite encompass the totality of werewolf folklore, nor does it purports to be the definitive treatise on the matter, it is <i>a</i> work about the subject, comprehensive indeed, but an entry point to the diversity of those stories and how they vary through time and place, intended for those who know little about it, instead of a compilation of every story and aspect meant for those on the field. It also focus on the European werewolf, which is a very different thing from saying that outside Europe there was nothing that could affect 90's pop culture or someone's understanding of what a werewolf is, specially if you consider that this person may not be European or descended to begin with.<br /> <br /> Shamanism, putting aside the complexity of the word and the discussions around it, covers a plethora of religious beliefs and practices with little in common outside the existence of a medium to intermediate between the human and the spiritual realms as they understand it. A huge amount of such practices have or had notions of transformation, physical and/or spiritual, through the connection with a spirit, usually called a &quot;totem&quot;. And the Wolf is one of the most common totems around the many areas of the world where wolves exist. So we have stories about shamans that turn into wolves, that leave their bodies as wolves, that visit the spirit realms as wolves, send their souls within wolves, fuse their souls with wolf companions physical or spiritual, and a lot of other variations.<br /> <br /> Pointing to those stories and saying they don't count for the argument in question because they don't abide to your narrow definition of werewolf or shamanism isn't just blatantly wrong for many, but misses the point of the argument entirely. And this can be repeated with the other examples I gave and many other folklore inspiration within Apocalypse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-03T13:34:45-07:00","id":1485713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485689#post1485689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand your objection to my point about Lykanthropos?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're flipping between two different (if somewhat overlapping) definitions of werewolf so that whenever one is inconvenient to your argument, you can use the other.<br /> <br /> By the arguments you've presented the Faoladh (aka the Werewolves of Ossory) are both legit werewolves, and not legit werewolves depending which post we're going by. &quot;Werewolf&quot; was a term applied to them later, as the Irish words for them centered around wolf-pelts, since they're the &quot;wear a skin of an animal&quot; style shapeshifter. Either they are legit werewolves (they have been referred to as such for almost a thousand years and are wolf-centric mythology/folklore) or they aren't because they didn't call themselves man-wolves/wolf-men, and instead called themselves wolf-skins<br /> <br /> As I said before, you're engaging a retroactive classification scheme of your own, but trying to equivocate out of it by appeals to linguistics. I'm not saying that legends dubbed &quot;lykanthropos&quot; by the Greeks shouldn't count as werewolves, I'm saying the logic used to include them is contrary to the logic you used to exclude others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The studies define werewolves as a myth of creatures known for shifting into wolves that are local exclusively to europe. </div> </div> </div>Ha ha ha...<br /> ...<br /> Oh wait. You're serious.<br /> <br /> Please remember than anthropology is a science. It requires that we observe, not predetermine. Any study that bakes in &quot;European only&quot; into a definition of werewolf isn't legitimate anthropology. Either you're citing unworthy sources, or you're doing those sources an incredible injustice by misrepresenting them with this summation. Which is it?<br /> <br /> Also consider that pretty much every major Indo-Europen culture has some form of &quot;men that transform into wolves,&quot; mythology (oh and a she-wolf raising founders of cities is also really common in those same groups) the idea that some imaginary line between Europe and Asia should be drawn is completely unjustifiable from an anthropological perspective as there is overwhelming evidence of common cultural and linguistic background combined with regular exposure through trade routes.<br /> <br /> And that's not even getting into evidence of similar mythologies and folklore in completely unrelated cultures. Pretty much anywhere where humans and wolves coexisted in early human civilizations, myths around humans becoming wolves (usually through a very direct correlation of respecting wolf pack hunting and seeking to instill such unity and violence on warriors) invariably come up.<br /> <br /> Proper anthropology might study European werewolf mythology by contrasting what makes it distinct from other cultural expressions, but defining the very concept of werewolves as solely European flies in the face of every principle of anthropology.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-03T15:17:00-07:00","id":1485724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485710#post1485710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip</div> </div> </div> </div>As much as I see your point, I still do not agree with the claim that Most werewolf mythology is shamanistic.<br /> <br /> I still don't see how defining werewolf as &quot;person that turns into wolf, but is a general purpose shapeshifter&quot; is a Narrow definition. Anything more open would have werewolves in the same situation the modern interpretation of dragons, Thing that is X except when it's not and very open to interpretation to the point that things are included even if they are only vaguely tangential.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485713#post1485713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're flipping between two different (if somewhat overlapping) definitions of werewolf so that whenever one is inconvenient to your argument, you can use the other.<br /> <br /> By the arguments you've presented the Faoladh (aka the Werewolves of Ossory) are both legit werewolves, and not legit werewolves depending which post we're going by. &quot;Werewolf&quot; was a term applied to them later, as the Irish words for them centered around wolf-pelts, since they're the &quot;wear a skin of an animal&quot; style shapeshifter. Either they are legit werewolves (they have been referred to as such for almost a thousand years and are wolf-centric mythology/folklore) or they aren't because they didn't call themselves man-wolves/wolf-men, and instead called themselves wolf-skins<br /> <br /> As I said before, you're engaging a retroactive classification scheme of your own, but trying to equivocate out of it by appeals to linguistics. I'm not saying that legends dubbed &quot;lykanthropos&quot; by the Greeks shouldn't count as werewolves, I'm saying the logic used to include them is contrary to the logic you used to exclude others.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually a good point and not something I realized I was doing. Especially considering most if not all werewolf myths evolve from some form of animal skin or belt wearing tradition.<br /> <br /> I'm still don't think it's to label skin-walkers would be a werewolf, not the least of which because many practitioners of the navajo religion have serious beef with people reinterpreting their religion to suit our entertainment. On the other hand, I can't come up with a definition that excludes them and includes other pelt-shifters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485713#post1485713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ha ha ha...<br /> ...<br /> Oh wait. You're serious.<br /> <br /> Please remember than anthropology is a science. It requires that we observe, not predetermine. Any study that bakes in &quot;European only&quot; into a definition of werewolf isn't legitimate anthropology. Either you're citing unworthy sources, or you're doing those sources an incredible injustice by misrepresenting them with this summation. Which is it?<br /> <br /> Also consider that pretty much every major Indo-Europen culture has some form of &quot;men that transform into wolves,&quot; mythology (oh and a she-wolf raising founders of cities is also really common in those same groups) the idea that some imaginary line between Europe and Asia should be drawn is completely unjustifiable from an anthropological perspective as there is overwhelming evidence of common cultural and linguistic background combined with regular exposure through trade routes.<br /> <br /> And that's not even getting into evidence of similar mythologies and folklore in completely unrelated cultures. Pretty much anywhere where humans and wolves coexisted in early human civilizations, myths around humans becoming wolves (usually through a very direct correlation of respecting wolf pack hunting and seeking to instill such unity and violence on warriors) invariably come up.<br /> <br /> Proper anthropology might study European werewolf mythology by contrasting what makes it distinct from other cultural expressions, but defining the very concept of werewolves as solely European flies in the face of every principle of anthropology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it? Not labelling things outside of Europe as werewolves might a means of cultural respect.<br /> <br /> You can compare and contrast similar mythologies without going through a culture's lexicon and labelling every thing there as X from your culture like the romans did with gods. &quot;This thing is similar to x, but is not X&quot; works just as well, and I don't see how that would be illegitimate anthropology.<br /> <br /> Not personally saying things outside of europe can't be werewolves, and I could 100% be misinterpreting what I read, but I could also see why werewolves as a european myth could be a thing.<br /> <br /> I have much more to think about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-03T16:53:54-07:00","id":1485731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485724#post1485724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still don't see how defining werewolf as &quot;person that turns into wolf, but is a general purpose shapeshifter&quot; is a Narrow definition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming you missed a &quot;not&quot; in there:<br /> <br /> You accept that being cursed by the gods to be a wolf is specifically a wolf thing, and thus an appropriate werewolf. However, these comes from mythological sources where the gods regularly transform people into all sorts of things. If Zeus turns people into animals based on his rather fickle judgements about them, isn't this general purpose shapeshifting because the actual entity doing the shape changing isn't limited to wolves? Again, this comes down to a logical inconsistency. &quot;This character is a werewolf because they use magic to turn into a wolf, this character isn't a werewolf because they can use magic to turn into lots of animals even if they prefer wolves, this character is a werewolf because they were cursed to become a wolf even if they could have been cursed to become any of a multitude of animals.&quot;<br /> <br /> How many animals are an &quot;option,&quot; isn't being used consistently, because you're trying to combine people that mystically seek transformation into animals with people that are cursed to become animals as one larger cultural expression.<br /> <br /> If the method of being changed from man to wolf matters, than you can't consider mystic practice and divine curse. If the method doesn't matter, than the number of alternative forms doesn't matter either.<br /> <br /> Hence, you're being narrow in your constructions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anything more open would have werewolves in the same situation the modern interpretation of dragons, </div> </div> </div>First, we're already there anyway in pop-culture.<br /> <br /> Second, so what? Why is it bad to recognize that humans have developed a common cultural experience that has hundreds of unique local expressions instead of insisting that we need to cluster expressions into tightly defined groupings?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm still don't think it's to label skin-walkers would be a werewolf, not the least of which because many practitioners of the navajo religion have serious beef with people reinterpreting their religion to suit our entertainment. On the other hand, I can't come up with a definition that excludes them and includes other pelt-shifters. </div> </div> </div>So what do you do with the mai-coh skin-walkers that were explicitly ones that worn wolf skins in all this?<br /> <br /> Or, you know, the vast number of other indigenous American cultures? The Tlngit were known to dress as wolfs or wear wolf pelts during territorial conflicts, and had strong mystic practices around using skins to acquire the attributes of revered animals. Were their wolf-warriors functionally different than the Irish people that performed the same symbolic use of wolf skins? Or is that close enough to say, &quot;yeah, werewolves are a larger human phenomenon.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is it? Not labelling things outside of Europe as werewolves might a means of cultural respect. </div> </div> </div>Werewolf is a common modern word that's accepted to discuss a broad range of cultural expressions (as I noted above, skin-wearing wolves and cursed to be a wolf by the gods are both accepted as werewolves in modern language). If we were worried about respecting cultures on the level you mean, we wouldn't be lumping in all of the various European wolf-myths in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can compare and contrast similar mythologies without going through a culture's lexicon and labelling every thing there as X from your culture like the romans did with gods. &quot;This thing is similar to x, but is not X&quot; works just as well, and I don't see how that would be illegitimate anthropology. </div> </div> </div>In this specific case, there simply is not the isolation between Europe, Asia, and north Africa, to consider them fully distinct.<br /> <br /> To give an example. There's a Turkic myth about &quot;dog headed men&quot; of specific tribe that raided to the south and attacked Turkic people. There's a Slavic myth about wolf-headed men from a tribe to the northeast that were found of raiding the Slavs. The names for this tribe that employs canine headed warriors are very similar, and when you put this on a map... a group from Asia and a group from Europe were both talking about the same thing: raiders from this one tribe that dress as canines while performing raids.<br /> <br /> This is why defining werewolves as a uniquely European myth does not work. Lines on maps aren't real. The geography wasn't sufficient to stop cultural exchange across those lines. It's bad anthropology because artificially cutting out the Turkic mythology massively skews analysis of folklore on the Slavic side of things because when you don't consider that non-Europeans had parallel mythology relating to a common source.<br /> <br /> This isn't about lexicons. This is about looking at beliefs as something that don't exist in a vacuum. When there's a common thread of wolf-man/etc. myths and folklore between Indo-European cultures stretching from Ireland to modern day China, you have to justify drawing a line between Europe and Asia, not assume it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-03T17:01:52-07:00","id":1485732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485551#post1485551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a neef for Frenzy when there is a Fist Change?</div> </div> </div> </div>It can help reinforce the &quot;anyone can die horribly at any time&quot; part of W:tA. Frenzy means not holding back, and not holding back means that someone that you might have wanted to take alive instead becomes a macabre decoration on a wall.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the garou was deliberately put into a stressful situation to trigger the fist change and frenzy, wouldn't there garou with the proper gifts or at least the ability to subdue the youngster be on site? </div> </div> </div>That's a very big if. Some of the Garou that you're counting on to subdue the first changeling might end up getting injured enough that they have to use Rage to stay alive. Shit can always go sideways.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Shouldn't kinfetch spirits be alert to sense the possibility of a imminent first change and fetch garou of the proper tribe to help the youngster navigate through it? </div> </div> </div>When they're still on the ball, sure. The game itself notes that they often lose track of their charges, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> W20 specifically put more emphasis on lost cubs being the norm then editions before. But that wasn't always the case. Evan had a first change but wasn't in a frenzy. </div> </div> </div>We never really see Evan's actual First Change, as we're introduced to him after he's been running around as a wolf for at least one night. What we do so is that he might very well have killed his father if the BSDs hadn't burst in and killed his parents first, as Evan's face is showing signs of changing form after being backhanded in the latest/last bout in a long chain of corporal punishment (his character history explicitly notes that his dad thought that beating him was the way to get him away from gangs, drugs, etc).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-05T05:19:52-07:00","id":1485831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485732#post1485732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It can help reinforce the &quot;anyone can die horribly at any time&quot; part of W:tA. Frenzy means not holding back, and not holding back means that someone that you might have wanted to take alive instead becomes a macabre decoration on a wall.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. But it also takes away gravitas from a frenzy for a story perspective.<br /> <br /> In a game world where any garou has, per definition, through a loss of self-control unavoidably killed a person would take away from any story element, when it happens for the first time.<br /> <br /> Having crossed that line &quot;per definition&quot; seems wrong to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485732#post1485732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a very big if. Some of the Garou that you're counting on to subdue the first changeling might end up getting injured enough that they have to use Rage to stay alive. Shit can always go sideways.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, having a garou with &quot;Calm the Savage Beast&quot; on stand by is not that hard within the sept. Better make it two if the first one fails the roll and doesn't spend a 2nd Willpower for automatic success....<br /> <br /> But, even without this. Sure, the garou in frenzy has no wound penalties and might spend Rage for full savagery, but if outnumbered three to one, please? It is a cub, the garou who are asked to subdue the cub are seasoned fighters. As garou they can soak the damage the frenzied garou will cause, they can spend additional actions on dodge and still have more attacks to cause bashing damage to the garou in frenzy.<br /> <br /> Not forcing the cub into a first change and hope for the best is a much bigger risk for it could happen at any time, not when there are garou around to take the heat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485732#post1485732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When they're still on the ball, sure. The game itself notes that they often lose track of their charges, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;weak willed and easy to distract&quot; is the wording, but also that chances increase with successes of the Baptism of Fire Rite. No specifics, though. Seems like it is up to the ST in question to adjust the look and feel of the Setting on how often the Rite looses its benefits before the cub has the First Change.<br /> As in any case, only garou with good dice pools should perform the Rite. So, I'd guess a sept has a designated baptist and when ever a child is born and found out to be true born, this garou will perform the Rite. If the parents know about garou, fine, if not, there is some B&amp;E and kidnapping involved. With the proper Gifts that also doesn't leave any traces... (other than the spiritual ones, intended by the Rite).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485732#post1485732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We never really see Evan's actual First Change, as we're introduced to him after he's been running around as a wolf for at least one night. What we do so is that he might very well have killed his father if the BSDs hadn't burst in and killed his parents first, as Evan's face is showing signs of changing form after being backhanded in the latest/last bout in a long chain of corporal punishment (his character history explicitly notes that his dad thought that beating him was the way to get him away from gangs, drugs, etc).</div> </div> </div> </div>I just re-read the comic and the scene I thought was his first change wasn't.<br /> <br /> There seems to be some possibilities.<br /> 1. He awakens &quot;again&quot; with ripped cloths because he sleepwalk-shapeshifts. If that would happen regularly, the Veil would be gone.<br /> 2. Or he was in a frenzy, passes out, awakens and can't remember &quot;again&quot;. This would mean there was a lot of death and destruction in his neighbourhood. Also, the cloth would be bloody, not just ripped.<br /> 3. He simply sleepwalks and runs though the undergroth of the park which rips his cloths. In that case the scene where he says &quot;Damn you&quot; a lot is his first change.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-05T10:48:56-07:00","id":1485847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485831#post1485831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True. But it also takes away gravitas from a frenzy for a story perspective.<br /> <br /> In a game world where any garou has, per definition, through a loss of self-control unavoidably killed a person would take away from any story element, when it happens for the first time.<br /> <br /> Having crossed that line &quot;per definition&quot; seems wrong to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the question is less if avoiding tragedy at a First Change is doable or not and more that it isn't reliable either way.<br /> <br /> There are a lot of things the Garou can do to ensure an inconsequential First Change, and provoke the cub into it to have it happen at a prepared setting. Heck, if the cub knows about them this can be Summer Camp-like, a pack take him to a secluded area to spend the days until First Change where nothing can go wrong (probably).<br /> <br /> But every single option can also go wrong for a number of reasons in practice. <b><i>Calm the Savage Beast</i></b> and others depend on the Sept having the right person for the task and this person being available at the time. Certainly doable for the big ones, less so for the small ones, and in no Sept you can have someone with such resources that does nothing else of importance. Much less have an entire pack on stand-by for this task alone that can guarantee being able to intervene without killing.<br /> <br /> A <b><i>Baptism of Fire Rite</i></b> has the same problems added to the roll itself. The best pool can still result in poor or no successes, and then the cub has years ahead to test those successes, so even a really good roll won't necessarily result in the spirit being there when it is needed.<br /> <br /> Provoking a frenzy in the cub isn't guaranteed, either, because First Changes aren't normal frenzies. The cub has a tough time before it, but you can hardly say that they're just succeeding at Willpower rolls until the First Change. The actual First Change isn't predictable, so provoking it may not be a thing.<br /> <br /> Of course, all that goes the other way around. too. The right people with the right skills may be available without issue. Even a relatively unskilled performer may have good successes by luck, and even with a single success the spirit may be there no problem when the time comes. With the Curse kicking in and the general bad mood of the cub they may very well be without targets at the Change even if there's no werewolf around.<br /> <br /> So it is not a &quot;per definition&quot; thing that a tragedy will occur. But it is a possibility that can't ever be ignored. For a single character it either happened or not and that's it, but for the horror aspect the simple fact that you can't completely be sure is terrifying. Imagine this for a regular Garou parent: you <b>can't</b> live with your child until the First Change, under the risk of messing things up with the Curse or a frenzy end up with dead children. But your child will become a risk for the rest of your family, and you may not be able to stop it. Until the time comes it is inconsequential if your fears will be founded or not, the fear and uncertainty are there. They're always there.<br /> <br /> Like Evan will always be haunted by the uncertainty. Did he killed his parents? He can't say, he can't know, he'll never know. The truth is irrelevant to the drama.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-05T17:26:08-07:00","id":1485869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485831#post1485831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True. But it also takes away gravitas from a frenzy for a story perspective.<br /> <br /> In a game world where any garou has, per definition, through a loss of self-control unavoidably killed a person would take away from any story element, when it happens for the first time.<br /> <br /> Having crossed that line &quot;per definition&quot; seems wrong to me.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's less of a line to cross and more of an &quot;X days since...&quot; deal, as it's going to happens eventually, and probably more than once. The line-crossing only happens if you regularly eat your opponents/victims on purpose.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, having a garou with &quot;Calm the Savage Beast&quot; on stand by is not that hard within the sept. Better make it two if the first one fails the roll and doesn't spend a 2nd Willpower for automatic success....<br /> <br /> But, even without this. Sure, the garou in frenzy has no wound penalties and might spend Rage for full savagery, but if outnumbered three to one, please? It is a cub, the garou who are asked to subdue the cub are seasoned fighters. As garou they can soak the damage the frenzied garou will cause, they can spend additional actions on dodge and still have more attacks to cause bashing damage to the garou in frenzy. </div> </div> </div>They might not be able to soak it up. That's the entire point. The damage roll might be great, the soak roll, all 4s and 5s. It's not like a video game with reliable damage negation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not forcing the cub into a first change and hope for the best is a much bigger risk for it could happen at any time, not when there are garou around to take the heat. </div> </div> </div>Yet, having Garou deal with it brings the possibility that one or more experienced Garou might be permanently injured or even die. It's the Kitsune breeding dilemma, only with incredible violence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;weak willed and easy to distract&quot; is the wording, but also that chances increase with successes of the Baptism of Fire Rite. No specifics, though. Seems like it is up to the ST in question to adjust the look and feel of the Setting on how often the Rite looses its benefits before the cub has the First Change.<br /> As in any case, only garou with good dice pools should perform the Rite. So, I'd guess a sept has a designated baptist and when ever a child is born and found out to be true born, this garou will perform the Rite. If the parents know about garou, fine, if not, there is some B&amp;E and kidnapping involved. With the proper Gifts that also doesn't leave any traces... (other than the spiritual ones, intended by the Rite). </div> </div> </div>Good dice pools, as noted, can end up farting out a botch. This is particularly true in the Storyteller system, home of the increasingly likely 90s Botch.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I just re-read the comic and the scene I thought was his first change wasn't.<br /> <br /> There seems to be some possibilities.<br /> 1. He awakens &quot;again&quot; with ripped cloths because he sleepwalk-shapeshifts. If that would happen regularly, the Veil would be gone.<br /> 2. Or he was in a frenzy, passes out, awakens and can't remember &quot;again&quot;. This would mean there was a lot of death and destruction in his neighbourhood. Also, the cloth would be bloody, not just ripped.<br /> 3. He simply sleepwalks and runs though the undergroth of the park which rips his cloths. In that case the scene where he says &quot;Damn you&quot; a lot is his first change. </div> </div> </div>I think that we may be giving Legacy Rite too much credit. It tells the story of exactly one Lost Cub, who is fortunate enough to find two very experienced guardians to help while he gets his shit together. Most Lost Cubs don't get that. Additionally, one of the tenets of the game (heh) is that there aren't enough Garou around to get everything that needs doing done. Note that in the Revised edition intro fiction, Evan doesn't have backup, and doesn't manage to find John North Winds Son until the casualties have already occurred. The account that he seems to be giving by suggestion also hints that the events of Legacy Rite might not have been the totality of how things ended up, though admittedly, that's in retcon territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-05T22:11:26-07:00","id":1485883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485869#post1485869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They might not be able to soak it up. That's the entire point. The damage roll might be great, the soak roll, all 4s and 5s. It's not like a video game with reliable damage negation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but what is the alternative?<br /> Having the cub life it's life (despite the kin fetch stating the Change is imminent) and hope for the best?<br /> Have a pack in permanent watch for Veil protection, even?<br /> And it the end, there are possibly several human and kinfolk dead?<br /> I mean, if the cub is my niece, then the potential victim is my sister.<br /> <br /> How is that honourable?<br /> How is that practical?<br /> How is that keeping good relations with the Kinfolk?<br /> <br /> If a cub isn't a totally lost cub, but has a kinfetch then the garou should make an effort to do things differently. There are enough lost cubs, with no Baptism of Fire or failed ones, to pose a problem. Especially since it is unclear how pre-Change garou detection is supposed to work in W20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-05T22:43:42-07:00","id":1485885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485883#post1485883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, but what is the alternative?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you have to come up with an answer to this out of character, and why do you think your answer is objectively right?<br /> <br /> The whole point sometimes is the question. The drama and the horror are in the question. Do not take it out of the question by coming with a standard answer.<br /> <br /> If a character does come to this situation, the very fact that there's no easy way out is the whole point from a story perspective. They have to make a decision with many repercussions and possible outcomes, and then live with whatever consequences await for them.<br /> <br /> Yes, the potential victim is your sister. The potential blood in your hands is your niece. Or maybe she'll begin life in the Nation marked as your murderer. And again, any decision you make may end up having no bad consequences, but also any of them may end up very badly. And there may be other solutions, lateral thinking goes a long way.<br /> <br /> Basically you're worried with a given theme dominating the setting too much, but you're going the other way around and throwing it and the many other avenues for story it gives out the window.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-06T10:32:29-07:00","id":1485915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485885#post1485885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do you have to come up with an answer to this out of character, and why do you think your answer is objectively right?</div> </div> </div> </div>The garou culture is based on anecdotal evidence collected by Galliards.<br /> <br /> Any individual story can go this way or that way, and the general setting should allow for all this individualism.<br /> <br /> But as a people the Garou should have come up with best practice approaches that eventually turned into traditions - possibly several in different regions or dependant on tribal customs. I mean, binding a special type of spirit to the cub is even codified as a Rite - and kinfetch spirits have no other mention, iirc, so tribal totems possibly even created special spirits just for this occasion, given the fact that the Rite of Binding states that binding a spirit to a person instead of a place or object is performed only when there is great need .<br /> <br /> So, for the LARP I run there is a need for varying NPC septs where characters originate from who then settle in the sept we play and there is a need to deal with cubs relatively often, for (as opposed to the tabletop game) it is often the starting &quot;rank&quot; for LARP characters. So, I have a need for a practical baseline.<br /> <br /> If people in the &quot;Incoming judgement&quot; threat argue that calling the cops to the bawn and mention a &quot;cult&quot; will create police reports that will lead to hunters and techno-mages causing trouble, then youngsters who disappear after leaving mutilated victims, who might be their parents and siblings, on a regular basis should lead to just as much trouble for septs.<br /> I get that W20 especially focuses a lot on the &quot;lost cub&quot; angle as a character background. But does it make sense? This take on how to handle cubs is dangerous and senseless and as a people garou should have better approaches to this topic. They have other Gifts and Rites for very specific problems, so I seems fair to argue, that there should be better approaches to this problem as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-06T12:41:00-07:00","id":1485928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1478313-warning-grumpy-post-the-fenrir-have-fallen?p=1485915#post1485915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">youngsters who disappear after leaving mutilated victims, who might be their parents and siblings, on a regular basis should lead to just as much trouble for septs.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't happens in a regular basis because Garou are even rarer than vampires. Are there even 1.000 Garou in the US at any given time? And we know they die frequently, but not literally constantly. Our games are naturally snapshots of unusual moments instead of a representation of the average day in any given Sept.<br /> <br /> With their low numbers and spread nature, even if every single cub caused such an outcome that wouldn't be a blimp in the statistics of violence, and cleaning after them is a thing, sometimes easier than avoiding the problem.<br /> <br /> Those numbers also mean, again, that the Garou simply can't afford such consistency all the time. There <b>is</b> a &quot;better practices&quot; for the whole thing, what is not there is a formula to ensure that such practice is always viable.<br /> <br /> And a baseline for your LARP doesn't change any of this. What is being presented is the inherent horror and risk, not anyone saying that such practices fail all the time. I completely agree that, barring the player wanting a specific backstory, the best approach is to assume that they didn't had to face this horror realized in their past. So what? What does it change about PC hearing stories of NPCs that didn't had such a blessed First Change, or just wondering &quot;what if&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}